8aMhhoNS+g+SUeccrlqd\nAcnnRygMUAxDCav20LsZSsx4ldBtI0v3Alg3w7xcr2suy87aJ8RPmZGEaArzomhk\nXv2xMLUtaI0DFX1zwS5OfIMCcwr4ln6PJf0hIr84kiQGHJL63F3dkaomPkOMFDb0\n/SRBiNHWFYepQNzt0xWfQSDzmdGgS0cPhUYtAnn/0fiFavBBHBH4EhWftEL3RaUy\nVyL9yottCWNDNcUjH2qpCOYP3QcAaE1SWFJsDHDvHhFKSv0MNltNkmyHmGbXFBsa\njmHZO8EXb5QuWey3tl6JwGrpRfj8vBVRRJCizWwOO1YM6rMFgqewATiAoTQHpdmZ\nu5RNEa9MDnyqNWzMDlhH\n=Ro5E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cd9302b43eeb7019cb53477774f2629e5f73bb69\nparent e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786465899 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786465899 -0700\n\nfix(code): hide incomplete extras from version output (#5352)\n\n`dcode -v` and `/version` now list an optional integration only when all\nof its declared dependencies are installed.\n\n---\n\nShared transitive dependencies such as `aiohttp` no longer make an\nunavailable provider appear installed. Partial dependency status remains\navailable to installation and update flows.\n\nVerified with code-package formatting, lint/type checks, focused\nextras/version tests, and `dcode -v`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/09fb29ab-e3fe-e15e-ad1f-07a0adefe8dc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-11T16:31:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/38f32cdbfdfcf1728178dbee85a42751dd3f3d2e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/38f32cdbfdfcf1728178dbee85a42751dd3f3d2e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/38f32cdbfdfcf1728178dbee85a42751dd3f3d2e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271"}]},{"sha":"e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUxMmFjYmFjODllNTUzMDQ4YjAzZmI2MTMyYjUzZTYxYjM0MzMyNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-11T06:29:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-11T06:29:53Z"},"message":"fix(code): serialize dcode self-upgrades across processes (#5252)\n\nCloses #5250\n\nWhen several dcode terminals are open at once, only one of them installs\nan update now — the others keep running the version they launched with\nand pick up the new one next launch.\n\n---\n\nNothing coordinated the startup auto-update across processes. Every\nlaunching terminal independently decided an update was available and ran\nits own `uv tool install -U` against the same tool environment. The only\nlock in the area, `_environment_mutation_lock`, is an in-process\n`asyncio.Lock`.\n\nTwo things partly hid this, neither of which is a lock. A terminal\nopened *after* another finished upgrading self-skips, because\n`is_installed_version_at_least` reads the on-disk distribution metadata\n— that covers \"open a new tab later\" but not \"open four tabs at once\".\nAnd uv takes its own lock on the tool directory, so concurrent installs\nqueue rather than corrupt; but they *wait*, and a queued loser can\nexceed the upgrade timeout, be reported to the user as `Auto-update\nfailed`, and write a 24-hour cooldown suppressing its next legitimate\nattempts. Upgrading in place is also actively hostile to *running*\nsessions: `_prewarm_deferred_imports` already carries a defensive guard\nbecause a concurrent upgrade can make a not-yet-imported module\ntransiently absent and crash the TUI.\n\n`update_install_lock` is a non-blocking context manager pairing a\nprocess-local `threading.Lock` with a `FileLock(thread_local=False)` on\na dedicated lock file in the state directory — the same shape as\n`_approval_state_lock` and `_trust_store_lock`, so no new dependency. It\nyields whether the caller may install; losers return immediately rather\nthan stalling startup behind an install they do not need, and record no\nfailure cooldown, since nothing failed. It is taken by all three paths\nthat replace the installed package: startup auto-update, `/update`, and\nthe update notification's install action.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `update_install_lock` exclusion is tested against a real second OS\nprocess holding the same lock file, not a patched filelock.\n- Covers release on normal exit, release after an exception, refusal of\na second in-process holder, the fail-open path, the startup skip\nrecording no cooldown, lock release before the re-exec, and the two\napp-level install paths deferring and releasing.\n- The unit-test state-dir isolation fixture now redirects the lock file,\nso no test can contend with a genuinely running dcode.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/429f3ff6-a998-e50d-8257-82169b8dc905)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"895812a509b49ba91693aceb149a03b4f1d7f2a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/895812a509b49ba91693aceb149a03b4f1d7f2a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqesFhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARGQQACadkQST3HL+b20T1Ybop2Qh\nDQhZTjxEJr+g0hVwxvLwxAyedIc5lZ2NRuKsBwR3uAD66VhNbSm4vBZiw5XhTYbo\nBrmRyQkNTJUC6fW2yUFfP+jyfDxQcG7kZ2cObF8ndOSuQduLN7AseyeDd48135ji\neRrhWXkA+9j6ueBILP40MUHJKwAhdxdjgyujw9ZnWkTjGR/7AlPoAEfGy0VsYD8W\ng/yya7rYd3qTfph2LNZ5vH2fuUvPGBT3qD1fAG+/96Ix9pcuDYpcpin4ruI1NR5d\n3dYWg1tBrLc1OKeZm6rNfYqYX2e3vy4Hus8SHkxWCepvpKnhlmvvpuel0CAx5jHA\nl2Omu42BYknrVHVWDDBWf6ut2CgjqTb5Dji+0lHjxnTL+NB/udC6b2lHymIszCTe\n7d9dJuNlXyOpDwOsFhLVuUgv7LGesn7Z9nAR/3vxIu/QmrX1O2iBHdK2QQFgh2Kf\n76ISSUANU2aebj/fiH7Dy2LBJT/wrLTuMHLmS2YJGAJyAZG9guq7qYp2QEWACWJV\nJdqKRpB5Iw/haXf+89vVegXyzT7dVloTMK7QMJfMZgAZpdmvLFGdA6E0b8iHFAp4\nL6w/1l2joJfNakm1vCNKQXquUpi7XGdOYyDTA/E7+hSrQLmPHwxdoxdIcbGQnAsM\nK+DHV4bbdwM5IVwViMVq\n=ddbq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 895812a509b49ba91693aceb149a03b4f1d7f2a3\nparent c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786429793 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786429793 -0700\n\nfix(code): serialize dcode self-upgrades across processes (#5252)\n\nCloses #5250\n\nWhen several dcode terminals are open at once, only one of them installs\nan update now — the others keep running the version they launched with\nand pick up the new one next launch.\n\n---\n\nNothing coordinated the startup auto-update across processes. Every\nlaunching terminal independently decided an update was available and ran\nits own `uv tool install -U` against the same tool environment. The only\nlock in the area, `_environment_mutation_lock`, is an in-process\n`asyncio.Lock`.\n\nTwo things partly hid this, neither of which is a lock. A terminal\nopened *after* another finished upgrading self-skips, because\n`is_installed_version_at_least` reads the on-disk distribution metadata\n— that covers \"open a new tab later\" but not \"open four tabs at once\".\nAnd uv takes its own lock on the tool directory, so concurrent installs\nqueue rather than corrupt; but they *wait*, and a queued loser can\nexceed the upgrade timeout, be reported to the user as `Auto-update\nfailed`, and write a 24-hour cooldown suppressing its next legitimate\nattempts. Upgrading in place is also actively hostile to *running*\nsessions: `_prewarm_deferred_imports` already carries a defensive guard\nbecause a concurrent upgrade can make a not-yet-imported module\ntransiently absent and crash the TUI.\n\n`update_install_lock` is a non-blocking context manager pairing a\nprocess-local `threading.Lock` with a `FileLock(thread_local=False)` on\na dedicated lock file in the state directory — the same shape as\n`_approval_state_lock` and `_trust_store_lock`, so no new dependency. It\nyields whether the caller may install; losers return immediately rather\nthan stalling startup behind an install they do not need, and record no\nfailure cooldown, since nothing failed. It is taken by all three paths\nthat replace the installed package: startup auto-update, `/update`, and\nthe update notification's install action.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `update_install_lock` exclusion is tested against a real second OS\nprocess holding the same lock file, not a patched filelock.\n- Covers release on normal exit, release after an exception, refusal of\na second in-process holder, the fail-open path, the startup skip\nrecording no cooldown, lock release before the re-exec, and the two\napp-level install paths deferring and releasing.\n- The unit-test state-dir isolation fixture now redirects the lock file,\nso no test can contend with a genuinely running dcode.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/429f3ff6-a998-e50d-8257-82169b8dc905)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-11T06:29:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e12acbac89e553048b03fb6132b53e61b3433271/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab"}]},{"sha":"c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMyMDZlYjQ1MGQ2MTJmNzc5MjRlZTU1ZWNkMTM2ZmJjNTJmNDU5YWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-11T06:24:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-11T06:24:13Z"},"message":"fix(code): drop the \"Message restored to input\" toast (#5253)\n\nInterrupting a prompt with `Esc` no longer shows a \"Message restored to\ninput\" toast — the prompt still returns to the chat input, silently.\n\n---\n\nThe restore is self-evident: the text reappears in the chat input, right\nwhere the user is looking. The toast reported that back to them while\ncovering the bottom-right of the transcript, which is most intrusive\nwhen `dcode` runs in a tiled or narrow terminal.\n\nThe behavior itself is unchanged —\n`_restore_interrupted_message_to_input` still returns the prompt (and\nany captured media) only when the chat input holds no draft and the turn\nproduced no visible output. `Ctrl+C` still does not restore at all.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038692df-2613-b315-330e-00ce0e0d82a2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7324298a3e006b77332884e386a862a0c42716a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f7324298a3e006b77332884e386a862a0c42716a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqesANCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl/oQAAdMwmaZWLyUYApJxhikGyFM\nsB1K99bsYTu6IjuyhlQO4Bhf8kLlxLNuSViZBdoimW1Onz3j7pbfBvsLmeYsMY7w\nTRkx1bfPonQAdkTrqqUgfrA8CJjbfSEOm8GoN4w8T4MBcn7jrQO3/kGjuFEliSUn\n0+Q5Rc7W695Sgj4db44Xz+Ov3W0dmgpiOrk1HKAnt/2cjIgB34E7JzGC3i4Dpqos\noUjYAhr/IgPUX1FE3TI5vPaDFi8TeN+RfKgazh6hAtXoOJ6Yqy/NKYt8Oj+0QmKp\nqIUf2ySx78ijbpkPOU5YaWuUrZU1Y+zm2f0TdBfk2TCMFn1oaOnYq59q74LmyHKs\nkcmTg35YoBQnFRYyVokB840hMfYsZRQqJ+AgjFlrKTU6pIzEpxS8ylPyYSm3+uaI\nw/Olk/UgopEggkeWcyAZ8tMUuRV1p0F7oh9kbMSOAeMBm4d23Nc+koeJOF7ixTqP\npcVNSPcAneEzS9v0QpaxMxgnQEzY2nyGELTX2mAMHpFO5R70skGnCN+PeHBui4GY\n+vEd3TjpQrwv9J0XB0fZNZ3562ErPQQogDRfRPZuHCQ2+hKaJvemOaesI1POsdiT\nAsSqFRE7P1rMUOrOizsBpdqwngKCaGgHmRuDDLtnIFAN1DYY+vVE/+57MQec9/6Z\nFxTysulQakS+Z0jTP94i\n=oINO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f7324298a3e006b77332884e386a862a0c42716a\nparent 8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786429453 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786429453 -0700\n\nfix(code): drop the \"Message restored to input\" toast (#5253)\n\nInterrupting a prompt with `Esc` no longer shows a \"Message restored to\ninput\" toast — the prompt still returns to the chat input, silently.\n\n---\n\nThe restore is self-evident: the text reappears in the chat input, right\nwhere the user is looking. The toast reported that back to them while\ncovering the bottom-right of the transcript, which is most intrusive\nwhen `dcode` runs in a tiled or narrow terminal.\n\nThe behavior itself is unchanged —\n`_restore_interrupted_message_to_input` still returns the prompt (and\nany captured media) only when the chat input holds no draft and the turn\nproduced no visible output. `Ctrl+C` still does not restore at all.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038692df-2613-b315-330e-00ce0e0d82a2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-11T06:24:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c206eb450d612f77924ee55ecd136fbc52f459ab/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70"}]},{"sha":"8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjZjg1MTdlN2ZiNzI4ZmVkZDA3ZGIxNWEwNTc3YjMwNWNkNjlmNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-10T22:49:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-10T22:49:17Z"},"message":"feat(code): warn above configurable session cost threshold (#5405)\n\nDeep Agents Code now warns once when a thread's estimated cost exceeds a\nconfigurable soft limit, defaulting to $50, and suggests `/offload` or\n`/clear`.\n\n---\n\nCost warnings use the graph's authoritative cumulative total rather than\nprovisional estimates, avoiding alerts on spend that may later be\ncorrected downward. Configure `[warnings].session_cost_threshold_usd`;\nnon-positive values disable the warning.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"445\" height=\"284\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 12 03 15 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d1b1763-dfe4-4101-af2c-f3828a40a0f0\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"a57f3107064e8617281d65ab0ed0caa9c4f38569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a57f3107064e8617281d65ab0ed0caa9c4f38569"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqelVtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATPYQAIfNmxSfZWmy5jzxcv+mcNNh\n2lyscaLm5SvYvcu05AXNkmNvevzS0DsWYl0eiZ44Oz2+EWRXuHTjkqiKz8Vt5zKW\n+Jco8FLadpGoTN9SwWdb0OoWVvSCLDSYTqX+sNmOQtrGfm+CB+WJ6UnMN+g0rSOk\n4mK0h4D5VPDqC3Xk+wh5O61a3JfyXgJD9DVqZjF79El3BRU4DkIEEt/bX5Dj5IiZ\nDxEOPwwCe1nBa3bl0Jd/ToHU04IZ/60y5gRLlpsX39x3huPlUp3BY4mR7HgiG3TP\nq/3jf27vN2NXMSJmi3PxlCJqoEw15rWoLCv9BrvaezNr0VxBHJ51SoqI+tovVoX7\ndl8tf5+BO+9rBgCMxZWNKLOlEXrqj6r/YeJ/7nsz0Gz9X/ZNL0IxitkAFLT7My16\nstZ9x3z8thT+D367PTFr0kz4FfRaJvRu34PX5EcRZALvH0Ui6wQMBU35ACKwpeYW\nURgjcx2qv1MlrXvdv1RLOanEz2ax+nnNBKMBtjEWp8L4j62I3upu/ZYkPt31h8/Z\n6sK7kJJ8OcMdS1BrFBQNu7LGlqbcoKl0DAl8eR5RdSuu5Df8GPx2Jz0oVbmAudyV\nlb2mRNUuYO0Uz2h4elbTovz080/E9WCYSEItdbpSkhgiQB3g81uxIMaPrCACdL0F\n6nTGUf77kXURMs0Yl818\n=sJQq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a57f3107064e8617281d65ab0ed0caa9c4f38569\nparent 6a5d93f9ba7391189f65e6b999b724253577085d\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1786402157 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786402157 -0700\n\nfeat(code): warn above configurable session cost threshold (#5405)\n\nDeep Agents Code now warns once when a thread's estimated cost exceeds a\nconfigurable soft limit, defaulting to $50, and suggests `/offload` or\n`/clear`.\n\n---\n\nCost warnings use the graph's authoritative cumulative total rather than\nprovisional estimates, avoiding alerts on spend that may later be\ncorrected downward. Configure `[warnings].session_cost_threshold_usd`;\nnon-positive values disable the warning.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"445\" height=\"284\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-10 at 12 03 15 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d1b1763-dfe4-4101-af2c-f3828a40a0f0\"\n/>","verified_at":"2026-08-10T22:49:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cf8517e7fb728fedd07db15a0577b305cd69f70/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jo