ffer.</li>\n<li>Reject duplicate Host headers in request headers. Thanks to Sunand\nMohan for the report.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.4.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Incompatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li>Support for PyPy 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li><code>Stream.end_stream()</code> now raises\n<code>NoSuchStreamError</code> or <code>StreamClosedError</code>\nexceptions, instead of a generic <code>KeyError</code>.</li>\n<li>Duplicate <code>content-length</code> headers with different values\nnow raise <code>ProtocolError</code>.\nPreviously, the first <code>content-length</code> header was accepted\nand later conflicting values were ignored. Thanks to Harshal Parekh for\nthe report.</li>\n<li>Parse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110\ngrammar for numbers (1*DIGIT). Thanks to Arkadiusz Marta for the\nreport.</li>\n<li><strong>backfill from v4.3.0</strong> Convert emitted events into\nPython <code>dataclass</code>, which introduces new constructors with\nrequired arguments.\nInstantiating these events without arguments, as previously commonly\nused API pattern, will no longer work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Compatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.14 has been added.</li>\n<li><code>H2Connection.receive_data</code> now accepts any byte-like\nobject that\nimplements the buffer protocol, such as <code>bytes</code>,\n<code>bytearray</code>, and\n<code>memoryview</code>. Existing <code>bytes</code> callers are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li>Align CONNECT pseudo-header validation with RFC 9113 s8.3 and RFC\n8441 s4.\nOrdinary CONNECT now requires <code>:method=CONNECT</code> and\n<code>:authority</code>, and\nforbids <code>:scheme</code>/<code>:path</code>. Extended CONNECT (e.g.,\nWebSocket) requires\n<code>:scheme</code>, <code>:path</code>, <code>:authority</code> plus\n<code>:protocol</code>. (PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1309\">#1309</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix incorrect substring matching of secure header in\n<code>cookie</code> and <code>:method</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bugfixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix to allow sending 0 bytes on a stream even if the flow control\nwindow is negative.</li>\n<li>Reject non-zero <code>SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH</code> values received\nfrom servers.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/bc239af1d1b85bc70482804f30a0e0e587d90a08\"><code>bc239af</code></a>\nv4.4.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/92b925ed1b1817c82db32893503f74f47fcf4452\"><code>92b925e</code></a>\nadd test for duplicate host headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/292a40829feefda98c8509dcdbbb4a57af9bd6a6\"><code>292a408</code></a>\nreject duplicate Host headers in request headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/04d3b87cbc1db020d28c7cfb44fe194558efbdde\"><code>04d3b87</code></a>\nupdate changelog</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/439b970d0fa19891fa81068907de97dfa3a07c3a\"><code>439b970</code></a>\nprepare for next release cycle</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/9a7ff7430df669fa8e90b6121f3cc1ed64d1115a\"><code>9a7ff74</code></a>\nperformance: remove consumed frames in place from data buffer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1321\">#1321</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/6cce763997eca5b826f3e435a611b7a7fc73f633\"><code>6cce763</code></a>\nv4.4.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/dfafda3b0cd96455b45d1785ef1ebc6968bba5cf\"><code>dfafda3</code></a>\nBump pytest from 8.4.2 to 9.0.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1320\">#1320</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/b45207cedf9fabe2c77bb3c1c10f403a610599a0\"><code>b45207c</code></a>\ndependencies and packaging++</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/c40145f69c5473850849fe96301ac0416b1afea6\"><code>c40145f</code></a>\nparse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110 grammar\nfor numbers (1*DI...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/compare/v4.3.0...v4.4.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=h2&package-manager=uv&previous-version=4.3.0&new-version=4.4.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-08-07T05:10:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bb12361b4d76fab4f10bc7603262527443634bfd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bb12361b4d76fab4f10bc7603262527443634bfd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bb12361b4d76fab4f10bc7603262527443634bfd/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76"}]},{"sha":"78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc4ZGQ1MjgxODJlMjE0OGFjNThjNTg3NjdlMTU1OGM2ZGRjYzNjNzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-07T05:08:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-07T05:08:01Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump h2 from 4.3.0 to 4.4.1 in /libs/evals (#5382)\n\nBumps [h2](https://github.com/python-hyper/h2) from 4.3.0 to 4.4.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">h2's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.4.1 (2026-08-03)</h2>\n<p><strong>Bugfixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Performance improvement: remove consumed frames in-place from data\nbuffer.</li>\n<li>Reject duplicate Host headers in request headers. Thanks to Sunand\nMohan for the report.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.4.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Incompatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li>Support for PyPy 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li><code>Stream.end_stream()</code> now raises\n<code>NoSuchStreamError</code> or <code>StreamClosedError</code>\nexceptions, instead of a generic <code>KeyError</code>.</li>\n<li>Duplicate <code>content-length</code> headers with different values\nnow raise <code>ProtocolError</code>.\nPreviously, the first <code>content-length</code> header was accepted\nand later conflicting values were ignored. Thanks to Harshal Parekh for\nthe report.</li>\n<li>Parse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110\ngrammar for numbers (1*DIGIT). Thanks to Arkadiusz Marta for the\nreport.</li>\n<li><strong>backfill from v4.3.0</strong> Convert emitted events into\nPython <code>dataclass</code>, which introduces new constructors with\nrequired arguments.\nInstantiating these events without arguments, as previously commonly\nused API pattern, will no longer work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Compatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.14 has been added.</li>\n<li><code>H2Connection.receive_data</code> now accepts any byte-like\nobject that\nimplements the buffer protocol, such as <code>bytes</code>,\n<code>bytearray</code>, and\n<code>memoryview</code>. Existing <code>bytes</code> callers are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li>Align CONNECT pseudo-header validation with RFC 9113 s8.3 and RFC\n8441 s4.\nOrdinary CONNECT now requires <code>:method=CONNECT</code> and\n<code>:authority</code>, and\nforbids <code>:scheme</code>/<code>:path</code>. Extended CONNECT (e.g.,\nWebSocket) requires\n<code>:scheme</code>, <code>:path</code>, <code>:authority</code> plus\n<code>:protocol</code>. (PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1309\">#1309</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix incorrect substring matching of secure header in\n<code>cookie</code> and <code>:method</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bugfixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix to allow sending 0 bytes on a stream even if the flow control\nwindow is negative.</li>\n<li>Reject non-zero <code>SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH</code> values received\nfrom servers.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/bc239af1d1b85bc70482804f30a0e0e587d90a08\"><code>bc239af</code></a>\nv4.4.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/92b925ed1b1817c82db32893503f74f47fcf4452\"><code>92b925e</code></a>\nadd test for duplicate host headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/292a40829feefda98c8509dcdbbb4a57af9bd6a6\"><code>292a408</code></a>\nreject duplicate Host headers in request headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/04d3b87cbc1db020d28c7cfb44fe194558efbdde\"><code>04d3b87</code></a>\nupdate changelog</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/439b970d0fa19891fa81068907de97dfa3a07c3a\"><code>439b970</code></a>\nprepare for next release cycle</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/9a7ff7430df669fa8e90b6121f3cc1ed64d1115a\"><code>9a7ff74</code></a>\nperformance: remove consumed frames in place from data buffer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1321\">#1321</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/6cce763997eca5b826f3e435a611b7a7fc73f633\"><code>6cce763</code></a>\nv4.4.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/dfafda3b0cd96455b45d1785ef1ebc6968bba5cf\"><code>dfafda3</code></a>\nBump pytest from 8.4.2 to 9.0.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1320\">#1320</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/b45207cedf9fabe2c77bb3c1c10f403a610599a0\"><code>b45207c</code></a>\ndependencies and packaging++</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/c40145f69c5473850849fe96301ac0416b1afea6\"><code>c40145f</code></a>\nparse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110 grammar\nfor numbers (1*DI...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/compare/v4.3.0...v4.4.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=h2&package-manager=uv&previous-version=4.3.0&new-version=4.4.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e18d8e3ed0d99cc06b33abbf0d08a845603dce3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e18d8e3ed0d99cc06b33abbf0d08a845603dce3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdWgxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO88QAEOzq95urmg73sZpl3QfkUne\nuOOVrTFfP9SM0ykcQe+tEo/nFy3jsxW8KnHf3YDAfSsfeqghF3abrZzBw2eO3dcU\n1r2W3kr2zeyoml1tczZifV2GGrDqj3iORPKd5Aw3y/vJ5k+INF1TLnAhfVraX6/J\nf1J3HUGR8FwJMyMfiuoEf80UlcayCGr/AwqNUX5bkWP7fcDgwpqg+KCQ2kMy7jyP\nxagMOlDd8P0GLQpfuCgV+8EPhImcKLCgVahcGtkIfx5Zl1Zt64C4qSQqPH2JnYvj\ngi1+NtBqxsnV2eYV3FXwGk8hH4GUXBSqVfuiiPfDwk7oivcUW/v4RhZB2Xt+a0MY\nBCULuNy+yWmzU0VPB0sFp0Tlku+jDui2Kd8OyIfcHN2NChXQ942ZvoU2XCx+m+T7\ng/3JTG5LsYK+SL/jO75DZI5d6UR30VLpmUwZWVquVoydNRJbEXZGKOG/0yqMVb1I\nM0ALrMXAcLxcL+JOBqXQjQuJ4Q96Lz1gjrjAkktlcwd/FcSfSCuM6YMj3JcNrPSo\n1g7OTTbmOUma8WCSOwXcwPi0HgK8Mi/tE7a8T54zu1Mu+xxRjSCCMwXfc9n9EA2T\ns9kOd9CxmR+2ApEI246Rw3acdbH3dV5VQgT1Ue8pkkvVE4MulW4Oy1if1lrDD5dy\nEBagQ9TFyxI4AF04lnPA\n=h3jE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e18d8e3ed0d99cc06b33abbf0d08a845603dce3d\nparent a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786079281 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786079281 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump h2 from 4.3.0 to 4.4.1 in /libs/evals (#5382)\n\nBumps [h2](https://github.com/python-hyper/h2) from 4.3.0 to 4.4.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">h2's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.4.1 (2026-08-03)</h2>\n<p><strong>Bugfixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Performance improvement: remove consumed frames in-place from data\nbuffer.</li>\n<li>Reject duplicate Host headers in request headers. Thanks to Sunand\nMohan for the report.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.4.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Incompatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li>Support for PyPy 3.9 has been removed.</li>\n<li><code>Stream.end_stream()</code> now raises\n<code>NoSuchStreamError</code> or <code>StreamClosedError</code>\nexceptions, instead of a generic <code>KeyError</code>.</li>\n<li>Duplicate <code>content-length</code> headers with different values\nnow raise <code>ProtocolError</code>.\nPreviously, the first <code>content-length</code> header was accepted\nand later conflicting values were ignored. Thanks to Harshal Parekh for\nthe report.</li>\n<li>Parse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110\ngrammar for numbers (1*DIGIT). Thanks to Arkadiusz Marta for the\nreport.</li>\n<li><strong>backfill from v4.3.0</strong> Convert emitted events into\nPython <code>dataclass</code>, which introduces new constructors with\nrequired arguments.\nInstantiating these events without arguments, as previously commonly\nused API pattern, will no longer work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>API Changes (Backward Compatible)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for Python 3.14 has been added.</li>\n<li><code>H2Connection.receive_data</code> now accepts any byte-like\nobject that\nimplements the buffer protocol, such as <code>bytes</code>,\n<code>bytearray</code>, and\n<code>memoryview</code>. Existing <code>bytes</code> callers are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li>Align CONNECT pseudo-header validation with RFC 9113 s8.3 and RFC\n8441 s4.\nOrdinary CONNECT now requires <code>:method=CONNECT</code> and\n<code>:authority</code>, and\nforbids <code>:scheme</code>/<code>:path</code>. Extended CONNECT (e.g.,\nWebSocket) requires\n<code>:scheme</code>, <code>:path</code>, <code>:authority</code> plus\n<code>:protocol</code>. (PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1309\">#1309</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix incorrect substring matching of secure header in\n<code>cookie</code> and <code>:method</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Bugfixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix to allow sending 0 bytes on a stream even if the flow control\nwindow is negative.</li>\n<li>Reject non-zero <code>SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH</code> values received\nfrom servers.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/bc239af1d1b85bc70482804f30a0e0e587d90a08\"><code>bc239af</code></a>\nv4.4.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/92b925ed1b1817c82db32893503f74f47fcf4452\"><code>92b925e</code></a>\nadd test for duplicate host headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/292a40829feefda98c8509dcdbbb4a57af9bd6a6\"><code>292a408</code></a>\nreject duplicate Host headers in request headers</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/04d3b87cbc1db020d28c7cfb44fe194558efbdde\"><code>04d3b87</code></a>\nupdate changelog</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/439b970d0fa19891fa81068907de97dfa3a07c3a\"><code>439b970</code></a>\nprepare for next release cycle</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/9a7ff7430df669fa8e90b6121f3cc1ed64d1115a\"><code>9a7ff74</code></a>\nperformance: remove consumed frames in place from data buffer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1321\">#1321</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/6cce763997eca5b826f3e435a611b7a7fc73f633\"><code>6cce763</code></a>\nv4.4.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/dfafda3b0cd96455b45d1785ef1ebc6968bba5cf\"><code>dfafda3</code></a>\nBump pytest from 8.4.2 to 9.0.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-hyper/h2/issues/1320\">#1320</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/b45207cedf9fabe2c77bb3c1c10f403a610599a0\"><code>b45207c</code></a>\ndependencies and packaging++</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/commit/c40145f69c5473850849fe96301ac0416b1afea6\"><code>c40145f</code></a>\nparse <code>content-length</code> headers according to RFC9110 grammar\nfor numbers (1*DI...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-hyper/h2/compare/v4.3.0...v4.4.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=h2&package-manager=uv&previous-version=4.3.0&new-version=4.4.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-07T05:08:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78dd528182e2148ac58c58767e1558c6ddcc3c76/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a"}]},{"sha":"a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE5N2JkYjY1Nzc4YTY3YzI4YjNlZjdjYTU5ZTM5YTg4ODUwYzBmMmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-07T02:16:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-07T02:16:52Z"},"message":"ci(infra): fail on unexpected test warnings (#5346)\n\nEvery package under `libs/` now fails its test run on any warning the\nrepo has not explicitly accepted. Each package's pytest `filterwarnings`\nopens with `\"error\"`, followed by a short reviewed allowlist of\ncategorical third-party warnings (each with a justification comment).\nOne test that deliberately emits a warning\n(`test_metadata_less_dist_info_does_not_raise`) scopes its exception\nwith `pytest.mark.filterwarnings` instead of a package-level entry. A\nstatic contract test under `.github/scripts/tests/workflows/` asserts\nevery package opts in and the workflow bypass wiring stays intact.\n\nApplying the policy surfaced two real bugs, fixed at the source rather\nthan allowlisted: a `SyntaxWarning` from a non-raw docstring in the ACP\n`GenericFakeChatModel`, and a `ResourceWarning` from an unclosed\n`task.toml` handle in the DRBench adapter test.\n\nMaintainers can bypass the policy on a PR by applying the\n`bypass-warnings-check` label and re-running failed jobs: `_test.yml`\nreads live PR labels from the GitHub API (re-runs replay the original\nevent payload, so `github.event.pull_request.labels` can be stale) and\npasses `-W default` on the pytest command line, which outranks every ini\nfilter for that run. The step is fail-closed — an API error enforces\nrather than bypasses — and `push`/`merge_group` runs always enforce, so\nthe label cannot smuggle warnings into the merge queue.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e0cf512ff4bd616c54102045dc7e2954e18047c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0e0cf512ff4bd616c54102045dc7e2954e18047c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdUAUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASycQABWQceC6eek79r/DMk4zAOjE\ngXpK+7qyH+TfxSeDab5OfavtfO3qGPLCsTQOND7wcMHEn4274MUO/ohAxVhCtV8y\nb5EmHZqHoDbXJkS9Dk4jQLHWbo5GgnmVLOl6gtG5mS1Z1ryWtDx802Zz6nDJjWNO\no1MtcFyKefRFqDd3PwG7qfL22ufP2ck8TyupN0a9SWQea72nueKIqz8xpDYVXypg\nEEZsjG9KYGvzsgHYok91ZHFPYIRopKDvRjI69qhVI5Yi4AlhRW8ljVhI3lvObpEJ\nh4JMqzd8hXlUnWxO3MN97BJd2RNA860mEquBe1CvTIYygHHaHWX1TzvFjGlFNixo\n+/DxnJasaN9lR3Z2QxfO23h9cUf1OyPOrJhuereL5iGGRKx5Vu83tc5cQuHGJfIR\nx8U1njuFAFDJNv2PukX1u7e4TsU3CqxXuc/m8nG1bfCIOGXCvFD4LovqBOftp1re\nUkH0lTImPXeeknOoqzmMDUDAMcm3uAxTZCjnY3o4KGBOFlfEnDaNnltGYFtFwIzq\nv/8xLPasJW9PI7XgSWsNXgXb1Gha9Rf01m8J8dIurCCosuyJV0bG5pxjK0IMBzqF\ngZZ0jqFQqLBaIOCD1ZMqD5r/CzRK8q73jtx6BuGxDegQNb99XrxP0EI7zKYvYEUH\n7nDEP8r4fpxXBwRAh1Uz\n=Idm2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0e0cf512ff4bd616c54102045dc7e2954e18047c\nparent f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786069012 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786069012 -0400\n\nci(infra): fail on unexpected test warnings (#5346)\n\nEvery package under `libs/` now fails its test run on any warning the\nrepo has not explicitly accepted. Each package's pytest `filterwarnings`\nopens with `\"error\"`, followed by a short reviewed allowlist of\ncategorical third-party warnings (each with a justification comment).\nOne test that deliberately emits a warning\n(`test_metadata_less_dist_info_does_not_raise`) scopes its exception\nwith `pytest.mark.filterwarnings` instead of a package-level entry. A\nstatic contract test under `.github/scripts/tests/workflows/` asserts\nevery package opts in and the workflow bypass wiring stays intact.\n\nApplying the policy surfaced two real bugs, fixed at the source rather\nthan allowlisted: a `SyntaxWarning` from a non-raw docstring in the ACP\n`GenericFakeChatModel`, and a `ResourceWarning` from an unclosed\n`task.toml` handle in the DRBench adapter test.\n\nMaintainers can bypass the policy on a PR by applying the\n`bypass-warnings-check` label and re-running failed jobs: `_test.yml`\nreads live PR labels from the GitHub API (re-runs replay the original\nevent payload, so `github.event.pull_request.labels` can be stale) and\npasses `-W default` on the pytest command line, which outranks every ini\nfilter for that run. The step is fail-closed — an API error enforces\nrather than bypasses — and `push`/`merge_group` runs always enforce, so\nthe label cannot smuggle warnings into the merge queue.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-07T02:16:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a97bdb65778a67c28b3ef7ca59e39a88850c0f2a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0"}]},{"sha":"f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY2OTgwNGJmY2UyNjczZGU0ZjIxNzE2NjRhYzViOTFjMWMyNDhlYTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-07T01:59:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-07T01:59:50Z"},"message":"fix(code): store update logs under the OS cache dir (#5363)\n\nUpdate logs from self-updates (`uv tool install` / `pip install` output)\nare ephemeral diagnostics, not application state. This moves\n`UPDATE_LOG_DIR` from `~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/` to\n`<cache>/deepagents-code/update_logs/`, where `<cache>` is the\nplatform-native cache directory (`~/Library/Caches` on macOS,\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%` on Windows, `$XDG_CACHE_HOME` or `~/.cache` elsewhere).\n\n---\n\nBefore this change, every self-update wrote a timestamped log under\n`~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/`. That directory also holds OAuth\ntokens, the sessions database, and input history — things users expect\nto persist — while the update logs are transient `uv`/`pip` output that\nthe retention policy (`UPDATE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS = 14`,\n`UPDATE_LOG_MAX_FILES = 10`) already treats as disposable. A cache\ndirectory is the more correct home.\n\n- New `default_cache_dir()` resolver lives next to `DEFAULT_STATE_DIR`\nin `model_config.py`: `~/Library/Caches` on macOS, `LOCALAPPDATA` on\nWindows (falling back to `~/AppData/Local`), and `XDG_CACHE_HOME`\nelsewhere when it is an absolute path (falling back to `~/.cache`).\nRelative `XDG_CACHE_HOME` values are invalid per the XDG spec and are\nignored rather than resolved against the launch directory.\n- Resulting `UPDATE_LOG_DIR` values:\n    - macOS: `~/Library/Caches/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n    - Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n- Linux with `XDG_CACHE_HOME` set:\n`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n    - Linux without it: `~/.cache/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n- The install script writes its own `install.log` under\n`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}` on every platform, so on macOS the two\nlogs intentionally land under different roots. Each side follows the\nconvention appropriate to it — a portable one-shot POSIX bootstrap (like\nthe rustup and uv installers) versus a long-lived app (like\n`platformdirs`, and `uv`'s own cache at `~/Library/Caches/uv`). Both\ndocstrings now state this explicitly so the divergence isn't later\n\"fixed\" by mistake.\n- `create_update_log_path` / `cleanup_update_logs` signatures and the\n`OSError`-tolerant debug-log-and-continue behavior in `perform_upgrade`\nare unchanged — a non-writable cache dir must not break updates. The\ntimestamped `<stamp>-update.log` naming and retention policy are\nuntouched. Existing logs under the old\n`~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/` path are simply orphaned; nothing\nreads them back.\n- Nothing in the codebase reads update logs back (verified: write-only\nacross the package), so no reader migration is needed. No docs/help text\nreferenced the old path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- New `TestDefaultCacheDir` in `test_model_config.py`: XDG\nset/unset/empty/relative, macOS with and without `XDG_CACHE_HOME`,\nWindows with and without `LOCALAPPDATA`.\n- `test_update_check.py` (388 tests, including the existing\n`UPDATE_LOG_DIR` patch-based fixture) passes unchanged.\n- `make -C libs/code lint` (ruff + ty + format) passes.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"84a80d70dac3dfcc9dca95e450ca66e8822b02b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/84a80d70dac3dfcc9dca95e450ca66e8822b02b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdTwWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9CIQAHM+gaQa/OXRUH42kGQxw/B1\nIA+3gqKNOWQiK3zOj6g+HHqDNzdKQLwTNCOmJFXU1+6cwUKaqOfXYlpBJy9t/enz\nYBT6HBW8U+PpkjdYKuVfOUmsPc7Ny5D+TcN9J/N5qckTjcTELchIoqm1qzm3UXNy\n5wiYMNgzvyJhBZo17Mn5bHBJcfQ5ElTpMJs0kJ4L5UMgJtAE2wsWRtxyidEk8pY4\naxplAM5mSRcnk3AOSR6DK1/h3uIXQtlH4aYhL9hpCKjTwejFbNGby9CXADx3Sz6M\nd7gC27CrxvoDlviLHcQLtGhrZGoD1dDniHK3VRqfl378+ExvH3Y29eICZvuTU/YB\ny6pZusa/jOPoySF4zeCO6ytNFVH8Fic3L5FNgFcVJvs0MYhIB1jlrXonw4bmYuWT\nKFGNi0TsOGZSvsixlRLpLgVMJrr+s6HC/6bUhnecnbiP8fBILuI1SJ13N3MEUiZV\njQJbdxJ34yc9pmCmOfAeTj1QcK96nvBigpRhPu5ekopc2PhdNBb3c68o1PQWvbhO\nYKPx6uKpWEBx85PAukJ8cmSLOm1NMk6X7F8uOMF3IDDpYFj2FflH2bRtDtRRtoP9\n7BgM3YYWyv0AaRmR/LWIYEtuCgJy1aVq58D0MyCwtbYLdBrvqv3K4HliyItcVo8n\nrPK6eqnEf49YBeQ8BdCx\n=iMUH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 84a80d70dac3dfcc9dca95e450ca66e8822b02b0\nparent 6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786067990 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786067990 -0400\n\nfix(code): store update logs under the OS cache dir (#5363)\n\nUpdate logs from self-updates (`uv tool install` / `pip install` output)\nare ephemeral diagnostics, not application state. This moves\n`UPDATE_LOG_DIR` from `~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/` to\n`<cache>/deepagents-code/update_logs/`, where `<cache>` is the\nplatform-native cache directory (`~/Library/Caches` on macOS,\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%` on Windows, `$XDG_CACHE_HOME` or `~/.cache` elsewhere).\n\n---\n\nBefore this change, every self-update wrote a timestamped log under\n`~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/`. That directory also holds OAuth\ntokens, the sessions database, and input history — things users expect\nto persist — while the update logs are transient `uv`/`pip` output that\nthe retention policy (`UPDATE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS = 14`,\n`UPDATE_LOG_MAX_FILES = 10`) already treats as disposable. A cache\ndirectory is the more correct home.\n\n- New `default_cache_dir()` resolver lives next to `DEFAULT_STATE_DIR`\nin `model_config.py`: `~/Library/Caches` on macOS, `LOCALAPPDATA` on\nWindows (falling back to `~/AppData/Local`), and `XDG_CACHE_HOME`\nelsewhere when it is an absolute path (falling back to `~/.cache`).\nRelative `XDG_CACHE_HOME` values are invalid per the XDG spec and are\nignored rather than resolved against the launch directory.\n- Resulting `UPDATE_LOG_DIR` values:\n    - macOS: `~/Library/Caches/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n    - Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n- Linux with `XDG_CACHE_HOME` set:\n`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n    - Linux without it: `~/.cache/deepagents-code/update_logs/`\n- The install script writes its own `install.log` under\n`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}` on every platform, so on macOS the two\nlogs intentionally land under different roots. Each side follows the\nconvention appropriate to it — a portable one-shot POSIX bootstrap (like\nthe rustup and uv installers) versus a long-lived app (like\n`platformdirs`, and `uv`'s own cache at `~/Library/Caches/uv`). Both\ndocstrings now state this explicitly so the divergence isn't later\n\"fixed\" by mistake.\n- `create_update_log_path` / `cleanup_update_logs` signatures and the\n`OSError`-tolerant debug-log-and-continue behavior in `perform_upgrade`\nare unchanged — a non-writable cache dir must not break updates. The\ntimestamped `<stamp>-update.log` naming and retention policy are\nuntouched. Existing logs under the old\n`~/.deepagents/.state/update_logs/` path are simply orphaned; nothing\nreads them back.\n- Nothing in the codebase reads update logs back (verified: write-only\nacross the package), so no reader migration is needed. No docs/help text\nreferenced the old path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- New `TestDefaultCacheDir` in `test_model_config.py`: XDG\nset/unset/empty/relative, macOS with and without `XDG_CACHE_HOME`,\nWindows with and without `LOCALAPPDATA`.\n- `test_update_check.py` (388 tests, including the existing\n`UPDATE_LOG_DIR` patch-based fixture) passes unchanged.\n- `make -C libs/code lint` (ruff + ty + format) passes.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-07T01:59:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f69804bfce2673de4f2171664ac5b91c1c248ea0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3"}]},{"sha":"6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZlYjM3NDhjZTY3M2FmZGMzNDU3MTIzNmViNTUxNzg1YjBhYTU0ZDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-07T00:42:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-07T00:42:19Z"},"message":"chore(code): harden installer ripgrep gating and prompt semantics (#5344)\n\nHardens the `dcode` install script (`curl ... | bash`) in two ways,\nadapted from patterns in Prime's installer.\n\n---\n\n## Gate system ripgrep on a minimum version\n\nThe `system` ripgrep path (brew/apt/dnf/pacman/zypper/apk/nix/cargo)\nused to count any `command -v rg` after install as success — an ancient\ndistro package would satisfy it and then behave differently at runtime.\nEach branch now checks the resulting `rg --version` against a floor\n(12.0.0, below the 14.1.1 the managed installer pins) and only succeeds\nwhen it clears it; a too-old or unprobeable pre-existing `rg` warns\ninstead of silently passing, and a failed version probe no longer aborts\nthe installer.\n\n## Three-valued `prompt_yn`\n\n`prompt_yn` returned the same code for \"user said no\" and \"no terminal\nexists to ask on,\" forcing callers to guess. It now returns 0 (yes), 1\n(no), or 2 (no usable terminal). The upgrade prompt completes the update\non the no-terminal case (cron/CI/systemd) rather than conflating it with\na decline, the PATH-setup prompt declines only on an explicit \"no,\" and\nthe extras-removal prompts continue (with a warning) when nobody could\nbe asked.","tree":{"sha":"2c5566c4518d943192e2fb79f7da59ff3cf0f824","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2c5566c4518d943192e2fb79f7da59ff3cf0f824"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdSnrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALEoQAGGspDDmwBdllR24N0Ar5nMP\nJFk5Yi0sQhpJzybhTohA8KuocoR09eWwbbrSH05YEF6AwFOdxfV0EXNml5nbyuOu\nK+t7Bc/4066qMIO65tOcTwsb37Ldy2eCPuvBiQxAI1X1pjiREc/K9WBeDuMOytyF\nJCw/r+oZsDEJN6KB6+196S1lpF5lGPkySvSC/gq+w/cfaOlsnVVddZS/4Weluza1\nK9FrfkeR2EG5o6i+HZb1oVMzVqI2PAShuMykcmCbEoIfU/ADiO1Ofzv5WVLo7uqw\nwCUCsnxaY1S9salDVo0cDau2Clg6LkvfoiDKfPg+B77pvGMmDTCk751B3q4vHIDV\nSAY7sVgWKn0VkBqFW4bDggOHOzhYAhDK1TNdyKTYNszZg6fsgdUWpxNZ8FlN21hP\nVfPe+4GCKW9j2O9GZ3xzSAUk9labK0a9IQ86MvM/KZ/ofkWvMPC+aEgk77vT/f1L\nE1ww+3kkNuF3G5vacyENQ+4QBUXr6lBJGMNjNOdLHv1UT5eGb/38eKj4b2GWxCfh\nepuRynzcUaICFw4T+9GP79piOFpZxFXkswpyANmMZHZGaSl+WpZFXFP81NU+uoIF\neRW0fNsY+l/+ILo1vr4iCrcyEoI/70ldgajB3N8L676qMxhVJT6J5XYtkYjGVZNr\nSxpwAwiFnkCQqAd2P4zS\n=8w7V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c5566c4518d943192e2fb79f7da59ff3cf0f824\nparent 889f217dd558254c1d9e77dca307fb326a5b1c21\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786063339 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786063339 -0400\n\nchore(code): harden installer ripgrep gating and prompt semantics (#5344)\n\nHardens the `dcode` install script (`curl ... | bash`) in two ways,\nadapted from patterns in Prime's installer.\n\n---\n\n## Gate system ripgrep on a minimum version\n\nThe `system` ripgrep path (brew/apt/dnf/pacman/zypper/apk/nix/cargo)\nused to count any `command -v rg` after install as success — an ancient\ndistro package would satisfy it and then behave differently at runtime.\nEach branch now checks the resulting `rg --version` against a floor\n(12.0.0, below the 14.1.1 the managed installer pins) and only succeeds\nwhen it clears it; a too-old or unprobeable pre-existing `rg` warns\ninstead of silently passing, and a failed version probe no longer aborts\nthe installer.\n\n## Three-valued `prompt_yn`\n\n`prompt_yn` returned the same code for \"user said no\" and \"no terminal\nexists to ask on,\" forcing callers to guess. It now returns 0 (yes), 1\n(no), or 2 (no usable terminal). The upgrade prompt completes the update\non the no-terminal case (cron/CI/systemd) rather than conflating it with\na decline, the PATH-setup prompt declines only on an explicit \"no,\" and\nthe extras-removal prompts continue (with a warning) when nobody could\nbe asked.","verified_at":"2026-08-07T00:42:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6eb3748ce673afdc34571236eb551785b0aa54d3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptio