:"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9"}]},{"sha":"21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIxZmQwZDY3OTRkY2JlMDliNjdlNjc4ODYzYzE0ZTAyYzRmMmI2ZDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T06:10:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T06:10:05Z"},"message":"chore(code): surface update status, log path, and extras loss in installer (#5342)\n\nThe install script now leads an available update with an explicit\n`Update available: deepagents-code X → Y` verdict before the changelog\nlink, prints the persistent uv install log path on every run (not just\non failure), ends a real upgrade with `Upgrade complete.` instead of\n`Setup complete.`, and warns before a bare re-run silently drops extras\nthe existing install was built with — including the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` re-run command that preserves them.\n\n---\n\nBefore / after:\n\n**Update prompt** — the changelog link previously appeared without first\nstating that an update exists:\n\n```console\n# Before\n▸ What's new: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/releases/tag/deepagents-code%3D%3D0.2.0\nUpdate deepagents-code 0.1.0 → 0.2.0? [y/N]\n\n# After\n▸ Update available: deepagents-code 0.1.0 → 0.2.0\n▸   What's new: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/releases/tag/deepagents-code%3D%3D0.2.0\nInstall update? [y/N]\n```\n\n**Extras loss** — re-running the installer without\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` rebuilds the environment against the bare\npackage and silently removes every extra the install was built with\n(model providers, sandbox backends, etc.). The extras are now read off\nuv's own `uv-receipt.toml` and called out, with the exact re-run\ncommand, before that happens. An interactive user can also back out;\nexplicitly passing extras or doing an editable→PyPI swap already\nexpresses intent, so those skip the warning:\n\n```console\n# Before\n(no output; the extras are gone after the reinstall)\n\n# After\n⚠ This install has extras that a bare re-run will remove: anthropic,daytona\n⚠   To keep them, re-run with: DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS=\"anthropic,daytona\"\nContinue anyway and remove them? [y/N]\n```\n\nA receipt that exists but can't be read or parsed (symlink, unreadable\npermissions, unexpected format) warns too — a false negative here costs\nthe user the exact packages this check protects.\n\n**Footer** — the footer now distinguishes a version move from a fresh\ninstall:\n\n```console\n# Before (any successful run)\n✔ Setup complete. Run: dcode\n\n# After (unpinned run that moved version)\n✔ Upgrade complete. Run: dcode\n```\n\nOther outcomes get their own wording: `Dependencies updated.` for a\nsame-version dependency bump and `Already installed.` for a no-op. A\npinned move (`bash -s -- 0.1.0` over 0.2.0 is a downgrade, and there's\nno version comparison to tell) keeps `Setup complete.`\n\n**Log path** — uv's full stderr (dependency diff, rebuild notice) is\ncaptured to a persistent log, but the script only mentioned it on\nfailure or a same-version dependency bump, so on a normal upgrade the\ndetails scrolled away with no way back. It's now printed after any\nsuccessful install that wrote a log:\n\n```console\n# After\n✔ deepagents-code upgraded to 0.2.0.\n▸ Full log: ~/.cache/deepagents/install.log\n```\n\nThe log stays under `~/.cache` (not `~/.deepagents/.state`) because it's\nephemeral output, not application state.","tree":{"sha":"eb007e0d9360773214619fc3529ce6fb0e9a306f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/eb007e0d9360773214619fc3529ce6fb0e9a306f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdCU9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5PEQAGIRr+QJsAYibC7v+P0+M9DO\neGZ8wmlxbZT9qaKQXINY58/YaVIxi5OP5cuIUzJ0UM3s/DpRR1jO6lUthFv92ViE\nCtDkm8Aoh34ratIwxbhxcvmSRsNwngYTD9gp4HhQwIQgaZiIbkJfcMjpsvW4aWk7\nXwHWG0B6NXlYJZ/vxutRAQS08QMH2xS5ppiDfaEGnAoBkhed4dJA1mcXBwP8Pkva\ngbKd12A78nL02xVmW0GCu8DpaWiZ2/qY520OAijY602Lt4uLIXWkssU++8WgfqsI\npoHXBhWWUHBZ1IfSKiz0UrD83qErBX8nDVxz+V7oXfHHlj7crhjmnHvNXq4Ez44S\n9XaBoVSBFUgPcCpg/YKP7YxYyMp+IGJwIMrLjiOvAGAAfqJrSAT+/ltZUUwO08MD\nGbfTcjY3NH/iOEeRpf54FCizkFl3sIVLSovNf516j6MMimJl2pYMaO7mbi34Gfi7\n+VT6/yPx+EgiQPIhTUdwz0EcA27VPpJN/FJmVmG2NIkwON7n/mrrz4MWkWQTp46y\nChnhxweV0z6uZGShNT7tFkDKZl37h/BLpvaJFVDbD4M9fc7MuMfvsUKfvOaGpqBD\npTin5ivLmQb8wPk2y+Ngp6culo3YJelTGCzJpABM5p8msJxgi4/p9C1vdGmXzFIZ\n4uYeDPNKs/0fxRQCKu5+\n=4N5Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb007e0d9360773214619fc3529ce6fb0e9a306f\nparent 65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785996605 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785996605 -0400\n\nchore(code): surface update status, log path, and extras loss in installer (#5342)\n\nThe install script now leads an available update with an explicit\n`Update available: deepagents-code X → Y` verdict before the changelog\nlink, prints the persistent uv install log path on every run (not just\non failure), ends a real upgrade with `Upgrade complete.` instead of\n`Setup complete.`, and warns before a bare re-run silently drops extras\nthe existing install was built with — including the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` re-run command that preserves them.\n\n---\n\nBefore / after:\n\n**Update prompt** — the changelog link previously appeared without first\nstating that an update exists:\n\n```console\n# Before\n▸ What's new: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/releases/tag/deepagents-code%3D%3D0.2.0\nUpdate deepagents-code 0.1.0 → 0.2.0? [y/N]\n\n# After\n▸ Update available: deepagents-code 0.1.0 → 0.2.0\n▸   What's new: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/releases/tag/deepagents-code%3D%3D0.2.0\nInstall update? [y/N]\n```\n\n**Extras loss** — re-running the installer without\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` rebuilds the environment against the bare\npackage and silently removes every extra the install was built with\n(model providers, sandbox backends, etc.). The extras are now read off\nuv's own `uv-receipt.toml` and called out, with the exact re-run\ncommand, before that happens. An interactive user can also back out;\nexplicitly passing extras or doing an editable→PyPI swap already\nexpresses intent, so those skip the warning:\n\n```console\n# Before\n(no output; the extras are gone after the reinstall)\n\n# After\n⚠ This install has extras that a bare re-run will remove: anthropic,daytona\n⚠   To keep them, re-run with: DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS=\"anthropic,daytona\"\nContinue anyway and remove them? [y/N]\n```\n\nA receipt that exists but can't be read or parsed (symlink, unreadable\npermissions, unexpected format) warns too — a false negative here costs\nthe user the exact packages this check protects.\n\n**Footer** — the footer now distinguishes a version move from a fresh\ninstall:\n\n```console\n# Before (any successful run)\n✔ Setup complete. Run: dcode\n\n# After (unpinned run that moved version)\n✔ Upgrade complete. Run: dcode\n```\n\nOther outcomes get their own wording: `Dependencies updated.` for a\nsame-version dependency bump and `Already installed.` for a no-op. A\npinned move (`bash -s -- 0.1.0` over 0.2.0 is a downgrade, and there's\nno version comparison to tell) keeps `Setup complete.`\n\n**Log path** — uv's full stderr (dependency diff, rebuild notice) is\ncaptured to a persistent log, but the script only mentioned it on\nfailure or a same-version dependency bump, so on a normal upgrade the\ndetails scrolled away with no way back. It's now printed after any\nsuccessful install that wrote a log:\n\n```console\n# After\n✔ deepagents-code upgraded to 0.2.0.\n▸ Full log: ~/.cache/deepagents/install.log\n```\n\nThe log stays under `~/.cache` (not `~/.deepagents/.state`) because it's\nephemeral output, not application state.","verified_at":"2026-08-06T06:10:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/21fd0d6794dcbe09b67e678863c14e02c4f2b6d9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6"}]},{"sha":"65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY1ZDZmZTI1NTQ5OGZlOWRmZTQ5MzI0NzllMDI2NmUzMTE3NWY2YTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T04:37:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T04:37:37Z"},"message":"docs(code): orient hooks package docstrings toward v2, banner legacy (#5347)\n\nAgents and developers landing on any hook-related file now get immediate\norientation on which hook system is current: the `hooks` package\ndocstring names Hooks v2 as current and legacy as deprecated (removal\nSeptember 1, 2026) and points to the canonical v2 references,\n`hooks/legacy.py` opens with a `DEPRECATED:` banner before its format\ndocumentation, `hooks/loading.py` includes a copy-pasteable minimal v2\nconfig example plus a pointer to the stdin payload envelope in\n`hooks/models/wire.py`, and `hooks/migration.py` notes that\n`_LEGACY_EVENT_MAP` is the authoritative list of legacy events still\nmigrated (unmapped events are silently dropped).\n\n---\n\nMotivation: an agent searching for \"hooks\" previously landed on\n`legacy.py` first — its ~70-line module docstring reads like the\ncanonical format reference — and could build against the legacy\nlist-shaped config without ever discovering Hooks v2. Meanwhile the\npackage entry point docstring gave no orientation at all.\n\nDocstring-only change; no behavior modified. Where details already live\nelsewhere (precedence, schema, wire envelope), the docstrings point to\nthe canonical module instead of restating them.","tree":{"sha":"3d1ac5cf4d7002d42f8c2ea8bccac9748f007f86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3d1ac5cf4d7002d42f8c2ea8bccac9748f007f86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdA+RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARtwQAHkZfP0BSRst3HZcvCFpPkNE\nZIzFHSu5RQMGhBu/Uvq1e1abSCQrFc5qfdBsQwqxCOuzSCaKFShT9cBjY29GYPwc\n6w2nedgtkzcEYzOGIAAOzVQLKyf2gTnN1sPRvIXWZKetHDZtoZrscmj8COKnNh2A\nGp7zXCe18t4hF3+4xaQlk8/HNZz8z9EEoBSuMHcIID+3cnQDKotvtny/rdd7jyH2\nw3HzVzwB7qWUXj9fiAaqAVppVnb8Qkewm1KES9JRaJ87YsnKrVU8ONFbg/jdF1+u\n5Osz3fHaTihRCgW6xFwnlI+GYQdf06qiENDFc7UUjBWJz3HswE89qh7ix/op7MJJ\nIN/fIVRvpTe4m0uQPOUh/RHLyf86vxlGtm84oLtfc2+zQiS90sfTSPhTUWahFxTy\ntZ8HOdVaQVwV9LW2Nb0FxY83eFnu15XTohpF/hrxQ3LYYg/fsOfCoY36IJn+PCag\nevxqEnzr5uJWo83WG7wggqddWW2Kc8GnXn/H0mDwNL6Zm8xmNVfjAO81K1RLM/WT\nrWCOaTlJWnVj3OWDrmkpNW8bugwM9e66XrxPxVExFHNcJwlxhHGRb5l//3yDeecc\nVPbBSS0gAcFelWqLLsftZfa5ADZ+CS1XcOkOVgER/HCoqiteJ7k5I9ECL0aoWRrF\nio++2UGfPlYcpl01xzU1\n=cKzr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3d1ac5cf4d7002d42f8c2ea8bccac9748f007f86\nparent be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785991057 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785991057 -0400\n\ndocs(code): orient hooks package docstrings toward v2, banner legacy (#5347)\n\nAgents and developers landing on any hook-related file now get immediate\norientation on which hook system is current: the `hooks` package\ndocstring names Hooks v2 as current and legacy as deprecated (removal\nSeptember 1, 2026) and points to the canonical v2 references,\n`hooks/legacy.py` opens with a `DEPRECATED:` banner before its format\ndocumentation, `hooks/loading.py` includes a copy-pasteable minimal v2\nconfig example plus a pointer to the stdin payload envelope in\n`hooks/models/wire.py`, and `hooks/migration.py` notes that\n`_LEGACY_EVENT_MAP` is the authoritative list of legacy events still\nmigrated (unmapped events are silently dropped).\n\n---\n\nMotivation: an agent searching for \"hooks\" previously landed on\n`legacy.py` first — its ~70-line module docstring reads like the\ncanonical format reference — and could build against the legacy\nlist-shaped config without ever discovering Hooks v2. Meanwhile the\npackage entry point docstring gave no orientation at all.\n\nDocstring-only change; no behavior modified. Where details already live\nelsewhere (precedence, schema, wire envelope), the docstrings point to\nthe canonical module instead of restating them.","verified_at":"2026-08-06T04:37:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/65d6fe255498fe9dfe4932479e0266e31175f6a6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8"}]},{"sha":"be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJlOTEwOTQxOTk1ZjBmZmFmNzgwODFkNjUxOWM3NGExODY0YjNkYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T03:50:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T03:50:36Z"},"message":"feat(infra): acknowledge accepted `@release-bot` commands with a reply comment (#5345)\n\nRunning `@release-bot draft` or `@release-bot apply` on a release-please\nPR now gets an immediate reply confirming the command was accepted,\ninstead of silence until the drafted or applied comment appears minutes\nlater.\n\n---\n\nManual release-bot commands go through several validation gates in\n`validateTrigger` — the PR must be a release-please branch, it must be\nready for review, and the commenter must have write access. Every\nrejection path already posted an explanatory comment, but the success\npath returned `shouldRun: true` without saying anything, leaving the\nmaintainer staring at an unchanged PR wondering whether the command\nregistered, whether the workflow is queued, or whether they mistyped the\nmention.\n\nThe acknowledgment comment is posted only after all gates pass and only\nfor manual `issue_comment` commands; the automatic `ready_for_review`\ndraft trigger stays silent to avoid adding noise to every release PR.\nThe reply names the command and component (e.g. \"Running `draft` for the\n`deepagents-code` release PR...\") so it's clear what was accepted, and\nnotes that the result arrives as a follow-up comment.","tree":{"sha":"c3bec04788402a735e439eea9c97431c9e7ecff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c3bec04788402a735e439eea9c97431c9e7ecff3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdASMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARkgQAI3OHuc/c7+H0BWmsCiBV2XF\nOw4rf018J67tj821BirwHphEPxgA7U5p9GMlAnKAzV3Go6fxWNRjoJOwiC/Tp0Mj\nPnk+Y5Kpx759ijYZttm34z+gLbWZ5/IQx3XbEtpP/Ij77VoYX4b9Od0qM/eYw8fZ\neM/ZpdH0F5aJHCUOPGHDf8ah1W/2wIW8Z56aqxkIYMraYR195aUh2ACpVUXNU/KT\nUMg6H7x7QDIS/HXaNuRgVZysykFvrq5qFOfJkgQBit12UNlWqP5n2UC70Ud6Byw4\ng2tW9B8INBQ/ysxvfUAXIE44tx3WPUzZVSSZ9QYQDy3fO0sY9bGoSsIA9ESVtdoq\nB4wSqS3uEOtX1lPJxBakoJmWFq58QggQWPU0SBTVN8lPri4QiM305ZdtRJl8dKgi\n9GkekiCIbVGoIw/iCModP9ZsmG8VXZyVxppL80aJ39pZC7/hSxOQwbR2TkayKJTf\nz4jFNdivNIVz2QiTexmwdLdS8Xwr/xSjWwSfjXAuW1Nmur6cGF/bRd3FcFxHQ+xI\nTGpiPt/0dnIeHm4zHF/EewzHJQ7yHWXaTk0eMLGbarfNq6T/5MSDomtW+y4DkSMZ\nv/lqXTM8yPiomEt/VTMQyaZpUaa0KbDUAs9ZcnQ3VjJzeux25kpJ7buhUdhLzwyQ\nCm90pH5C32w48vJGEoE7\n=EY3w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c3bec04788402a735e439eea9c97431c9e7ecff3\nparent 0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785988236 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785988236 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): acknowledge accepted `@release-bot` commands with a reply comment (#5345)\n\nRunning `@release-bot draft` or `@release-bot apply` on a release-please\nPR now gets an immediate reply confirming the command was accepted,\ninstead of silence until the drafted or applied comment appears minutes\nlater.\n\n---\n\nManual release-bot commands go through several validation gates in\n`validateTrigger` — the PR must be a release-please branch, it must be\nready for review, and the commenter must have write access. Every\nrejection path already posted an explanatory comment, but the success\npath returned `shouldRun: true` without saying anything, leaving the\nmaintainer staring at an unchanged PR wondering whether the command\nregistered, whether the workflow is queued, or whether they mistyped the\nmention.\n\nThe acknowledgment comment is posted only after all gates pass and only\nfor manual `issue_comment` commands; the automatic `ready_for_review`\ndraft trigger stays silent to avoid adding noise to every release PR.\nThe reply names the command and component (e.g. \"Running `draft` for the\n`deepagents-code` release PR...\") so it's clear what was accepted, and\nnotes that the result arrives as a follow-up comment.","verified_at":"2026-08-06T03:50:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be910941995f0ffaf78081d6519c74a1864b3dc8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec"}]},{"sha":"0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBiZDE1ZGMwZTFjNTJmYWZkZDQwNGY5MWI3YTE3MjMxMmI4ZjBmZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-06T03:10:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T03:10:59Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.53 (#5310)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.53](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.52...deepagents-code==0.1.53)\n(2026-08-06)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added pricing coverage with Baseten built-in overrides and local\nfallback overrides when `genai-prices` is missing data\n([#5312](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5312),\n[#5304](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5304)).\n- Suggest compacting large resumed threads\n([#5318](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5318)).\n- Added terminal program trace metadata\n([#5329](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5329)).\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Preserved runtime offload archive routing\n([#5328](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5328)).\n- Always restart after a successful startup auto-update\n([#5317](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5317)).\n- Fixed leaked turn coroutines and SQLite handles\n([#5218](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5218)).\n- Keep MCP shutdown-race tracebacks from appearing in the terminal\n([#5325](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5325)).\n- Open the `/auto model` selector immediately while connecting\n([#5341](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5341)).\n- Route failures to `PostToolUseFailure`\n([#5315](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5315)).\n- Use dismissed copy for ask-user prompts\n([#5331](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5331)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2d346ac7c777af9d20636bc763a4f679e33f210","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b2d346ac7c777af9d20636bc763a4f679e33f210"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc/tDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj7IQAAdYz8CpBGxzR7bT0TiZhhwj\n2c8ektsKabARa+74jdbt0XtAesrozfQp3C8M7Tcu2fT29sRT5wsVXvO+argon3fh\nuiBwAwv/O7Gx8sifc5Ql10kK0gaS2E6uSAm8+pfjhd/XWUfjoAhTBazx72wQVTRE\noXUAwtIIH/rsYgTslFM1R68rxlFdyLGVjHjGCsv3cBUM7MS++MbnvlwqZprKFWli\nPIC7m5S8KeBYKptXREOO+bV6xhhC/cv+KD8oBQEAnoBvTsflJ9IOAyCLuVkEV3bF\nG+M1VpgbcaPtiQZHMMnIu9LhU+FSFSimOgr1qFHQzafCaJ6Q/3rXh91bMnIkNJFc\nqjdHKQj9MylMQgmd8cOLXmR0Z7yJw7pFY/NGXJP3IFkh+0srXcvpV4B+9rXTscwi\nS5q1+WfzkvBdQ1Mn+CN7BYZgLmishvJYj2sNFxRRWRQJgR0kPjeMxVgqnNNrAP9r\nqCIsQ2lWeNvl1Q+cuis5gZtjW060BF/xMsFO+pYNnzuEjuV2goSYy633p14wvYa0\nWr/ei9MLhvYlGN8944iDTxgZ7aauhFEBcys8/2ZWYXsmwcyO+hMAobPi3bswv5Yi\nMMpVlx5SHu34eXqQyGAxv9vLCw835LxJC2yN9PUpZSiapynlj1dJPLD1OjYxegEX\nkmGTRlQJ4Q6EtJhl3l7N\n=5rfP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b2d346ac7c777af9d20636bc763a4f679e33f210\nparent 72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785985859 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785985859 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.53 (#5310)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.53](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.52...deepagents-code==0.1.53)\n(2026-08-06)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added pricing coverage with Baseten built-in overrides and local\nfallback overrides when `genai-prices` is missing data\n([#5312](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5312),\n[#5304](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5304)).\n- Suggest compacting large resumed threads\n([#5318](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5318)).\n- Added terminal program trace metadata\n([#5329](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5329)).\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Preserved runtime offload archive routing\n([#5328](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5328)).\n- Always restart after a successful startup auto-update\n([#5317](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5317)).\n- Fixed leaked turn coroutines and SQLite handles\n([#5218](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5218)).\n- Keep MCP shutdown-race tracebacks from appearing in the terminal\n([#5325](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5325)).\n- Open the `/auto model` selector immediately while connecting\n([#5341](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5341)).\n- Route failures to `PostToolUseFailure`\n([#5315](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5315)).\n- Use dismissed copy for ask-user prompts\n([#5331](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5331)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-06T03:11:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0bd15dc0e1c52fafdd404f91b7a172312b8f0fec/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d"}]},{"sha":"72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcyYmZjMWU2ODU3NDkwOWNlYjkyOWJlODY5YzY2ZmJkYzlmZTVhMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T01:45:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T01:45:13Z"},"message":"fix(code): open `/auto model` selector immediately while connecting (#5341)\n\nTyping `/auto model` during startup (or mid-turn) now opens the Auto\nclassifier model selector immediately, matching bare `/model`, instead\nof being parked behind the message queue until the app finishes\nconnecting.\n\n---\n\n`_can_bypass_queue` previously treated every argument form of an\n`IMMEDIATE_UI` command as queue-bound, because most of them act directly\n(`/model <name>` switches models). But `/auto model` with no further\narguments routes straight to the classifier picker — a modal that defers\nall validation and mutation (`_set_auto_classifier_model`, install-extra\nflow) to its dismiss callback, exactly like bare `/model`. There is no\nserver dependency at open time.\n\nThe fix adds an `IMMEDIATE_UI_ARG_FORMS` frozenset in\n`command_registry.py` next to the derived tier sets, so the bypass is\ndata-driven and extensible rather than an inline string special case.\n`_can_bypass_queue` now bypasses when the submitted value is the bare\ncommand or one of these whitelisted forms. The mutating forms — `/auto\nmodel <spec>` and `/auto model clear` — stay queue-bound, as does every\nother command's argument form.","tree":{"sha":"f3d609528e23a120da92bddbb65dceb0bb219dee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f3d609528e23a120da92bddbb65dceb0bb219dee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc+cpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAe8QAJzPEaFxPaI39DWVn6QorZDU\n31jgBNJs8OmT4yirrVthjmyVq1XfMK7s3V9/e6vpVji6uVilE4MLPm/+TxFy9uAi\n/1UPE840fci9v5whE4ic32RKqXSil0SWeQbiwSxjO+ZuuSYfrPpiFrTzOwZ4VRWl\nUwKmyUmrhYcLyxRxsfajhCmMspT4M4oqnd8xtbhULmcDMGdfu6qiHqNMMFiddISY\nzu39c0EsmSRo9KeEweFioE+Ukn1ClnyZPwrAk3f1fDI70CQAJwREb/EVmgEf4MFr\ngPt1P5G3R/Hf8iTwKeZaeyT5C5I+Jerb2J2BNKGl4/XUfVBt+cZZwzuECRJfUHbj\nLQj/l6kmdxpf3A97Qm2cRkHlxhMNtM0+lb4fgJ9egq6fXuLXFB6cKJKLIbE4DPv9\npcWcOVn/1q55cVJIB01pGb9VATk19h4GWpcJjI9dcwaDjWCTAyTgOMK4joTuySTN\nqyJsTy5hloDM970gGdW5Zc1q9JKtxdxniEmXTGa+3446NokapUK+d/FJO69NT4Ki\ncQx0ltdvb+Mn3VkG7vv890yDiBAUKWXDWwMe4kMw1dTeyW3UjpzetQDGmCCnFO+f\nylfGJ6udr+B0EFn8nPNClPf4x5qhPUhbeCde2igTlppudSm76dpqmsV//Gh0nmAq\nmNGqZIExKRK3LhrkrkxN\n=VR5m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f3d609528e23a120da92bddbb65dceb0bb219dee\nparent 63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785980713 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785980713 -0400\n\nfix(code): open `/auto model` selector immediately while connecting (#5341)\n\nTyping `/auto model` during startup (or mid-turn) now opens the Auto\nclassifier model selector immediately, matching bare `/model`, instead\nof being parked behind the message queue until the app finishes\nconnecting.\n\n---\n\n`_can_bypass_queue` previously treated every argument form of an\n`IMMEDIATE_UI` command as queue-bound, because most of them act directly\n(`/model <name>` switches models). But `/auto model` with no further\narguments routes straight to the classifier picker — a modal that defers\nall validation and mutation (`_set_auto_classifier_model`, install-extra\nflow) to its dismiss callback, exactly like bare `/model`. There is no\nserver dependency at open time.\n\nThe fix adds an `IMMEDIATE_UI_ARG_FORMS` frozenset in\n`command_registry.py` next to the derived tier sets, so the bypass is\ndata-driven and extensible rather than an inline string special case.\n`_can_bypass_queue` now bypasses when the submitted value is the bare\ncommand or one of these whitelisted forms. The mutating forms — `/auto\nmodel <spec>` and `/auto model clear` — stay queue-bound, as does every\nother command's argument form.","verified_at":"2026-08-06T01:45:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/72bfc1e68574909ceb929be869c66fbdc9fe5a1d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09"}]},{"sha":"63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYzYWExMjkwMzZjYzkzZTUyZjY1NTQwYWNiMWI4M2M2NGJhZDljMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T01:14:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T01:14:41Z"},"message":"chore(code): harden installer downloads, PATH setup, and shell coverage (#5336)\n\nHardens the installer's download path and reworks PATH setup to cover\nevery shell the user might open, adopting patterns from Meta's `muse`\ninstaller.\n\n## PATH setup\n\n- The PATH block is written to **every shell startup file that exists**\n— e.g. both `~/.bashrc` and `~/.bash_profile`, or a `ZDOTDIR` zshrc plus\na legacy `~/.zshrc` — so `dcode` resolves even if the user later\nswitches shells. One interactive prompt names every file the answer\ncovers.\n- The line written to each file is chosen by **the target file's syntax,\nnot the current shell**: only fish's `conf.d` file gets fish syntax;\n`.zshrc`, `.bashrc`, `.bash_profile` and `.profile` always get the POSIX\nexport.\n- Fish gets a standalone `conf.d/deepagents-code.fish` (auto-sourced by\nfish, honors `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`) instead of an edit to `config.fish`.\nRe-running replaces the managed block rather than appending another one.\n- `ZDOTDIR` is respected, from the environment or parsed out of\n`~/.zshenv`, and is honored even when the directory doesn't exist yet —\nzsh reads only `${ZDOTDIR}/.zshrc`, so the installer creates the\ndirectory and writes there rather than falling back to a `~/.zshrc` zsh\nwould never read. A pre-existing `~/.zshrc` is still updated alongside,\nso unsetting `ZDOTDIR` later doesn't strand the entry.\n- **Only a top-level `ZDOTDIR=` counts.** The portable-dotfiles idiom\nguards the relocation:\n\n  ```sh\nif [ -d \"$HOME/.config/zsh\" ]; then export ZDOTDIR=\"$HOME/.config/zsh\";\nfi\n  ```\n\nWhile that directory is absent the guard is false and zsh reads\n`~/.zshrc`. Honoring the assignment anyway would make the installer\n*create* the directory, flipping the guard true — after which zsh reads\nonly the new dir, holding nothing but the PATH block, and silently stops\nsourcing the user's aliases, prompt and plugins. Assignments nested in a\nblock are skipped. An unreadable `~/.zshenv` warns rather than silently\nfalling back.\n- Symlinked startup files keep their links: the rewrite follows the\nchain to the final regular file and replaces it with a temp-file + `mv`\nin that file's directory, so an interrupted install can't leave a\nchezmoi/stow/home-manager source truncated and the next `apply`/`restow`\ncan't revert the entry. The original mode is carried over, and a failure\nto restore it is reported rather than silently tightening the file to\n0600.\n- `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_MODIFY_PATH` opts out for version-managed dotfiles\nand MDM fleets: the binary is still installed and verified, no startup\nfiles are touched, and the manual export line is printed. It accepts the\nsame *truthy* spellings as `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES` and treats an\nunrecognized value as \"do not modify\" — an opt-out protecting managed\ndotfiles has to fail toward leaving them alone.\n- Writing a startup file never reports \"PATH is fixed for the current\nshell\", so the reload hint is always emitted and a failure on any\ncandidate is surfaced rather than masked by a success elsewhere. The\ninverse holds too: **declining the prompt writes nothing, so it does not\nprint \"Restart your shell\"** — a restart can't pick up an edit that was\nnever made.\n- Failure diagnostics name what actually failed. `mkdir`/`touch`\nfailures keep their error text, and the managed-block rewrite hedges its\nhint, since that path can also fail on an unresolvable symlink, a\n`mktemp` failure or a failed `mv`.\n\nThree deliberate divergences from muse's profile coverage:\n\n- On macOS, a missing `~/.bashrc` is not created — Terminal runs login\nshells that never read it. An existing `.bashrc` is still updated.\n- `~/.profile` is written when it is the file a bash login shell will\nactually read (bash files exist but neither `~/.bash_profile` nor\n`~/.bash_login` does), or when the current shell is neither zsh, bash,\nnor fish.\n- The login-file fallback tests what the run is *going to create*, not\nonly what is on disk. On macOS, bash with no dotfiles has\n`~/.bash_profile` queued as its primary file; checking the filesystem\nalone would add `~/.profile` too and create both.\n\n## Downloads\n\n- curl pins HTTPS for the request and any redirects (`--proto '=https'\n--proto-redir '=https'`) and caps redirect chains at 3.\n- wget has no `--proto-redir` equivalent: `--https-only` only applies in\nrecursive mode, so it doesn't stop a 3xx from downgrading a one-shot\nfetch (verified against wget 1.25.0 — it follows a 302 to plaintext and\nexits 0 where curl refuses). `wget_download` therefore rejects non-HTTPS\nURLs outright and audits the response headers for a downgrading\n`Location`, failing closed. `--https-only` and `--max-redirect=3` are\nstill passed where supported.\n- Hardening flags are probed against `wget --help` first, so BusyBox\nwget (Alpine) still works instead of dying on an unrecognized option.\nThe probe **captures** the help text before matching rather than piping\ninto `grep`: BusyBox exits 1 from `--help`, and under `set -o pipefail`\nthat status would become the pipeline's even on a match, reporting every\noption as unsupported. That fails *open* — it drops `-S` and reduces the\nredirect audit to a no-op on exactly the minimal systems the probe\nexists for. When `-S` genuinely isn't available, the missing audit is\nreported rather than degrading in silence.\n- The downloaded uv installer is parse-checked before execution with the\ninterpreter named in its own shebang, catching truncations that leave\nunbalanced syntax (the shebang check alone would pass them). That same\ninterpreter then runs it — checking with bash and executing with `sh`\nwould let bash-only syntax pass the check and fail at execution, with\nthe user pointed at a nonexistent truncated download.\n- Signal traps exit with the conventional 128+signal codes (129/130/143)\nso CI and wrappers can distinguish an interrupted install from an\nordinary failure. The handler defaults its signal argument: under `set\n-u` an unbound `$1` would abort the handler and let the EXIT trap print\nthe contradictory \"Installation failed\" line.\n- Download retry backoff doubled (2s then 4s) — a 1s/2s wait is too\nshort to outlast the transient it absorbs, and 6s total is still well\ninside a user's patience.","tree":{"sha":"19b4e343415fd908725853dc8cb5dac686f9dcd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/19b4e343415fd908725853dc8cb5dac686f9dcd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc+ABCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV88QADf6cVPyRxHIm04morIruNeX\nPEyonBKPoGHIvG0YCkLXXWSq1NukU83Rp4l6BocZQjavVMBv+OhPc8q8ZuANrF8r\nbDwOp3vp6X3tPfjvbABMhT+WxkJjlx0pIPdzzPFXblF7PZnd/KDHjr3l4mJdRHuW\nMW0XY9tmaS1P+ToXfIc7mRjsThYj2EcQ/TUu+gdwlxzpDpQzGC2AXexNcfk8g6W5\n+jo5CKSSqMTjirovFX2LS5eAE+AWWoWeKJ5pCUYXMgY9rj/Iz9jx4mVmBOkCl+m/\nngcByXPGyE7OvaC/k9m7AriJPbeC1Lbb6Gnm0Oicm1TN/6JsPpqPNF+0Kn8BVyeN\noB+KE4BfQ6cbnC2GUDazZxLiiAIhBNiArDld+ZH+tTaizQpJv0LG9BUnj1qbuvbI\n7CvFIPzPOLrPNzYme0KJN3ZeBxXOZCKqk5qldrPXnZeUpt2RZb9fu61W5FhBOiX7\nenMM3EBd12ul5NwqC5CDhh1t21hqFn6SvRLvBVibx2kSD0pE1hQLRlPQFGxqp/Qa\n8Zl8y5/GnO1gQ8MJ3KlRUN46Zj4ScQftD1rbsNjTN+8IGDHWTYCV9ZxFgXTkPnrd\nwltaUJrGJQot2mgI4+A/NDHUUc/Iol266V7IOGOydsDydXn3Pm0J0gHsSGr6GW/m\nPfsn6FJXVNTTa3eAW+qZ\n=XnkS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 19b4e343415fd908725853dc8cb5dac686f9dcd9\nparent bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785978881 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785978881 -0400\n\nchore(code): harden installer downloads, PATH setup, and shell coverage (#5336)\n\nHardens the installer's download path and reworks PATH setup to cover\nevery shell the user might open, adopting patterns from Meta's `muse`\ninstaller.\n\n## PATH setup\n\n- The PATH block is written to **every shell startup file that exists**\n— e.g. both `~/.bashrc` and `~/.bash_profile`, or a `ZDOTDIR` zshrc plus\na legacy `~/.zshrc` — so `dcode` resolves even if the user later\nswitches shells. One interactive prompt names every file the answer\ncovers.\n- The line written to each file is chosen by **the target file's syntax,\nnot the current shell**: only fish's `conf.d` file gets fish syntax;\n`.zshrc`, `.bashrc`, `.bash_profile` and `.profile` always get the POSIX\nexport.\n- Fish gets a standalone `conf.d/deepagents-code.fish` (auto-sourced by\nfish, honors `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`) instead of an edit to `config.fish`.\nRe-running replaces the managed block rather than appending another one.\n- `ZDOTDIR` is respected, from the environment or parsed out of\n`~/.zshenv`, and is honored even when the directory doesn't exist yet —\nzsh reads only `${ZDOTDIR}/.zshrc`, so the installer creates the\ndirectory and writes there rather than falling back to a `~/.zshrc` zsh\nwould never read. A pre-existing `~/.zshrc` is still updated alongside,\nso unsetting `ZDOTDIR` later doesn't strand the entry.\n- **Only a top-level `ZDOTDIR=` counts.** The portable-dotfiles idiom\nguards the relocation:\n\n  ```sh\nif [ -d \"$HOME/.config/zsh\" ]; then export ZDOTDIR=\"$HOME/.config/zsh\";\nfi\n  ```\n\nWhile that directory is absent the guard is false and zsh reads\n`~/.zshrc`. Honoring the assignment anyway would make the installer\n*create* the directory, flipping the guard true — after which zsh reads\nonly the new dir, holding nothing but the PATH block, and silently stops\nsourcing the user's aliases, prompt and plugins. Assignments nested in a\nblock are skipped. An unreadable `~/.zshenv` warns rather than silently\nfalling back.\n- Symlinked startup files keep their links: the rewrite follows the\nchain to the final regular file and replaces it with a temp-file + `mv`\nin that file's directory, so an interrupted install can't leave a\nchezmoi/stow/home-manager source truncated and the next `apply`/`restow`\ncan't revert the entry. The original mode is carried over, and a failure\nto restore it is reported rather than silently tightening the file to\n0600.\n- `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_MODIFY_PATH` opts out for version-managed dotfiles\nand MDM fleets: the binary is still installed and verified, no startup\nfiles are touched, and the manual export line is printed. It accepts the\nsame *truthy* spellings as `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES` and treats an\nunrecognized value as \"do not modify\" — an opt-out protecting managed\ndotfiles has to fail toward leaving them alone.\n- Writing a startup file never reports \"PATH is fixed for the current\nshell\", so the reload hint is always emitted and a failure on any\ncandidate is surfaced rather than masked by a success elsewhere. The\ninverse holds too: **declining the prompt writes nothing, so it does not\nprint \"Restart your shell\"** — a restart can't pick up an edit that was\nnever made.\n- Failure diagnostics name what actually failed. `mkdir`/`touch`\nfailures keep their error text, and the managed-block rewrite hedges its\nhint, since that path can also fail on an unresolvable symlink, a\n`mktemp` failure or a failed `mv`.\n\nThree deliberate divergences from muse's profile coverage:\n\n- On macOS, a missing `~/.bashrc` is not created — Terminal runs login\nshells that never read it. An existing `.bashrc` is still updated.\n- `~/.profile` is written when it is the file a bash login shell will\nactually read (bash files exist but neither `~/.bash_profile` nor\n`~/.bash_login` does), or when the current shell is neither zsh, bash,\nnor fish.\n- The login-file fallback tests what the run is *going to create*, not\nonly what is on disk. On macOS, bash with no dotfiles has\n`~/.bash_profile` queued as its primary file; checking the filesystem\nalone would add `~/.profile` too and create both.\n\n## Downloads\n\n- curl pins HTTPS for the request and any redirects (`--proto '=https'\n--proto-redir '=https'`) and caps redirect chains at 3.\n- wget has no `--proto-redir` equivalent: `--https-only` only applies in\nrecursive mode, so it doesn't stop a 3xx from downgrading a one-shot\nfetch (verified against wget 1.25.0 — it follows a 302 to plaintext and\nexits 0 where curl refuses). `wget_download` therefore rejects non-HTTPS\nURLs outright and audits the response headers for a downgrading\n`Location`, failing closed. `--https-only` and `--max-redirect=3` are\nstill passed where supported.\n- Hardening flags are probed against `wget --help` first, so BusyBox\nwget (Alpine) still works instead of dying on an unrecognized option.\nThe probe **captures** the help text before matching rather than piping\ninto `grep`: BusyBox exits 1 from `--help`, and under `set -o pipefail`\nthat status would become the pipeline's even on a match, reporting every\noption as unsupported. That fails *open* — it drops `-S` and reduces the\nredirect audit to a no-op on exactly the minimal systems the probe\nexists for. When `-S` genuinely isn't available, the missing audit is\nreported rather than degrading in silence.\n- The downloaded uv installer is parse-checked before execution with the\ninterpreter named in its own shebang, catching truncations that leave\nunbalanced syntax (the shebang check alone would pass them). That same\ninterpreter then runs it — checking with bash and executing with `sh`\nwould let bash-only syntax pass the check and fail at execution, with\nthe user pointed at a nonexistent truncated download.\n- Signal traps exit with the conventional 128+signal codes (129/130/143)\nso CI and wrappers can distinguish an interrupted install from an\nordinary failure. The handler defaults its signal argument: under `set\n-u` an unbound `$1` would abort the handler and let the EXIT trap print\nthe contradictory \"Installation failed\" line.\n- Download retry backoff doubled (2s then 4s) — a 1s/2s wait is too\nshort to outlast the transient it absorbs, and 6s total is still well\ninside a user's patience.","verified_at":"2026-08-06T01:14:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63aa129036cc93e52f65540acb1b83c64bad9c09/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1"}]},{"sha":"bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJkMjA3OWJiZDU5N2ZmN2YyOGRiNTQ2NmUwYzYyNDM0Yjg0ZDZmZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T01:01:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T01:01:38Z"},"message":"style(code): trim Auto classifier picker copy and show active model (#5311)\n\nThe `/auto model` picker now says which model Auto currently reviews\nactions with, and drops the description copy that duplicated the `/auto`\nusage text.\n\n---\n\nThe old description spent its sentences on caveats already covered by\nthe `/auto` usage text: a warning that a weaker model weakens the\nreview, and an instruction to run `/auto model clear`. In their place\nthe modal names the active classifier, distinguishing an explicitly\nconfigured one from the main agent model it otherwise inherits, resolved\nthrough the existing `_auto_classifier_review_model_spec` and\n`_auto_classifier_display_spec` helpers. The usage text still carries\nthe \"clear\" hint and the fallback behavior; the picker keeps only the\npointer to `/auto model clear` when a classifier is explicitly set.\n\nThe description is passed as a plain `Content` rather than a string so a\nuser-controlled model spec is never parsed as Rich markup.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/fb473506-b2dc-14d6-b2ab-442b791cecc9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"593ae6802114b346c7a244f44aea5ebf4fdbf627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/593ae6802114b346c7a244f44aea5ebf4fdbf627"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc9zyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGtoQAIfUdgwcIl2ZL9Q1JPNIt9vh\nqqD87nVJZIFPfi5vpMeFgOUl97xPZLGcuEH4p9sVVUZ0aHhIK1644TYEUD70UYa4\nQzFu0xadkmKyz7cgyqkab2Imn9l058r4FKPz2ehB3iWIlaibFpLWeNENkX06ovpv\nNHEhrsXR+t/3tHmoC1ZAcrB6SW7zI3F2EINXj5JGTO/Nds6DtvApigVHXhK0qRLA\np1FNuWVvL+pDX5igkv1LYqwYRC73oB66jW9lro1cDeA55strmFK1U7qZfq8hnJah\nVpAyvKNWvyoLm4/l4LJFCiHmKHO/0Nt5wU7CkUSH7pC89ATSO+KBFxvTlpunKuZy\nGtFgh+3v9i52saJYvkhVzBH4lLjXkDIPf5lj5xC/l3UplCKmrcKpzppN2EaHKm/Q\nGqjfgr2VTCrD357GSsfeseR50yc9lR/npwTRgZRuewJtTRk1Xp35ZAzwgGxz0346\nSj8hIz9+Gksyl3f3PeuoBPfHf+T+ufRe0sYnEGvOW7L1NSRxUjNunx3PNl1+hJHQ\ngn+dCPAukA1dJNuL2VJLYgvoEhIHPWWYyseDqL50ur2FbqNCeES7QD81KmMFgohh\nBTINU0d9CXPo7dcmcDOrws0363DHS0daRGgIvURAifnhyJv6OMhlrD3t0TTfXPLt\nypsnxA7vw745AUGjrU2H\n=ZMnN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 593ae6802114b346c7a244f44aea5ebf4fdbf627\nparent 8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785978098 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785978098 -0400\n\nstyle(code): trim Auto classifier picker copy and show active model (#5311)\n\nThe `/auto model` picker now says which model Auto currently reviews\nactions with, and drops the description copy that duplicated the `/auto`\nusage text.\n\n---\n\nThe old description spent its sentences on caveats already covered by\nthe `/auto` usage text: a warning that a weaker model weakens the\nreview, and an instruction to run `/auto model clear`. In their place\nthe modal names the active classifier, distinguishing an explicitly\nconfigured one from the main agent model it otherwise inherits, resolved\nthrough the existing `_auto_classifier_review_model_spec` and\n`_auto_classifier_display_spec` helpers. The usage text still carries\nthe \"clear\" hint and the fallback behavior; the picker keeps only the\npointer to `/auto model clear` when a classifier is explicitly set.\n\nThe description is passed as a plain `Content` rather than a string so a\nuser-controlled model spec is never parsed as Rich markup.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/fb473506-b2dc-14d6-b2ab-442b791cecc9)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-06T01:01:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd2079bbd597ff7f28db5466e0c62434b84d6ff1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5"}]},{"sha":"8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhjZGVlMTViYmM1NDM4MTIyOWE2ODZmODI2MzY1NmJlMDIwMmI5YjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T00:59:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T00:59:36Z"},"message":"fix(code): always restart after a successful startup auto-update (#5317)\n\nAfter a startup auto-update installs, `dcode` now always restarts into\nthe new version instead of continuing with a mix of old and new code —\nwhich could crash startup with an `ImportError` or show the old version\non the splash screen. If the restart cannot happen, it prints the new\nversion and asks you to relaunch rather than starting a broken session.\n\n---\n\nThe install rewrites the site-packages the running process imports from,\nso modules already loaded stay on the old release while the TUI loads\nfrom the new one; a constant added in 0.1.52 made that combination\ncrash.\n\n- The shadow detector compares resolved targets, so it accepts an alias\nthat leads into the upgraded uv installation while still detecting\ngenuine PATH shadows.\n- On Windows, uv shim selection now resolves `PATHEXT` candidates only\ninside uv’s bin directory. This recognizes `.cmd` aliases to uv’s `.exe`\nshim and prevents a project-local executable from becoming the\nauto-update restart target.\n- Failed `os.execv` prints a relaunch hint and exits `0`; other\npost-install errors name the error, point at the debug log, and exit\n`1`. Both record the update cooldown so a persistently failing re-exec\ncannot loop forever.\n- Failed installs remain fail-soft and launch the existing version.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9f0447bd33dae2e50a44cdc922407e5f17f7ee8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b9f0447bd33dae2e50a44cdc922407e5f17f7ee8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc9x4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9QwQADwRk8/GQYbhg6gd9KFO4cAt\ngIHxON7RnGHVNc3rkxYt225MU2PzS5JAeMLQ3B1pFHtgGoW8sIQgS2Vv67ZZ9ffV\nlNSBoaHsLGKWORPXwQHgQUIda+a1jK/fRltMZ8GeaM4Dx3O2ByahMiVS/QXqqyC9\nZ6f2PtAnzqLTwe38+fBHwd0Vpoit1HoKgq01lXXcia0LMlCwXHBq/CJRPBgyo6Wz\neQlyWJ7lZ6/Q1GjStAXC9XlRvfQn401zU2ELWbQSKoBNgERHF/RtW1uhsFJ4i0oM\ni4lsA+3RMYe/0Kek07cVEb6i86KpY4GXO2JPwKH24193ERiW00Ekkn74YyHw1PkD\nuFavBR4eStVgLk5Bvt+i8s9w0EKnf0GSAFnDcqUMIdzBEJENmDDIAZKBWzY8jMJk\n7vhMPQ6JglSkgN6f9+rdYJ8+ClYN8SfBCN15quUQcMcybct3ovLT691pbPsDO69X\nUkMghXDOpwbmslzMjmexpZcnmykH78JrF34Kfck17D4OadvQEbRRO+FIZwhSvzHm\njkocRUwrYh2qdCvXWREFblhKs2Pf2eaaGUAnbReGXCs97Q1V1Gez9wqJDqdRwQo+\nOqcp2mQOoI+cGma9c50WLxvqJqI7aGeoJLREy/YGvBcUZeq0AEY7fqT3yN948AO2\n1FKm98hvQQBUn1dXj2i1\n=UVHP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9f0447bd33dae2e50a44cdc922407e5f17f7ee8\nparent 920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785977976 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785977976 -0400\n\nfix(code): always restart after a successful startup auto-update (#5317)\n\nAfter a startup auto-update installs, `dcode` now always restarts into\nthe new version instead of continuing with a mix of old and new code —\nwhich could crash startup with an `ImportError` or show the old version\non the splash screen. If the restart cannot happen, it prints the new\nversion and asks you to relaunch rather than starting a broken session.\n\n---\n\nThe install rewrites the site-packages the running process imports from,\nso modules already loaded stay on the old release while the TUI loads\nfrom the new one; a constant added in 0.1.52 made that combination\ncrash.\n\n- The shadow detector compares resolved targets, so it accepts an alias\nthat leads into the upgraded uv installation while still detecting\ngenuine PATH shadows.\n- On Windows, uv shim selection now resolves `PATHEXT` candidates only\ninside uv’s bin directory. This recognizes `.cmd` aliases to uv’s `.exe`\nshim and prevents a project-local executable from becoming the\nauto-update restart target.\n- Failed `os.execv` prints a relaunch hint and exits `0`; other\npost-install errors name the error, point at the debug log, and exit\n`1`. Both record the update cooldown so a persistently failing re-exec\ncannot loop forever.\n- Failed installs remain fail-soft and launch the existing version.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-06T00:59:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8cdee15bbc54381229a686f8263656be0202b9b5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f"}]},{"sha":"920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkyMGZiNjY3NjNlODViNzU5YzJlYzNjYWMwOTBiY2NkN2YwNWI1NWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-06T00:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-06T00:17:41Z"},"message":"fix(code): use dismissed copy for ask-user prompts (#5331)\n\nDismissing an `ask_user` prompt now shows \"Question dismissed\"\n(pluralized when a batch dismissed several questions) instead of\n\"Question cancelled\" — \"cancelled\" already means interrupting a turn\nwith Ctrl+C. When a dismissal or rejection discarded answers typed into\nanother prompt in the same batch, the banner naming that loss now says\nwhich of the two caused it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9f7aa705f0d60832cea7bf702436815f2a5611d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d9f7aa705f0d60832cea7bf702436815f2a5611d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc9KlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKN4QALIKFMwWV82VdcTACJ/82BJO\naRT6US1FdFQTsCNCimwJSGnjwdilI/vJvpMlbhaJCBtfaYB2M+2lqVPwYnVkWERU\nY7tTcL8Nf91EFBTZ90yMd4deUj7ByazQ83gg2RnvmEjXOSDiczSFTs5A3J6ChY12\nunfAIF3D2mv4mbUBC4aN2W8D5fM73twIX+ZMgyXCVDDcknxp1G9aN5WHCHTMWklI\nSe8jHdYEvoXTPKb9UWRTzqfsGytRQS1hDD6PvDLSwyOTpRRZTUOMe6xJAoLOY4yr\nBHLy5kUxgLPPaiUbHNlfRE4XnzncG/+RmQJwIUfvQtAojsP39hxurmGWTIi3dXLn\noAMWQjp6boFtD9tN2lR5KDLVqZ9jDEUwfyNQG6jiROaR2St57XkdhECtntLtXuwa\nC7HaBO+VY6UyDvDf45d+y4WyELJ/ffdvLzoi+k05Zz4bhYf1ovmBjBywPXP3pyAv\nFzQAKOXqm49XXtGl8NQUdHnICmd2B0mNlhXkNY0rFvrJXZ7tIzMjbxdu74oNczRR\nyDtGchpQWgXURkHicvrprJ3ObT7uCeJAESfIbm6cqs+Sd+iVairtvN5cpApUppCr\ntkr/+aYQyfAN2wqS5GMWgx4fLPoyK2VBgHQBv54NN65IHS4jDfrE7uaoJmUE10oH\nrk6JZ62CwabEH4VKeJhq\n=gZ4h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9f7aa705f0d60832cea7bf702436815f2a5611d\nparent cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785975461 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785975461 -0400\n\nfix(code): use dismissed copy for ask-user prompts (#5331)\n\nDismissing an `ask_user` prompt now shows \"Question dismissed\"\n(pluralized when a batch dismissed several questions) instead of\n\"Question cancelled\" — \"cancelled\" already means interrupting a turn\nwith Ctrl+C. When a dismissal or rejection discarded answers typed into\nanother prompt in the same batch, the banner naming that loss now says\nwhich of the two caused it.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-06T00:17:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/920fb66763e85b759c2ec3cac090bccd7f05b55f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7"}]},{"sha":"cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNiMjMyOWQxZWM0ODA0NTVhN2JhNGUyYjI3N2NiZDcyN2M5MjE1Yzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-05T23:58:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T23:58:53Z"},"message":"feat(code): suggest compacting large resumed threads (#5318)\n\nLarge-context threads now offer compaction before resume, with options\nto continue without compacting or cancel.\n\n---\n\nThe threshold defaults to 400,000 tokens and is configurable with\n`[threads].compact_on_resume_threshold`.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"783\" height=\"308\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-05 at 10 21 45 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ac3b711-2653-44de-a324-727993d4a6fb\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"beb42c035d94179026357613b58fcdfaa052ec44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/beb42c035d94179026357613b58fcdfaa052ec44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc849CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/2UQAFUH2DTtuOeE8KLOGifdNqLG\neKDJtr8uZBVU/Abrr8XQfko4nIPjCBYsli0YYX3H5jrBHG5Ao8qM2O3Y1UcUkpf0\neM4BN8fwXl7DwgjWncoouUqg2MpSsMritVpj9TdbHkRUVVJ7pdM7iedv5phma3di\nZHiLCqmPrXah2YmwTu13Hqiu/uBG8Ia6Xw/YqLcDdnFJiilVBv7jWWcUzhBKCcFg\nzMg6rtmuYHnXSI4runZRlT0droDEHHxFBacERzrZ0hQk6xbqA1s6P0mQPTxr239s\nCjY+oKIUSC3JcIV3Q7zUP1S/XfKZsRI87SQprytAWVK6EPEqo2+Ma7lMhS+bSwij\nppqo4HiOmeHRdawiogqBjP4/MxN0/oV9psoEXvZO9UEMYeECT2slHptswCtitD7Z\njUXeeaAcl7ZQz9YMaI87ESyzRq/eIfaS0TDXnIn9qiqevFZeC4TD3oXSfZNZz0lk\nMtNGpgNiefvtk4QBX8Ue0bKArXMtkdlR+j9KJpNDWoSv7hf1dtamqzyt1z7XJgMk\nqMFC8UlIP/MpUlY1+kYP6KbmQmJCijx0pbUlnhrl0AU69a7ZclbA2sUTkwn53SBK\nX8n2FuWstwBvcd3KY5apcOgdY3PL4OXCn0F1RRaSVyRq6oJ5s9IBJdI4xhixhgUF\nu7rv/38DXsnBIKenroAI\n=cfgS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree beb42c035d94179026357613b58fcdfaa052ec44\nparent ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785974333 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785974333 +0000\n\nfeat(code): suggest compacting large resumed threads (#5318)\n\nLarge-context threads now offer compaction before resume, with options\nto continue without compacting or cancel.\n\n---\n\nThe threshold defaults to 400,000 tokens and is configurable with\n`[threads].compact_on_resume_threshold`.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"783\" height=\"308\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-05 at 10 21 45 AM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ac3b711-2653-44de-a324-727993d4a6fb\"\n/>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-05T23:58:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cb2329d1ec480455a7ba4e2b277cbd727c9215c7/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c"}]},{"sha":"ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVkMGI2Nzg1ZjhlMGQ3M2MzNTI2ZDBkMjFlZjU1YjQ3OTFmOGU0MWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-05T23:06:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T23:06:32Z"},"message":"feat(ci): raise langchain minimums workflow (#5330)\n\nAdds a workflow that raises LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds\nto the latest stable PyPI release and opens a `chore(deps):` PR with the\nresult. Runs weekly (Monday 09:00 UTC) across every release package, and\ncan be dispatched manually against a single package or `all`.\n\nKeeping integration minimums current is a recurring manual chore. This\nautomates the \"bump the floor\" half: for each in-scope requirement\n(`langchain*`, `langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) declaring a\n`>=`/`~=` floor in `[project.dependencies]`,\n`[project.optional-dependencies]`, or `[dependency-groups]`, the floor\nis rewritten in place and one PR is opened.\n\n- **Raises within the existing range, never past an upper bound.**\n`deepagents>=0.7.0,<0.8.0` becomes `>=0.7.9,<0.8.0`, never the\nunsatisfiable `>=0.8.0,<0.8.0`. Pre-releases are never selected, and a\nfloor already ahead of the latest stable release (intentional prerelease\ncoordination) is left alone. Each rewrite is checked against the\nversions PyPI actually offers, so a bump can't quietly exclude a version\nthe old range allowed.\n- **Preserves everything else in the specifier.** Upper bounds, extras,\nand markers survive verbatim, and `~=` ceilings are held by keeping the\noriginal component count — `~=1.2` becomes `~=1.9`, not `~=1.9.4`.\n- **Skips what it shouldn't touch.** Exact `==` pins, specs with no\nfloor, URL requirements, workspace-local `[tool.uv.sources]` deps, and\nthe manifest's own package name.\n- **Regenerates every `uv.lock` the edits invalidate** — not only the\nedited packages: a lockfile embeds the specifiers of anything it\nresolves from a local path source, so raising a floor in\n`libs/deepagents` stales `libs/evals` and friends. Interpreter versions\ncome from `check_lockfiles_pre_commit` so they match what\n`check_lockfiles.yml` verifies.\n- **Reports failure instead of silence.** An unresolvable PyPI lookup or\nan unrewritable manifest is listed in the PR body under \"Not raised\" and\nfails the run, so an unattended cron never renders an outage as\n\"everything is already up to date\".\n- **Idempotent per package.** If a PR is already open for the selected\npackage, or nothing needs raising, the run exits without creating a\nduplicate. PRs are created with the Org Membership App token so required\n`pull_request` checks trigger, and titled `chore(deps):` so\nrelease-please doesn't fan out a separate release PR.","tree":{"sha":"a7cf6409af44e2425a7d43cb8346ff87e0a29d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a7cf6409af44e2425a7d43cb8346ff87e0a29d02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc8H4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA13MQAA9LZ2NHBzwy0lXFk6SpQkpZ\nZFCdSlbAhelUYJx540icZpa9LlfZZSS8JccGBy2/gfFF9yfhgqtTczR1xLPi+p1q\nqJMOg0IE3sMMCpZPxRkJ/v2QXfWTAldWUctUe7K4sSHzAeEJn1x3drHV70aEiXek\nEUkmNKTuGrRWaep4vb7RjHYc44HU8n3quBixmoN5ApxnYW9s4Z38SJ6A/aCaveFV\nZDdxbsep+WwJFbMg4IEuiZUkZwIodz57nUBi/PrAHY6XhOZ7S1bKQpzMiqquvzVn\np1qy8BTjq4M4wxl3YtLTV1ZrfJmr3oBwIo7IboKb74JjSYO+dIdQA1MRsDP8M+Qa\nVIj3mV4paCYkBs4VqLaajAYL0vTOTWWIHX7SiC3IzWVTg7+xyntoLudu6CAWQdb7\nFsLQf9k2HgeKG1HgHMAFHSmkNwOaZogGjO4PqlJM8Zrwzo+igvvWJK2fxHSMHTke\n8tc6avXD7s0cNzXhToB2LQFc3oSf8+EnKFMtD8T7b/oQjWMmyVMAXnGkxR1ZZVWl\nOOJO9SARJWzy0xZI+qr7N+kZJgWZYQEhgWStS1ML6edEd0sbLGWfx2wGAv1HWAGs\n8924Tx3BDaPoEmsfvJESI/moBTvKm+9g4gw5LGpSDpGdK3DqNTZNspoH11G/KP5n\nj/PsWHoV0STFG8qOSrzS\n=skQW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7cf6409af44e2425a7d43cb8346ff87e0a29d02\nparent 7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785971192 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785971192 -0400\n\nfeat(ci): raise langchain minimums workflow (#5330)\n\nAdds a workflow that raises LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds\nto the latest stable PyPI release and opens a `chore(deps):` PR with the\nresult. Runs weekly (Monday 09:00 UTC) across every release package, and\ncan be dispatched manually against a single package or `all`.\n\nKeeping integration minimums current is a recurring manual chore. This\nautomates the \"bump the floor\" half: for each in-scope requirement\n(`langchain*`, `langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) declaring a\n`>=`/`~=` floor in `[project.dependencies]`,\n`[project.optional-dependencies]`, or `[dependency-groups]`, the floor\nis rewritten in place and one PR is opened.\n\n- **Raises within the existing range, never past an upper bound.**\n`deepagents>=0.7.0,<0.8.0` becomes `>=0.7.9,<0.8.0`, never the\nunsatisfiable `>=0.8.0,<0.8.0`. Pre-releases are never selected, and a\nfloor already ahead of the latest stable release (intentional prerelease\ncoordination) is left alone. Each rewrite is checked against the\nversions PyPI actually offers, so a bump can't quietly exclude a version\nthe old range allowed.\n- **Preserves everything else in the specifier.** Upper bounds, extras,\nand markers survive verbatim, and `~=` ceilings are held by keeping the\noriginal component count — `~=1.2` becomes `~=1.9`, not `~=1.9.4`.\n- **Skips what it shouldn't touch.** Exact `==` pins, specs with no\nfloor, URL requirements, workspace-local `[tool.uv.sources]` deps, and\nthe manifest's own package name.\n- **Regenerates every `uv.lock` the edits invalidate** — not only the\nedited packages: a lockfile embeds the specifiers of anything it\nresolves from a local path source, so raising a floor in\n`libs/deepagents` stales `libs/evals` and friends. Interpreter versions\ncome from `check_lockfiles_pre_commit` so they match what\n`check_lockfiles.yml` verifies.\n- **Reports failure instead of silence.** An unresolvable PyPI lookup or\nan unrewritable manifest is listed in the PR body under \"Not raised\" and\nfails the run, so an unattended cron never renders an outage as\n\"everything is already up to date\".\n- **Idempotent per package.** If a PR is already open for the selected\npackage, or nothing needs raising, the run exits without creating a\nduplicate. PRs are created with the Org Membership App token so required\n`pull_request` checks trigger, and titled `chore(deps):` so\nrelease-please doesn't fan out a separate release PR.","verified_at":"2026-08-05T23:06:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed0b6785f8e0d73c3526d0d21ef55b4791f8e41c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9"}]},{"sha":"7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdkOTcwOTcwMGRkMjRjYzI0NzdjZDA5MWYwMWRlOTkwZjIzZWU0YTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-05T22:59:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T22:59:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep MCP shutdown-race traceback off the terminal (#5325)\n\nQuitting `dcode` while an MCP response is in flight no longer prints an\n`anyio.ClosedResourceError` traceback to the terminal on exit.\n\n---\n\nAn MCP transport's reader task can still be running while the session\nstream is torn down. Its `read_stream_writer.send(...)` raises\n`anyio.ClosedResourceError`, the SDK's surrounding `except` calls\n`logger.exception(...)`, and since nothing handles the `mcp` hierarchy\nthe record clears `logging.lastResort`'s WARNING threshold and prints a\nfull traceback — alarming-looking but harmless, since the app was\nalready exiting.\n\nA `logging.Filter` on each transport's own logger drops those records.\nIt has to live on the emitting logger: logger-level filters never run\nfor records propagated up from children.\n\n`_MCP_SHUTDOWN_RACE_MESSAGES` lists the messages whose `try` block wraps\na read-stream `send`, and a record is dropped only if it carries an\nanyio closed/broken-resource error:\n\n| Logger | Message |\n| --- | --- |\n| `mcp.client.streamable_http` | `Error parsing JSON response` (single\nJSON body) |\n| `mcp.client.streamable_http` | `Error parsing SSE message` (streamed\nresponse) |\n| `mcp.client.sse` | `Error in sse_reader` |\n\n`Error in post_writer` is excluded — it wraps the entire write loop, so\na closed stream there can also mean the transport was orphaned while the\nsession was live.\n\n**Why this is safe.** The in-flight request still fails loudly: the\nsession's receive loop hands pending response streams an\n`ErrorData(CONNECTION_CLOSED)` on its way out, so `send_request` raises\n`McpError(\"Connection closed\")`. A network-level drop can't reach the\nfilter — `httpcore` remaps anyio's stream errors onto `httpx.ReadError`\nand friends before httpx re-raises, and the filter never walks\n`__cause__`. For a `BaseExceptionGroup`, every leaf must be a teardown,\nso a group carrying a real fault stays visible. The `mcp` hierarchy gets\nno `NullHandler` (pinned by a test), so everything else reaches stderr.\n\n**Debug mode.** With `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` set, an installed filter is\n*removed* and the transport loggers are routed to the debug log. Both\nhalves matter: the filter would otherwise suppress the record for the\ndebug file handler too, and without that handler it would fall through\nto `lastResort` and print over the TUI.\n\nDrift-pin tests read the logger names off the installed `mcp` modules —\nmirroring the existing `genai-prices` pin — so an upstream rename fails\nin CI rather than in a user's terminal.","tree":{"sha":"1e6779ed7a41bcc64b4c9bb20befdf0659f79d99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1e6779ed7a41bcc64b4c9bb20befdf0659f79d99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc8BSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADHwQAFXbt23D6Zdv2MOeek6eAtWd\n3bKhVx01JJib7H1DH7U/Vo4Gs0qvdwjgbJCtGM0itTRdjW6geuoriFo4R5IPmFwf\nOzb32hF3qHMUA65C2DOosirh52KZwnAa+BIkFDyyiloelT3BRaPM048iV05lSvb0\nvrI2s7fQQyWbsCuEUg+UV29bwLh20xyhE99jigztg7Giwr8CyV37wvED85nG0Znw\n3RTSL10Z45JigV2dovZ15IM23nFw4aMBk6J04ILLLr7ikxfyFYRz6B1wYI5oM8im\nlG49hfzRkxqIlrGSp7iDr6GwXRnUPzJYR3ZEB2RtU+ospZLzf9+WDKq6hL8XWIF1\n+uv15WjqKGt+muV57tFBcPiQWdAe2j/SAt/IeywdE9UwxsUy2nNtl3UKBjeiz1m6\nxF7T4fq9e+aiFDy+0aXFxaFD4eJiiqA9sx1jEE/TzADZ90pbcDlbrvIE+4HoIc6d\nRksLJeCjxChRfwB/CoqdgKHC5GQRrKWvPB4qgGURbnb6yGZ0hybiCO5k5LzPYvU+\nzfLG3RYS8s0rkQhl/E12s5OYS75Q4NhxOYE2iI7UsZA1jlcLpm1s0Mc9lObKVhK6\nOZw1wtgUNzR0N/z9x46kz/ai3kWm1Z4JovwvPQRQRyfCU/Mmr+YartzOK3gM20ZL\noI+DxqDat401Hh7C9bcp\n=IGeD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1e6779ed7a41bcc64b4c9bb20befdf0659f79d99\nparent 43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785970770 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785970770 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep MCP shutdown-race traceback off the terminal (#5325)\n\nQuitting `dcode` while an MCP response is in flight no longer prints an\n`anyio.ClosedResourceError` traceback to the terminal on exit.\n\n---\n\nAn MCP transport's reader task can still be running while the session\nstream is torn down. Its `read_stream_writer.send(...)` raises\n`anyio.ClosedResourceError`, the SDK's surrounding `except` calls\n`logger.exception(...)`, and since nothing handles the `mcp` hierarchy\nthe record clears `logging.lastResort`'s WARNING threshold and prints a\nfull traceback — alarming-looking but harmless, since the app was\nalready exiting.\n\nA `logging.Filter` on each transport's own logger drops those records.\nIt has to live on the emitting logger: logger-level filters never run\nfor records propagated up from children.\n\n`_MCP_SHUTDOWN_RACE_MESSAGES` lists the messages whose `try` block wraps\na read-stream `send`, and a record is dropped only if it carries an\nanyio closed/broken-resource error:\n\n| Logger | Message |\n| --- | --- |\n| `mcp.client.streamable_http` | `Error parsing JSON response` (single\nJSON body) |\n| `mcp.client.streamable_http` | `Error parsing SSE message` (streamed\nresponse) |\n| `mcp.client.sse` | `Error in sse_reader` |\n\n`Error in post_writer` is excluded — it wraps the entire write loop, so\na closed stream there can also mean the transport was orphaned while the\nsession was live.\n\n**Why this is safe.** The in-flight request still fails loudly: the\nsession's receive loop hands pending response streams an\n`ErrorData(CONNECTION_CLOSED)` on its way out, so `send_request` raises\n`McpError(\"Connection closed\")`. A network-level drop can't reach the\nfilter — `httpcore` remaps anyio's stream errors onto `httpx.ReadError`\nand friends before httpx re-raises, and the filter never walks\n`__cause__`. For a `BaseExceptionGroup`, every leaf must be a teardown,\nso a group carrying a real fault stays visible. The `mcp` hierarchy gets\nno `NullHandler` (pinned by a test), so everything else reaches stderr.\n\n**Debug mode.** With `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` set, an installed filter is\n*removed* and the transport loggers are routed to the debug log. Both\nhalves matter: the filter would otherwise suppress the record for the\ndebug file handler too, and without that handler it would fall through\nto `lastResort` and print over the TUI.\n\nDrift-pin tests read the logger names off the installed `mcp` modules —\nmirroring the existing `genai-prices` pin — so an upstream rename fails\nin CI rather than in a user's terminal.","verified_at":"2026-08-05T22:59:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d9709700dd24cc2477cd091f01de990f23ee4a9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4"}]},{"sha":"43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzZDZiZDRhMWE2NzNjNzlkMThhODBlZjQ2MjdjYjUyMzM2ZGI4YzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-05T22:50:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T22:50:50Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 5.0.1 to 5.0.2 in the minor-and-patch group (#5338)\n\nBumps the minor-and-patch group with 1 update:\n[CodSpeedHQ/action](https://github.com/codspeedhq/action).\n\nUpdates `CodSpeedHQ/action` from 5.0.1 to 5.0.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/codspeedhq/action/releases\">CodSpeedHQ/action's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v5.0.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: add cycle-estimation and exclude-allocations inputs by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/pull/229\">CodSpeedHQ/action#229</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/compare/v5.0.1...v5.0.2\">https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/compare/v5.0.1...v5.0.2</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/0ca9cbbf4623b599a6c3ed4fc8a922942705d9f1\"><code>0ca9cbb</code></a>\nRelease v5.0.2 🚀</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/551137a90ed15b86fd959940ef7f195859e4f2a3\"><code>551137a</code></a>\nci: restrict GITHUB_TOKEN to contents: read</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/fc6326417e24ad420663371d3395c17c282acb8b\"><code>fc63264</code></a>\nfeat: add cycle-estimation and exclude-allocations inputs</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/codspeedhq/action/compare/88472375d0a4572cf70a9f1fe3a4e0ab8da1b924...0ca9cbbf4623b599a6c3ed4fc8a922942705d9f1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=CodSpeedHQ/action&package-manager=github_actions&previous-version=5.0.1&new-version=5.0.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e43156db234e200d606eeefbf6e2b20a0abaae1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e43156db234e200d606eeefbf6e2b20a0abaae1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc75KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhagQAEPJtKWdKtoz7umF0r9CPGlg\nMsjFiKerFJY/bIdxwbsYBu9PrNopM5mcIuJOeNMcGcpLfHkpYOnXxbu6qbvNS76G\nJtkBjHKTlE1bCoXWZO0USLxZow62jxVYLAxiZmEvQQGPNvUQPUrtfyqrg7wMaVD5\nxIHDETB5kbdLLhmQrsg3w6q6cDjxV6GXIZQNauSKWyZG4B395pLUx7n1O+CTUir/\nT9GHg3QpiEV6zgK0DsMCgwYaVQy0Dhy7PFJxPty7DPGEnRVmuTJZCnL3aDayOG7C\nGbg7HlAXW8ld6JPez8nmx4ALAd5pjs5KB/Qu/uyXt9io3VCFXP7gstamylJJBFau\nwCfn1VLjgqJVDs/CEPoObiPyUuRXBH4FR3wb1N5+nS2m0E999Am1uTTTVf4bCJ+o\net4uSn8EFQQAsBIH20m8VehVl8BAafJ+Sojfp6Rhex/JWSAZbM3Qp+myBe/Png1S\nttVvwOtDGFL0B58swH93rLIW8gfMCUHzl+Xj/RtcjI/EU2Jf6i1ajmkHiBj+/ON8\nmf4w3F3bFK84vx7yfsse2ybR8XbCnHNPQGPcr1QaVu05xz6CUKHeKHxWnOls9J5B\nkuiypOwIwJFTvhox+do7PLFpeWza1+ufDyjzzCAgnpj5f9ldyiOaiOcFc3KrRmWs\niK0Oww+IR+QeHsi26k36\n=79lq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e43156db234e200d606eeefbf6e2b20a0abaae1d\nparent 4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785970250 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785970250 -04