ulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-05T22:50:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43d6bd4a1a673c79d18a80ef4627cb52336db8c4/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf"}]},{"sha":"4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRiZWQ2MzJlODBkNmU0MjdmZDRkNTRmZTBiMTE0Nzg1MmQzYmZmYWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-05T22:40:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T22:40:12Z"},"message":"chore(infra): bump genai-prices daily via scheduled workflow (#5324)\n\nAdds `bump_genai_prices.yml`, a scheduled workflow that bumps\n`genai-prices` in `libs/code/uv.lock` daily, and drops `genai-prices`\nfrom the monthly Dependabot uv sweep so the two do not race the same\nlock entry.\n\n---\n\ndcode fetches the genai-prices catalog at runtime on an hourly timer, so\nnew *pricing data* already reaches users without a package bump. What\nthe pinned package governs is the code that parses that catalog: when\nupstream evolves the data schema, an outdated pin can fail to read a\nfreshly fetched snapshot. A monthly cadence leaves that window open for\nweeks.\n\nDependabot cannot express \"one dependency daily, the rest monthly\"\nwithin a single directory — GitHub rejects config where two blocks for\nthe same ecosystem and target branch cover the same directory, and\n`allow`/`ignore` filters do not exempt that rule. Hence a workflow,\nmodeled on `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`.\n\nEach run locks first and compares the pin on both sides, rather than\nasking PyPI what is newest. That lets uv apply the `>=0.1.1,<0.2.0`\nceiling, yanks and pre-releases itself, so a release we could never\nadopt reads as not-stale instead of failing the job daily; and the\npost-lock read is what the PR title, body and commit message quote, so\nthey cannot name a version the lockfile does not contain. Only `uv.lock`\nmoves — widening the bound for a `0.2.0` release stays a manual step.\n\nPRs are opened with the Org Membership App token so required checks run,\nand titled `chore(deps):` so release-please does not fan out a\n`release(deepagents-code)` PR.\n\nBehavior when a bump PR is already open:\n\n- Branch already at the resolved version → nothing is pushed. `main`\nkeeps the old pin while a PR is open, so an unguarded run would\nforce-push daily and re-run CI on an unchanged tree.\n- Newer version available → the branch is force-pushed and the PR is\nretitled to match, rather than a second PR being stacked.\n- Branch tip authored by someone other than the bot → the run warns and\nexits, so a hand-applied compatibility fix is not discarded.\n- Branch exists with the right content but no PR (a prior run died\nbefore `gh pr create`) → the branch is reused and the PR opened.\n\nFailures file a deduplicated tracking issue. Nothing else watches this\nworkflow, so a break would otherwise just look like the bump quietly\nceasing.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- YAML parses; every `run` step passes `bash -n` and the `github-script`\nbody passes `node --check`.\n- Ran the version-resolution step against the real lockfile on both\npaths: `0.1.1 → 0.1.1` not-stale (correct — 0.1.1 is the newest on\nPyPI), and a genuine `0.1.0 → 0.1.1` stale via a temporary pin.\n`libs/code` restored clean afterward.\n- Ran the push step verbatim (extracted from the parsed YAML) against a\nscratch remote with a stubbed `gh`, covering: fresh branch, force-push\nrefresh, no-churn skip, orphan-branch reuse, fork-PR isolation, and\nrefusal to clobber a human-authored tip.\n- Confirmed in a scratch repo that bare `--force-with-lease` to a URL is\nrejected as `stale info`, that the explicit-sha form used here succeeds,\nand that it still rejects when the expected sha is genuinely stale.\n- Exercised the lockfile-parsing error paths (missing `[[package]]`\ntable, dependency absent, duplicate entries) and the version-validation\nregex.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"aeb8c80c25cf56d794832b0d88d2e9d49c88f2a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aeb8c80c25cf56d794832b0d88d2e9d49c88f2a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc7vNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACtQQAFFYdAvMRlxNi0vuq/faC5bp\nCCxOiH6UGMJ4sOs7WPUm6ChBymmU0CfHX5Vxl17LtjKwrz3lP1hOPmkQ8uZSOKQQ\nFTIxRCisemfKs0TT89PsOV/RENBVOsWc1zBISW7yk9mwUmb4zXiNjjgqPpPbPiF6\n2tYgWtr5/ubbeSBc7nBhlR/obS3WZoZmfbNIsWqAHR6GujKvoiPJ0gmrmM5jSflU\n1CgzGizSn1yLtkI1dLGVHMPonDjVvGbiGZD5dX/8tsH5UFhrzBFZZCs1l1wfqqNa\n6KpzRFFAfPK0JVrw2MbPsnTee5ahx2V5SbCazlcAEdRau4MSCFRK/aiv8ZwU8U5+\nM3lldaN9HTpcNm7s626gysZONmXJc5QFly9Yk0MjPHk/1JZgLJDGQKparEiubKko\nuR8zzVK5nV0a9/3Qsd1T6wdoV0RVO9UWmWGgmoSF1kQBz3szMDb/NxQJj/gK89fe\nClYIWKFUxY+k93oSVVVYU6/SIPb0TTO7zJbWZA89zIjX5QJjl9i4UXlFZT+Iq+26\nIhuHmCyx/zsVeEqSMgNhlYFUK67X0r+1AQuxdPf+mVESodljy539y+KxYMmBZxuY\n9T2muh08cn+aBTrb/j7xnx9pejQ/02dgj7jHMxOk5aRI6xSrB2rO6AwWSossEyoX\n8jT0G/An20TJbRcha0IU\n=l0GM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aeb8c80c25cf56d794832b0d88d2e9d49c88f2a1\nparent 8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785969612 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785969612 -0400\n\nchore(infra): bump genai-prices daily via scheduled workflow (#5324)\n\nAdds `bump_genai_prices.yml`, a scheduled workflow that bumps\n`genai-prices` in `libs/code/uv.lock` daily, and drops `genai-prices`\nfrom the monthly Dependabot uv sweep so the two do not race the same\nlock entry.\n\n---\n\ndcode fetches the genai-prices catalog at runtime on an hourly timer, so\nnew *pricing data* already reaches users without a package bump. What\nthe pinned package governs is the code that parses that catalog: when\nupstream evolves the data schema, an outdated pin can fail to read a\nfreshly fetched snapshot. A monthly cadence leaves that window open for\nweeks.\n\nDependabot cannot express \"one dependency daily, the rest monthly\"\nwithin a single directory — GitHub rejects config where two blocks for\nthe same ecosystem and target branch cover the same directory, and\n`allow`/`ignore` filters do not exempt that rule. Hence a workflow,\nmodeled on `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`.\n\nEach run locks first and compares the pin on both sides, rather than\nasking PyPI what is newest. That lets uv apply the `>=0.1.1,<0.2.0`\nceiling, yanks and pre-releases itself, so a release we could never\nadopt reads as not-stale instead of failing the job daily; and the\npost-lock read is what the PR title, body and commit message quote, so\nthey cannot name a version the lockfile does not contain. Only `uv.lock`\nmoves — widening the bound for a `0.2.0` release stays a manual step.\n\nPRs are opened with the Org Membership App token so required checks run,\nand titled `chore(deps):` so release-please does not fan out a\n`release(deepagents-code)` PR.\n\nBehavior when a bump PR is already open:\n\n- Branch already at the resolved version → nothing is pushed. `main`\nkeeps the old pin while a PR is open, so an unguarded run would\nforce-push daily and re-run CI on an unchanged tree.\n- Newer version available → the branch is force-pushed and the PR is\nretitled to match, rather than a second PR being stacked.\n- Branch tip authored by someone other than the bot → the run warns and\nexits, so a hand-applied compatibility fix is not discarded.\n- Branch exists with the right content but no PR (a prior run died\nbefore `gh pr create`) → the branch is reused and the PR opened.\n\nFailures file a deduplicated tracking issue. Nothing else watches this\nworkflow, so a break would otherwise just look like the bump quietly\nceasing.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- YAML parses; every `run` step passes `bash -n` and the `github-script`\nbody passes `node --check`.\n- Ran the version-resolution step against the real lockfile on both\npaths: `0.1.1 → 0.1.1` not-stale (correct — 0.1.1 is the newest on\nPyPI), and a genuine `0.1.0 → 0.1.1` stale via a temporary pin.\n`libs/code` restored clean afterward.\n- Ran the push step verbatim (extracted from the parsed YAML) against a\nscratch remote with a stubbed `gh`, covering: fresh branch, force-push\nrefresh, no-churn skip, orphan-branch reuse, fork-PR isolation, and\nrefusal to clobber a human-authored tip.\n- Confirmed in a scratch repo that bare `--force-with-lease` to a URL is\nrejected as `stale info`, that the explicit-sha form used here succeeds,\nand that it still rejects when the expected sha is genuinely stale.\n- Exercised the lockfile-parsing error paths (missing `[[package]]`\ntable, dependency absent, duplicate entries) and the version-validation\nregex.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-05T22:40:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4bed632e80d6e427fd4d54fe0b1147852d3bffaf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c"}]},{"sha":"8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhkM2ExYTkyOWY3NTY5NjMwMDYwYWI2ODg2MmIyYTIxYzM4MmQ1OGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-05T22:24:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T22:24:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): `dcode_term_program` trace metadata (#5329)\n\ndcode traces now record the host terminal as `dcode_term_program` (from\n`TERM_PROGRAM`, e.g. \"iTerm.app\", \"vscode\", \"Apple_Terminal\"), making\nruns groupable and filterable by launch environment in LangSmith.\n\n---\n\nThis is a diagnostic key stamped by `build_stream_config` alongside the\nexisting `dcode_experimental` and `dcode_auto_approve` flags — not part\nof the `coding-agent-v1` contract, so it deliberately lives outside\n`build_coding_agent_metadata` and is omitted when `TERM_PROGRAM` is\nunset.","tree":{"sha":"66bfe1186be2ef9ec0e8965a7dd31f197fa06814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/66bfe1186be2ef9ec0e8965a7dd31f197fa06814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc7gqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIPwQACF0bm1bbdNgKkPs4DQxpNjO\nrd+PJklasWbmLlQN+mZGs718bjSqtvaD3q66H3cuc8ihGfMjXQIsTbNrcBUf0j9C\ntD9be199xlIO7gou9/zPjAoPK3NMPeyCOa7j1jDzNRxM/hsnNm9t7C6n+IcG1U1g\nS+TvLNKBzmcFduAU6xgwpVrzfes//StEJ1iT73zL7bnITSfaGf5GOf9Db7rNb2qT\njHy+HaI3OeJXPN5ofq83IH6nQ2bCxayDbpXkN/mfy0s/Bghb4zzABRjshixn+2Wj\nmbGTy8k6ahOh1+uD8vGNMDaZV9rTHyXJn0cA0CwQTfT4fJu57RpQJUMivqfBcpj3\nKpM2wnfQymg+eDyEh9WCimUwvtAvADlXfX/L/WGDaRZ57UhHgRkmrMa4wEOztI3D\nL78yqyyA9GrgqNyGVm5EawzlT1TaeNH2Vv/7+ZJQa9N8flENxZOKL1yhWoCFrJKs\n7RPSz9v0RqlSrRy5KYtDuqhZjtkchNQZ/rriK4hY8VNui2xFkY42YnZJ4rmq22ne\ns4ONSFbBJD3OhSO7UDMB7bGR6bJVBhdfh0pFlj6PP1LOVuMjpYaONhqIhvtJdJhd\np2deH4JpvqKPAmOYycYrSfhM9P6FeXSb2OT4fMH1x+gRkhfd5+h4nB/zapduUpCb\nT/hkS0w2cebNpoSpfvJq\n=qHiU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 66bfe1186be2ef9ec0e8965a7dd31f197fa06814\nparent af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785968681 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785968681 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `dcode_term_program` trace metadata (#5329)\n\ndcode traces now record the host terminal as `dcode_term_program` (from\n`TERM_PROGRAM`, e.g. \"iTerm.app\", \"vscode\", \"Apple_Terminal\"), making\nruns groupable and filterable by launch environment in LangSmith.\n\n---\n\nThis is a diagnostic key stamped by `build_stream_config` alongside the\nexisting `dcode_experimental` and `dcode_auto_approve` flags — not part\nof the `coding-agent-v1` contract, so it deliberately lives outside\n`build_coding_agent_metadata` and is omitted when `TERM_PROGRAM` is\nunset.","verified_at":"2026-08-05T22:24:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d3a1a929f7569630060ab68862b2a21c382d58c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440"}]},{"sha":"af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFmNThhZjJjYzQzNmU2Zjc3NDMzY2Q3NDQzNTMxNTNlZWNmYjQ0NDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shrikar Seshadri","email":"146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-05T21:09:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-05T21:09:04Z"},"message":"feat(evals): add DRBench as a `research` eval category (#5320)\n\nAdds ServiceNow's [DRBench](https://github.com/ServiceNow/drbench) as a\n`research` category in `unified_evals.yml`: enterprise deep-research\ntasks whose documents are served by a containerized app stack\n(Nextcloud, Mattermost, Roundcube IMAP, filebrowser), with the agent's\nreport graded by upstream's own metric suite.\n\n**Full walkthrough of how the benchmark and its grading work:**\n[DRBench: Architecture, Grading and\nResults](https://app.notion.com/p/DRBench-Architecture-Grading-and-Results-3b3808527b178101a3a6c43c5eb28872?source=copy_link)\n\n## What's here:\n- **100 Harbor task directories**: **not committed** — generated by\n`make dataset` from upstream's configs at the pinned commit\n`UPSTREAM_SHA`, with a blobless sparse checkout that takes ~2.4 MiB of\nconfig JSON and skips the ~69 MiB document corpus (app mode's per-task\nimage serves the documents). A git commit hash is a hash of its content,\nso the fetch is pinned as firmly as a copy would be, without carrying\n1,105 generated and vendored files — including 100 gold\n`solution/solve.sh` answer keys — in a public repo. A `drbench-dataset`\nCI job builds the dataset twice and diffs, since the generated tree is\nno longer reviewable in a diff.\n- **App mode, arm64 only** — upstream publishes the task images for\narm64, so `research` needs `sandbox_env: docker` with `runner_label:\nubuntu-24.04-arm`. It pins these itself, so no other input needs\nchanging to include it.\n- **Task profiles**: `lite` is upstream's own 15-task MinEval subset;\n`full` is a 30-task set matching the benchmark's easy/medium/hard\nproportions (representative, *not* comparable to the paper's\nFullBenchmark number).\n- **Per-suite configurability in `unified_evals.yml`**: sandbox\nenvironment (local Docker vs. LangSmith Sandboxes), runner CPU\narchitecture, and concurrency, each overridable per category (`research`\ndefaults to concurrency=1).\n\n## ⚠️ The default category set changes\n`categories` defaults from `autonomous,conversation,context` to\n**`autonomous,conversation,research`**. This is deliberate — `research`\nreplaces `context` rather than being added, to keep the default\ndispatch's cost and wall-clock roughly flat — but it means **the default\nscorecard no longer measures Context-Bench, and its trend line breaks at\nthis commit**. `context` still runs when named explicitly (`categories:\nautonomous,conversation,context,research` runs all four). Whoever owns\nthe nightly baseline should confirm this before merge.\n\n## Grading\nThe DRBench judge is a separate input. Upstream routes on the model\nname, so its verifier drives only `gpt-4o` / `gpt-4o-mini` directly;\nanything else must be a single `openrouter/<vendor>/<model>` slug. The\ndefault is `gpt-4o`. A suite-wide `judge_models` that DRBench cannot\ndrive does **not** fail the research leaf — it falls back to `gpt-4o`\nand says so in the step summary — so the ordinary independent-grader\nflow still works on a mixed dispatch. Use `research_judge_models` to pin\nDRBench's grader deliberately. Any grader other than `gpt-4o` makes the\nnumbers incomparable to earlier runs and to the paper, so re-baseline\nrather than reading a delta.\n\nBecause `research` is scored on a graded reward, its `pass@K` is 0.000\nby construction. The radar chart plots `avg@K` for such categories, and\nthe cross-model ranking is on macro `avg@K` — on a `pass@K` ranking, a\nrow whose research leaf succeeded was averaged against that structural 0\nwhile a row whose leaf failed was averaged without it, so failing\nresearch paid better than completing it.\n\n## Example runs\n-\n[30960340040](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30960340040)\n— full `research` suite\n-\n[30985445289](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30985445289)\n— `lite` suite (autonomous + conversation + research)\n-\n[31033935295](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31033935295)\n— DR0001 + DR0002 with no task files in the repo: avg@1 0.520, 0 errored","tree":{"sha":"51c5bfc6c45fa1a10b5b92569c41d0957714e029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/51c5bfc6c45fa1a10b5b92569c41d0957714e029"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc6ZwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcU8QABHWskWCDn2wj0iWwgOQWuME\n2HnukrwtaVcYFW4qFMf3JDXUph/A4u90IrJCAHNOXQLTJ6a/FZ+giJ93Y3MesnMh\nocH+vE0wWMd5P57RLdMuaF3tm5LQuY+bfKEIuLTlfmmrsh2nYxgnyQ+WL+Zq8Oz6\nUsul/gAMP+2yt9jDqnevC+9MZKl8/3u25efKH8eNzFX8KENbkJn4mOAod5IMw3Y+\nQD6tWdjzL4HRsnbhgSrPTn9a/DdlBbRIEaFaf+0iUXyCSZfXdQUTNyvkW3biGtO+\n4OxrjvaidTsepx9iaGXOChfBoC0veOwquL+9ByjN/PEDxPzK/ONXwA7NofnHWtMo\n1SMdS5YcJr+T1wgtsNf3RwNf8F3W/iaDkKT+cutqEwf6qHjBHs+uylmpnw3EmgNY\n03OzX2OoK+xDZTlhID9BPA9DkBLl3x05CrtuGw750AC3UBsu4BwN9L7RTTQTUks8\nh+zeV1ES3Jp3+BlrpCMDUiYILGzUbNMxOsggJsqZyfcLAfP1PbRd4PFGkjx3w2to\n7aoOHLvsM6VISYCgN5D03NYOJYfVK2J6I6ivp+80t5BKTnZqLR7CJx/dwp/jF3AZ\nNwQ6HSWrwugar4TL5EzlPxN160JbBlHTIQDgfzWEEQw1rb/gZ+QFFtUGZzmH0fTY\nsLnDn0bJCVFkoddkf6Bq\n=CRXL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 51c5bfc6c45fa1a10b5b92569c41d0957714e029\nparent a6e2608c382be362163e4f26f5ccc544cc13ccbd\nauthor Shrikar Seshadri <146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com> 1785964144 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785964144 -0700\n\nfeat(evals): add DRBench as a `research` eval category (#5320)\n\nAdds ServiceNow's [DRBench](https://github.com/ServiceNow/drbench) as a\n`research` category in `unified_evals.yml`: enterprise deep-research\ntasks whose documents are served by a containerized app stack\n(Nextcloud, Mattermost, Roundcube IMAP, filebrowser), with the agent's\nreport graded by upstream's own metric suite.\n\n**Full walkthrough of how the benchmark and its grading work:**\n[DRBench: Architecture, Grading and\nResults](https://app.notion.com/p/DRBench-Architecture-Grading-and-Results-3b3808527b178101a3a6c43c5eb28872?source=copy_link)\n\n## What's here:\n- **100 Harbor task directories**: **not committed** — generated by\n`make dataset` from upstream's configs at the pinned commit\n`UPSTREAM_SHA`, with a blobless sparse checkout that takes ~2.4 MiB of\nconfig JSON and skips the ~69 MiB document corpus (app mode's per-task\nimage serves the documents). A git commit hash is a hash of its content,\nso the fetch is pinned as firmly as a copy would be, without carrying\n1,105 generated and vendored files — including 100 gold\n`solution/solve.sh` answer keys — in a public repo. A `drbench-dataset`\nCI job builds the dataset twice and diffs, since the generated tree is\nno longer reviewable in a diff.\n- **App mode, arm64 only** — upstream publishes the task images for\narm64, so `research` needs `sandbox_env: docker` with `runner_label:\nubuntu-24.04-arm`. It pins these itself, so no other input needs\nchanging to include it.\n- **Task profiles**: `lite` is upstream's own 15-task MinEval subset;\n`full` is a 30-task set matching the benchmark's easy/medium/hard\nproportions (representative, *not* comparable to the paper's\nFullBenchmark number).\n- **Per-suite configurability in `unified_evals.yml`**: sandbox\nenvironment (local Docker vs. LangSmith Sandboxes), runner CPU\narchitecture, and concurrency, each overridable per category (`research`\ndefaults to concurrency=1).\n\n## ⚠️ The default category set changes\n`categories` defaults from `autonomous,conversation,context` to\n**`autonomous,conversation,research`**. This is deliberate — `research`\nreplaces `context` rather than being added, to keep the default\ndispatch's cost and wall-clock roughly flat — but it means **the default\nscorecard no longer measures Context-Bench, and its trend line breaks at\nthis commit**. `context` still runs when named explicitly (`categories:\nautonomous,conversation,context,research` runs all four). Whoever owns\nthe nightly baseline should confirm this before merge.\n\n## Grading\nThe DRBench judge is a separate input. Upstream routes on the model\nname, so its verifier drives only `gpt-4o` / `gpt-4o-mini` directly;\nanything else must be a single `openrouter/<vendor>/<model>` slug. The\ndefault is `gpt-4o`. A suite-wide `judge_models` that DRBench cannot\ndrive does **not** fail the research leaf — it falls back to `gpt-4o`\nand says so in the step summary — so the ordinary independent-grader\nflow still works on a mixed dispatch. Use `research_judge_models` to pin\nDRBench's grader deliberately. Any grader other than `gpt-4o` makes the\nnumbers incomparable to earlier runs and to the paper, so re-baseline\nrather than reading a delta.\n\nBecause `research` is scored on a graded reward, its `pass@K` is 0.000\nby construction. The radar chart plots `avg@K` for such categories, and\nthe cross-model ranking is on macro `avg@K` — on a `pass@K` ranking, a\nrow whose research leaf succeeded was averaged against that structural 0\nwhile a row whose leaf failed was averaged without it, so failing\nresearch paid better than completing it.\n\n## Example runs\n-\n[30960340040](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30960340040)\n— full `research` suite\n-\n[30985445289](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30985445289)\n— `lite` suite (autonomous + conversation + research)\n-\n[31033935295](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31033935295)\n— DR0001 + DR0002 with no task files in the repo: avg@1 0.520, 0 errored","verified_at":"2026-08-05T21:09:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/af58af2cc436e6f77433cd744353153eecfb4440/comments","author":{"login":"davibinboi","id":146694785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL5igQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146694785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi","html_url":"https://github.com/davibinboi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/gists{/gist