bb2ccd7ed7e4a702e893ac09b6b8f28df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c1f4ac3d53b3231d80be97691763850d230e8080","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcmJFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi5sQAHTmiRq/PV6UH10N0CxX0+04\ncJEC30PazA4gzrsH/FPcRLSallnFVXlq716zvLzuA7nBACIIdGq238+dtmaoKSIT\nuEGqQX9dZmuE3IGE1oj+CC4g+EGWCePDdYJlZWIvSAeoCwEVphZTPp7ycNRfes/b\nYW2xY4+SUspHRe/uXdsEmMF5GFIKG0lAPINoAK0QSNxL06AZoRaIUaBzOyTuTqp0\nUQ3WZk6+ZNjVlMqOtuNdWbGBp/U4ryrhm/huYHUJa+9MgI3cP7bfgnQQNWLjvmh9\nBV7pvvEvr9Yviuu5ei7otL5Ipp4IAof1WyCp2dtLT3H1uZmM+sjaMrDG+L/u4V8O\n8tlEfZ6fDHqTYwiDh2bYWUWWuOk5tZnz7QOQ6TvEouJVoiYok72RKPc50zbFChVc\nsG8bVHeofl1yjgMCAHfAJt1eNNro8tlrm8Kxso+73pns1q5yhrwwZTXSvr6UTI2O\nyPHLBLMq61mZeuZK5BZawFO//lxLrJ/8KQi3J3tiS1cz02qxO+tfWs/1lICGHUo7\nL3dCmlCK+a7iG89c1k85bN0VrSj5lRiPz6VQWBK2TnSLcn2KJ7KzHfwjycSRRlR5\nN8ktxtrh1nk+jWpS8SfqBFWKVZ1WS2b63UWpgqm9jQypDFR1fMrM5T2FiIllankZ\nqp+gnOTwZe3wfjg4k/aT\n=dHZ4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0561df5bb2ccd7ed7e4a702e893ac09b6b8f28df\nparent f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785881157 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785881157 -0700\n\nfix(code): route failures to `PostToolUseFailure` (#5315)\n\nSupersedes #5255\n\nFailed tool calls now fire `PostToolUseFailure`; `PostToolUse` remains\nsuccess-only.\n\n---\n\nUses `artifact.exit_code` from `deepagents==0.7.4` for shell failures.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T22:06:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1f4ac3d53b3231d80be97691763850d230e8080","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c1f4ac3d53b3231d80be97691763850d230e8080","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c1f4ac3d53b3231d80be97691763850d230e8080/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3"}]},{"sha":"f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYzNGZmYTBjYjhjMGM3OTQzYjExNmE3NTM1MzVkZjQ3ZTMyZGUyYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T20:02:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T20:02:33Z"},"message":"feat(code): add Baseten built-in pricing overrides (#5312)\n\nBaseten model cost estimates now fall back to a built-in pricing catalog\ninstead of showing `$0`. All 12 Baseten Model APIs models are priced at\ntheir published input / cached-input / output rates.\n\n---\n\n[Baseten Model\nAPIs](https://docs.baseten.co/inference/model-apis/overview#supported-models)\nshipped models that genai-prices does not yet cover, so `estimate_cost`\nreturned `None` for them and those requests dropped out of the session\ntotal. This adds a `baseten` provider block to `bundled_prices.json`\n(#5304's fallback-on-miss override), priced from the [Baseten pricing\npage](https://www.baseten.co/pricing).\n\nThis is a stopgap. Every entry carries `price_comments: \"Stopgap pending\npydantic/genai-prices#549\"` per the `bundled_prices.README.md` policy,\nenforced by\n`test_every_bundled_override_entry_is_priced_and_links_upstream`. The\nupstream addition is open at pydantic/genai-prices#549; once that merges\nand the hourly auto-update picks it up, these entries go inert\nautomatically (upstream always wins on a primary-catalog hit) and can be\nremoved as housekeeping.\n\nRates per 1M tokens (input / cached input / output):\n\n| Model | Slug | Input | Cache | Output |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| DeepSeek V4 Pro | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro` | 1.74 | 0.145 | 3.48\n|\n| DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731 | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731` | 0.13 |\n0.028 | 0.26 |\n| GLM 4.7 | `zai-org/GLM-4.7` | 0.60 | 0.12 | 2.20 |\n| GLM 5.2 | `zai-org/GLM-5.2` | 1.40 | 0.14 | 4.40 |\n| GLM 5.2 Fast | `zai-org/GLM-5.2-Fast` | 2.10 | 0.21 | 6.60 |\n| Inkling | `thinkingmachines/inkling` | 1.00 | 0.17 | 4.05 |\n| Inkling Small | `thinkingmachines/inkling-small` | 0.50 | 0.10 | 1.20\n|\n| Kimi K2.6 | `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6` | 0.95 | 0.16 | 4.00 |\n| Kimi K2.7 Code | `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.7-Code` | 0.95 | 0.16 | 4.00 |\n| Kimi K3 | `moonshotai/Kimi-K3` | 3.00 | 0.30 | 15.00 |\n| NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra | `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Ultra-550B-A55B` |\n0.60 | 0.12 | 2.40 |\n| OpenAI GPT 120B | `openai/gpt-oss-120b` | 0.10 | — | 0.50 |\n\nNotes:\n\n- Cached input uses `cache_read_mtok`, matching Baseten's \"Cache Input\"\nKV-cache rate (applied automatically to every request).\n- `openai/gpt-oss-120b` publishes no separate cached-input rate, so\n`cache_read_mtok` is omitted — cached tokens stay in the ordinary input\ntotal.\n- Extra `match` aliases cover the bare slugs Baseten's pricing \"Try\"\nlinks use: `glm-4-7`, `inkling`, `inkling-small`.","tree":{"sha":"55db25175c82a264ff77b3a8a1442f1525f09aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/55db25175c82a264ff77b3a8a1442f1525f09aaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqckVZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8F4QAFOZeiiENP9tDu9W5tm5Eauk\ne6KVWvQDu8R2t+UNg4TLX7fQFrd1lRl+BYW/FerlXYpJFcHMNZcagtQ24PjMMHml\nBNhhE8/3QfBNTdGm+V3361XD0vqXzji7M4QYyxuErfMrVInvz9uQE/adehFLuFN3\nVOm6reVoBa7r6wAsO8iDYp8xLQ2xg7j0NvM/ibfFDX2u5ihIZkwE16pJV4jvIhdf\nTGUC/tgjEXlLzMTgFy6il6HxdLs7ukpAcEuSQysz07ruaHHTswF+wBk/p1tScv02\nNLXfxCnRCMofQfnrtxj3eSkZcSANWM7K0IWWsVk1nrSHAge2GYYsZ3+Fo3zQw+KR\n/pX1lAxjMFtQ0S+QVv+kXYa4EMjE/33AkZn4gZ0mAdH8iXqeBSU5eWrwP9yKH11S\nsGIdn5DK0vrndZU0ZhGhgKmCmw4wp9PfyqUgMUYNnB7MZQkTwqinGMgKZqSFYFxw\n5zbAD4HKj1zKiN9HmPlJgQZXJZzcw5LR8qkA+n48xWvqpvufCxDnFEPHsF4vMwOo\nhnkgdPxhs1ftO6POJwVEm3uqs/ff61Qe7OL07aSDhuGlALnYMOL0bh9TVQ48OrfK\nxo2aKRFfpTPSGQigS3+jtNuJrGCqkch8KRneh7tR5fSp3o3hoTtjW3Qp658TS2F+\nnml7kCVsE0HTaf+cPnNQ\n=OnP9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 55db25175c82a264ff77b3a8a1442f1525f09aaa\nparent dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785873753 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785873753 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add Baseten built-in pricing overrides (#5312)\n\nBaseten model cost estimates now fall back to a built-in pricing catalog\ninstead of showing `$0`. All 12 Baseten Model APIs models are priced at\ntheir published input / cached-input / output rates.\n\n---\n\n[Baseten Model\nAPIs](https://docs.baseten.co/inference/model-apis/overview#supported-models)\nshipped models that genai-prices does not yet cover, so `estimate_cost`\nreturned `None` for them and those requests dropped out of the session\ntotal. This adds a `baseten` provider block to `bundled_prices.json`\n(#5304's fallback-on-miss override), priced from the [Baseten pricing\npage](https://www.baseten.co/pricing).\n\nThis is a stopgap. Every entry carries `price_comments: \"Stopgap pending\npydantic/genai-prices#549\"` per the `bundled_prices.README.md` policy,\nenforced by\n`test_every_bundled_override_entry_is_priced_and_links_upstream`. The\nupstream addition is open at pydantic/genai-prices#549; once that merges\nand the hourly auto-update picks it up, these entries go inert\nautomatically (upstream always wins on a primary-catalog hit) and can be\nremoved as housekeeping.\n\nRates per 1M tokens (input / cached input / output):\n\n| Model | Slug | Input | Cache | Output |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| DeepSeek V4 Pro | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro` | 1.74 | 0.145 | 3.48\n|\n| DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731 | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731` | 0.13 |\n0.028 | 0.26 |\n| GLM 4.7 | `zai-org/GLM-4.7` | 0.60 | 0.12 | 2.20 |\n| GLM 5.2 | `zai-org/GLM-5.2` | 1.40 | 0.14 | 4.40 |\n| GLM 5.2 Fast | `zai-org/GLM-5.2-Fast` | 2.10 | 0.21 | 6.60 |\n| Inkling | `thinkingmachines/inkling` | 1.00 | 0.17 | 4.05 |\n| Inkling Small | `thinkingmachines/inkling-small` | 0.50 | 0.10 | 1.20\n|\n| Kimi K2.6 | `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6` | 0.95 | 0.16 | 4.00 |\n| Kimi K2.7 Code | `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.7-Code` | 0.95 | 0.16 | 4.00 |\n| Kimi K3 | `moonshotai/Kimi-K3` | 3.00 | 0.30 | 15.00 |\n| NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra | `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Ultra-550B-A55B` |\n0.60 | 0.12 | 2.40 |\n| OpenAI GPT 120B | `openai/gpt-oss-120b` | 0.10 | — | 0.50 |\n\nNotes:\n\n- Cached input uses `cache_read_mtok`, matching Baseten's \"Cache Input\"\nKV-cache rate (applied automatically to every request).\n- `openai/gpt-oss-120b` publishes no separate cached-input rate, so\n`cache_read_mtok` is omitted — cached tokens stay in the ordinary input\ntotal.\n- Extra `match` aliases cover the bare slugs Baseten's pricing \"Try\"\nlinks use: `glm-4-7`, `inkling`, `inkling-small`.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T20:02:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f34ffa0cb8c0c7943b116a753535df47e32de2a3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac"}]},{"sha":"dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRiZTM5NDEzM2ZkMTJkMDgwMTVhOTY5OTMxMzdmYzRlN2ZhOTAzYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T19:41:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T19:41:50Z"},"message":"docs(evals): update unified-evals README for pinned Harbor 0.20.0 (#5306)\n\nDrops the stale `harbor_package_override` requirement (pinned Harbor\n0.20.0 / harbor-langsmith 0.3.0 forwards MCP servers, so every category\nruns out of the box) and adds `gh workflow run` + local `harbor run`\nsnippets, including single-task runs and the LLM-judge verifier env.\nDocs-only.","tree":{"sha":"4418cc51e771ec88f8546e20df620bdb1f5b5a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4418cc51e771ec88f8546e20df620bdb1f5b5a3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqckB+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAlAQAKGSbIZc6UGhtjQwTiqOvF5l\nyqjLWzdpGwgwd36IdqS6zwmx1y6pvJTvm5XrPAoiTzjDMLStN3vNGYXPzmGBnRbW\neQxIi9ggpv7sJUkgqOsl21aGQrvpG41Jd3R1GzD1iD9AKjrVi+N6x7g8I3fpIZIj\nESQ1OH7zGEgukmTQdfOTFlAeBiRU8fBS01/7ZOVyZGi1mwKj1CapTRG8EHVAbqjf\nCAflvKNnXq/E/4XvFNgLESL9gJbgeMHKJi1fXVvg5/JuIx5a9apcg1uEuXgTCfTH\nFJH3SkZOLwRILSyLO6G48gbUwFfEEAp1ieSI0j2pdMLAPoLbFhtiH5OaC7SvVd5T\n7lDQZ/WAjgiJFVnuoE6Mx7pcAaf/zJjXMlL8ltW5HnWIdgbnrExYnflnTDl8q0iP\nJq5yssdVzaID5eYdUSsDqMuSPnPyrf66rOWWL4QtRzN4pPeBGOnexio3++44PB/8\neXBbOAVZAntm2bMHDERSzWp5p0yQN0LuCTPdAWw+JnFwl0UOu4M849b1QFz5MEtl\neOOVgfKoNyxZbfLAzwwZBI7AoiWtbG6qfNF5bQHuUHGncwlGdBYQYJLaMZuSYQ8q\nAR1EofjPfLTU+smZV7Gu2fbL2SIpKR4f8qZ1TMwACUAqJSK6IBUU9mYWcuXqx9b1\num+UFbb9QTgzxUQDKJEe\n=/uxv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4418cc51e771ec88f8546e20df620bdb1f5b5a3b\nparent 89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1785872510 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785872510 -0400\n\ndocs(evals): update unified-evals README for pinned Harbor 0.20.0 (#5306)\n\nDrops the stale `harbor_package_override` requirement (pinned Harbor\n0.20.0 / harbor-langsmith 0.3.0 forwards MCP servers, so every category\nruns out of the box) and adds `gh workflow run` + local `harbor run`\nsnippets, including single-task runs and the LLM-judge verifier env.\nDocs-only.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T19:41:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dbe394133fd12d08015a96993137fc4e7fa903ac/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08"}]},{"sha":"89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg5YmNhZjJjMzFhYjM0N2NiNGNiNDU2M2JjMThmMjk2ZGJlY2VhMDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T19:40:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T19:40:14Z"},"message":"feat(code): local pricing overrides as a fallback when genai-prices misses (#5304)\n\nCost estimates now fall back to a local pricing catalog when\ngenai-prices has no rates for a model. Two sources are consulted, in\nprecedence order: a user-supplied `prices.json` in the user config\ndirectory (`~/.deepagents`) for models upstream lacks entirely, and a\nmaintainer-curated `bundled_prices.json` shipped inside the package as a\nstopgap while an upstream addition is pending. The fallback only fires\non a primary-catalog miss, so published upstream rates always win.\n\n---\n\n`estimate_cost` previously returned `None` for any model the\ngenai-prices catalog — bundled or hourly auto-updated (#5264) — did not\ncover, leaving those requests out of the session total with no recourse\nshort of waiting on a genai-prices release. This adds an escape hatch\nwithout giving up upstream as the source of truth.\n\nDesign points:\n\n- **Fallback-on-miss, upstream always wins.** Overrides are consulted\nonly from the existing `except LookupError` path in `estimate_cost`;\nthey are never installed via `set_custom_snapshot`. The hourly\nauto-updater wholesale-replaces the custom snapshot, so anything\ninstalled there would be clobbered every refresh — keeping overrides\noutside the snapshot mechanism is what makes the two features compose. A\nsuccessful primary lookup never touches the overrides, which means a\nbuilt-in entry automatically becomes dead weight the day a released\ngenai-prices ships the model, with no migration needed.\n\n  <details>\n  <summary>Worked examples</summary>\n\n> **Scenario 1 — why overrides can't live in the snapshot.** You start\n`dcode` after upgrading to a release whose `bundled_prices.json` ships a\nstopgap for `new-model-v2`. The updater fetches the upstream catalog in\nthe background and installs it via `set_custom_snapshot`, which replaces\nthe snapshot as a whole rather than merging into it. If the stopgap had\nbeen registered into the snapshot at startup, that first refresh would\nhave deleted it — from then on `new-model-v2` would be priced by neither\ncatalog and silently drop out of the session total, exactly the gap the\nstopgap shipped to close, with no warning and no way for the user to\nrestore it. Because the stopgap lives in the separate override catalog\ninstead, the refresh doesn't touch it: the primary lookup still raises\n`LookupError` for `new-model-v2`, and the fallback prices it as before.\n  >\n> **Scenario 2 — why a stale entry needs no migration.** A week later\nthe hourly fetch picks up an upstream catalog that now prices\n`new-model-v2`. From the next request on, the primary lookup succeeds,\nso the `except LookupError` path — the only place overrides are read —\nis never reached for that model. The stopgap entry is now dead weight:\nit costs nothing at runtime, and its removal is a housekeeping PR, not a\ncorrectness fix. There is no data to migrate, no flag to flip, and no\nversion check, because \"upstream now covers it\" and \"the override is\nunreachable\" are the same event.\n\n  </details>\n- **Same schema as upstream.** Both files use the raw provider-array\nschema of genai-prices' `prices/new_data/v2/data.json`\n- **User file wins on conflict.** On a conflicting `(provider id, model\nid)` pair, the user's `prices.json` entry replaces the built-in one\n(per-model). The user path resolves through the existing\n`model_config.DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR` constant\n- **Never breaks a model turn.** A missing user file is the normal case\nand stays silent. Malformed JSON, a non-array payload, an unreadable\nfile, or a schema validation failure each log a warning once and disable\nonly that source; `pricing_data_available()` and the contract-broken\nguard are untouched, so a bad override file never masquerades as a\nbroken pricing install. Successful override pricing logs at DEBUG —\nthat's the signal to pursue the upstream addition.\n- **Built-in ships empty.** `bundled_prices.json` is a structurally\nvalid empty provider array until the first stopgap is needed. The\nmaintenance policy lives in the sibling `bundled_prices.README.md` (JSON\nhas no comments): every entry must link the upstream genai-prices\nPR/issue, and must be removed once a released genai-prices covers it.","tree":{"sha":"329da9a3fd4d6263727811816b00efb7515cdc4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/329da9a3fd4d6263727811816b00efb7515cdc4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqckAeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMckQADGbcZG2fLvqs7pbY96hAyba\nYXIEie9LLDovWPMmAG+3ML0u4Jg5xlQIQtn0yhfaNNeY2EzlNHSDEABTdX01+u1Y\n5JysuvZXYOOqzC4rDSYsug+T/L4F/rh2XOz+UP+2c+0r+Gw3LEO4E46hKQmTClh3\nIj8zapiaptc6mJDuLKBdp66xjT+B/egu+dEM6kqg2OjRsjhtuDtcYc/EdThBj0hn\nA5OlzYnoKzwFjV2rWJRUhkfQf6lAVazyNR9WpABWoZO06/be1wjMNbt4OpnkztVj\nqxJ+kq/L/dYTPnungk+321EDR0/HOLmsH1fy9kF/H9cOcO/9LShEzwiww2LzyBLL\njTRUA/bSaIsXQpRX9is/rwb+0Q+q/3aonqi5Sljsm30gconMOkhUGe/dhPH3Wtvb\n93dODK2lGNBBcv2m+JwYsNYYh43VAV+RslCtwBXXhWqcFbXZB8ObNdeOMCj1PE38\nR7qS86e0kHyVNb9mCgmXQSmFrp6GhBKq/BbWovtOWYfKIGjy5zVr9CEbJwqY+Qm8\nL6JnDl4wJi/7p06exnRtBny4zE69aB2vk2GupSAEHU+FP7rua36AJ9duSh6//FsV\nhNyZThwtUPJWX3hUYZE9YAJgqCy7LkC3i+xSbyj6uv5DvPI87pW/QuI65xskbeXU\nJGLntH9rTsOTVj2dRUG+\n=mwxy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 329da9a3fd4d6263727811816b00efb7515cdc4f\nparent 994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785872414 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785872414 -0400\n\nfeat(code): local pricing overrides as a fallback when genai-prices misses (#5304)\n\nCost estimates now fall back to a local pricing catalog when\ngenai-prices has no rates for a model. Two sources are consulted, in\nprecedence order: a user-supplied `prices.json` in the user config\ndirectory (`~/.deepagents`) for models upstream lacks entirely, and a\nmaintainer-curated `bundled_prices.json` shipped inside the package as a\nstopgap while an upstream addition is pending. The fallback only fires\non a primary-catalog miss, so published upstream rates always win.\n\n---\n\n`estimate_cost` previously returned `None` for any model the\ngenai-prices catalog — bundled or hourly auto-updated (#5264) — did not\ncover, leaving those requests out of the session total with no recourse\nshort of waiting on a genai-prices release. This adds an escape hatch\nwithout giving up upstream as the source of truth.\n\nDesign points:\n\n- **Fallback-on-miss, upstream always wins.** Overrides are consulted\nonly from the existing `except LookupError` path in `estimate_cost`;\nthey are never installed via `set_custom_snapshot`. The hourly\nauto-updater wholesale-replaces the custom snapshot, so anything\ninstalled there would be clobbered every refresh — keeping overrides\noutside the snapshot mechanism is what makes the two features compose. A\nsuccessful primary lookup never touches the overrides, which means a\nbuilt-in entry automatically becomes dead weight the day a released\ngenai-prices ships the model, with no migration needed.\n\n  <details>\n  <summary>Worked examples</summary>\n\n> **Scenario 1 — why overrides can't live in the snapshot.** You start\n`dcode` after upgrading to a release whose `bundled_prices.json` ships a\nstopgap for `new-model-v2`. The updater fetches the upstream catalog in\nthe background and installs it via `set_custom_snapshot`, which replaces\nthe snapshot as a whole rather than merging into it. If the stopgap had\nbeen registered into the snapshot at startup, that first refresh would\nhave deleted it — from then on `new-model-v2` would be priced by neither\ncatalog and silently drop out of the session total, exactly the gap the\nstopgap shipped to close, with no warning and no way for the user to\nrestore it. Because the stopgap lives in the separate override catalog\ninstead, the refresh doesn't touch it: the primary lookup still raises\n`LookupError` for `new-model-v2`, and the fallback prices it as before.\n  >\n> **Scenario 2 — why a stale entry needs no migration.** A week later\nthe hourly fetch picks up an upstream catalog that now prices\n`new-model-v2`. From the next request on, the primary lookup succeeds,\nso the `except LookupError` path — the only place overrides are read —\nis never reached for that model. The stopgap entry is now dead weight:\nit costs nothing at runtime, and its removal is a housekeeping PR, not a\ncorrectness fix. There is no data to migrate, no flag to flip, and no\nversion check, because \"upstream now covers it\" and \"the override is\nunreachable\" are the same event.\n\n  </details>\n- **Same schema as upstream.** Both files use the raw provider-array\nschema of genai-prices' `prices/new_data/v2/data.json`\n- **User file wins on conflict.** On a conflicting `(provider id, model\nid)` pair, the user's `prices.json` entry replaces the built-in one\n(per-model). The user path resolves through the existing\n`model_config.DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR` constant\n- **Never breaks a model turn.** A missing user file is the normal case\nand stays silent. Malformed JSON, a non-array payload, an unreadable\nfile, or a schema validation failure each log a warning once and disable\nonly that source; `pricing_data_available()` and the contract-broken\nguard are untouched, so a bad override file never masquerades as a\nbroken pricing install. Successful override pricing logs at DEBUG —\nthat's the signal to pursue the upstream addition.\n- **Built-in ships empty.** `bundled_prices.json` is a structurally\nvalid empty provider array until the first stopgap is needed. The\nmaintenance policy lives in the sibling `bundled_prices.README.md` (JSON\nhas no comments): every entry must link the upstream genai-prices\nPR/issue, and must be removed once a released genai-prices covers it.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T19:40:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89bcaf2c31ab347cb4cb4563bc18f296dbecea08/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563"}]},{"sha":"994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5NDc5OWIyZjI1OTUwZWI3NmUxMDg1YjUwMjZkMWYxOWVjZWI1NjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T19:14:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T19:14:08Z"},"message":"fix(code): stop leaking turn coroutines and sqlite handles (#5218)\n\nInterrupting a turn, or exiting while a background thread-cache refresh\nis in flight, no longer strands an unawaited coroutine or an open SQLite\nhandle.\n\n---\n\nThe unit suite emitted three families of warnings, all at teardown. Two\nare ours and are fixed here; the third is upstream and is filtered.\n\n### An unawaited turn coroutine\n\n`_send_to_agent` handed `run_worker` an already-built `_run_agent_task`\ncoroutine. Textual never runs the work of a worker cancelled before its\nfirst event-loop step, so that coroutine was finalized unawaited — a\n`RuntimeWarning`, and (once interpreter teardown had gone far enough to\nbreak the import machinery its cleanup relies on) an unraisable\n`KeyError: '__import__'`. Passing a callable means the coroutine only\nexists if the worker actually runs, so there is nothing to strand.\nSeveral tests were closing that coroutine by hand purely to silence the\nwarning; those workarounds are gone, and a new test pins the callable\ncontract.\n\n**Where it started:** #5196. Handing `run_worker` a coroutine dates all\nthe way back to the original Textual REPL (#686), but it was harmless\nuntil something cancelled a worker before its first step. #5196 added\nthe recovery path for exactly that situation along with the tests that\nexercise it. Its parent commit runs the app test module with zero `never\nawaited` warnings; #5196 itself produces three.\n\n### An unclosed SQLite handle\n\n`aiosqlite` opens the database on its worker thread and hands the raw\n`sqlite3.Connection` back through a future, recording it on the\nconnection only when the awaiting coroutine resumes. A cancel landing\nanywhere in that window left the handle unreachable from the cleanup\nthat follows, so the garbage collector reported `ResourceWarning:\nunclosed database`. There are two halves to the window, and both are now\ncovered:\n\n- Cancelled while the worker is still opening, the library has no handle\nrecorded yet, so the cleanup it queues closes nothing. The session\nmodule now records the handle from the worker thread the moment the\nconnector returns.\n- Cancelled after the handle is delivered but before the coroutine\nresumes, the library clears its own reference before that queued cleanup\ncan run — so it again closes nothing. The guard now also queues an\nexplicit close ahead of the library's cleanup, while the handle is still\nreachable.\n\nBoth closes run on the thread that opened the handle, and closing twice\nis a no-op, so neither disturbs a normal shutdown. `get_checkpointer`\nbuilds its connection through the same helper rather than\n`AsyncSqliteSaver.from_conn_string`, so it gets the same guard.\n\n**Where it started:** #5174. The prewarm that reads the session database\nhas existed since #1481, but it ran once at startup, so it had normally\nfinished before anything cancelled it. #5174 re-fires it after every\nturn, which reliably leaves a session-DB read in flight when a test app\nexits. Counting handles that `aiosqlite` opened and never closed across\nthe goal-command tests: zero on the parent commit, fourteen on #5174.\n\n### A `typing` deprecation from `google-genai`\n\n`google.genai.types` builds a union alias out of\n`typing._UnionGenericAlias`, which CPython 3.14 deprecates, and it fires\nat import before any of this package's code runs. This one is not a\nregression from any change here — `deepagents-code` has been tested on\nthe 3.14 leg since the package was created in #3027, and the warning\nappears wherever a test imports the Google integration. It is tracked\nupstream as\n[googleapis/python-genai#1640](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/1640)\nand still unfixed as of `google-genai` 2.13.0, so it is filtered\nnarrowly (message, category, and module) rather than worked around.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f42590ef-0fe4-0b9f-6880-1c48b28446d5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"94a19e9c012830ca9f571dd2be1cd67293b74d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/94a19e9c012830ca9f571dd2be1cd67293b74d22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcjoACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKv4QAH3+rbr4WlwybSYqCwm7UvTp\nc7MK+G0TKy4swYtPXNwvQstHTa5UEVagB1sT6/mgn2HgiALkZmVGcPcEe4krvsi2\nSwaKaJIfceaXgKymWV9kOWVUonFq3nh14s3kgNq9VwImwila6Kc2CEA/eM8D8QdT\n+/DyLyb2cVtDZJ4yrNMXAJpMP1PqlJUlxAx5pst25oZgShfyNiQfxnXg5aG9bGIV\nZM5KjyiRMeclFqWWtpVLpUSVfx1hvS5szLUC7R3pqa93MD+2LcYIImrbYpPOTFpj\nlxLJO8s1o8737cpwiHWFG/iuDcA0ht7Mn5BCURD07F6mKnkAMwx2ovwx+hd16TIW\nVtJQoJ/GMTREm6sWyUhHcqCKC+WpkEEyRm2C7JjPwF3gAclQ594TKReGr/XxDAvd\nvGsmdkN0HA8SrOoQGZ5MVRnngElcgqbwX8A567jBjRqlih1rc+DeGfyz4Bj9iwcj\nOh8gIHmKJdzgQcEmeUg4U1dOiED6Cu9h8Iz14XgG+5beHnWm0hzIOxka8k9BIHkR\nungGAuCWCG3EghOzu8T1TNUhXqC20ECvNTq081ElU6b61Ge5zAIyuIN7iyYeKorY\nNm4ZXVKES4fuyQgvzBtTkoe3W5H60Tw3kA+f7yaq3flUyeuXh+KOyLC/OnJ/AvZd\nzA3kwtIMDS+hvj5mGIzs\n=xt4y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 94a19e9c012830ca9f571dd2be1cd67293b74d22\nparent b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785870848 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785870848 -0400\n\nfix(code): stop leaking turn coroutines and sqlite handles (#5218)\n\nInterrupting a turn, or exiting while a background thread-cache refresh\nis in flight, no longer strands an unawaited coroutine or an open SQLite\nhandle.\n\n---\n\nThe unit suite emitted three families of warnings, all at teardown. Two\nare ours and are fixed here; the third is upstream and is filtered.\n\n### An unawaited turn coroutine\n\n`_send_to_agent` handed `run_worker` an already-built `_run_agent_task`\ncoroutine. Textual never runs the work of a worker cancelled before its\nfirst event-loop step, so that coroutine was finalized unawaited — a\n`RuntimeWarning`, and (once interpreter teardown had gone far enough to\nbreak the import machinery its cleanup relies on) an unraisable\n`KeyError: '__import__'`. Passing a callable means the coroutine only\nexists if the worker actually runs, so there is nothing to strand.\nSeveral tests were closing that coroutine by hand purely to silence the\nwarning; those workarounds are gone, and a new test pins the callable\ncontract.\n\n**Where it started:** #5196. Handing `run_worker` a coroutine dates all\nthe way back to the original Textual REPL (#686), but it was harmless\nuntil something cancelled a worker before its first step. #5196 added\nthe recovery path for exactly that situation along with the tests that\nexercise it. Its parent commit runs the app test module with zero `never\nawaited` warnings; #5196 itself produces three.\n\n### An unclosed SQLite handle\n\n`aiosqlite` opens the database on its worker thread and hands the raw\n`sqlite3.Connection` back through a future, recording it on the\nconnection only when the awaiting coroutine resumes. A cancel landing\nanywhere in that window left the handle unreachable from the cleanup\nthat follows, so the garbage collector reported `ResourceWarning:\nunclosed database`. There are two halves to the window, and both are now\ncovered:\n\n- Cancelled while the worker is still opening, the library has no handle\nrecorded yet, so the cleanup it queues closes nothing. The session\nmodule now records the handle from the worker thread the moment the\nconnector returns.\n- Cancelled after the handle is delivered but before the coroutine\nresumes, the library clears its own reference before that queued cleanup\ncan run — so it again closes nothing. The guard now also queues an\nexplicit close ahead of the library's cleanup, while the handle is still\nreachable.\n\nBoth closes run on the thread that opened the handle, and closing twice\nis a no-op, so neither disturbs a normal shutdown. `get_checkpointer`\nbuilds its connection through the same helper rather than\n`AsyncSqliteSaver.from_conn_string`, so it gets the same guard.\n\n**Where it started:** #5174. The prewarm that reads the session database\nhas existed since #1481, but it ran once at startup, so it had normally\nfinished before anything cancelled it. #5174 re-fires it after every\nturn, which reliably leaves a session-DB read in flight when a test app\nexits. Counting handles that `aiosqlite` opened and never closed across\nthe goal-command tests: zero on the parent commit, fourteen on #5174.\n\n### A `typing` deprecation from `google-genai`\n\n`google.genai.types` builds a union alias out of\n`typing._UnionGenericAlias`, which CPython 3.14 deprecates, and it fires\nat import before any of this package's code runs. This one is not a\nregression from any change here — `deepagents-code` has been tested on\nthe 3.14 leg since the package was created in #3027, and the warning\nappears wherever a test imports the Google integration. It is tracked\nupstream as\n[googleapis/python-genai#1640](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/1640)\nand still unfixed as of `google-genai` 2.13.0, so it is filtered\nnarrowly (message, category, and module) rather than worked around.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f42590ef-0fe4-0b9f-6880-1c48b28446d5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T19:14:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/994799b2f25950eb76e1085b5026d1f19eceb563/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a"}]},{"sha":"b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI0Mjg2NDRkMzFkZDZiNDE2ZmUwZTJhYmI1MzM4NjEwYTI1NTNkMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-04T19:05:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T19:05:06Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.52 (#5228)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.52](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.51...deepagents-code==0.1.52)\n(2026-08-04)\n\n### Features\n\n- Hooks v2 is now generally available, with support for loading hooks\nfrom installed plugins.\n([#5307](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5307),\n[#5198](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5198))\n- Auto approval classifier configuration now supports selecting the\nclassifier model and setting a review timeout.\n([#5205](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5205),\n[#5302](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5302))\n- HITL rejection reasons are now framed for the model, and the approval\nmenu makes reject-with-feedback easier to discover.\n([#5259](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5259),\n[#5260](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5260))\n- Added a tri-state `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING` environment variable.\n([#5301](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5301))\n- The `/model` footer Ctrl+N hint now follows the current display mode.\n([#5247](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5247))\n- The price catalog now refreshes hourly in the background.\n([#5264](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5264))\n- Updated recommendations to include DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731.\n([#5244](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5244))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed several Hooks v2 lifecycle issues: session-end teardown is now\nbounded, hooks refresh after cwd switches, malformed hook resumes are\nhandled, hook stops surface without agent errors, and unused\n`SessionEndCause` members were removed.\n([#5248](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5248),\n[#5249](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5249),\n[#5233](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5233),\n[#5276](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5276),\n[#5240](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5240))\n- `PreCompact` now fires before auto-compaction.\n([#5277](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5277))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c5314de14be2c0bc5c620e425c4211ee18908e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1c5314de14be2c0bc5c620e425c4211ee18908e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcjfiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABPoQAAdM4mhycjM9SN6aw+yxo3j/\nkm4jJ0NqyyXyDfPZ2RmWiG4Y0DmgjJrEJ8bnJ/Togwbnmo0JbSeYH/CrGfadVLSg\nZqwhnXFIBwCwF9AvBUU14DUkmZ5FZs5Yjex0Xh+pa4qEJzt5mEG13dM5Hb6lnvjO\n0ydMe9tAKlXSzaW6VhLGrgofL/A+GFlftyZVtTGCSAg56V5++8rUcRYHEwHEBXfY\niMt4RV8NYxkFfFXQnbu5BylCQ/O19L7HRbkwTdw9OP7Gcl7inSJG0pTIg4Z8coDS\nO3LlEqUBi8MgOC2sWGZ9SeqYpYVxzrBuEA3Zu09Ud7o4BsBHN6W7oT4AsWVqSY8j\n0fJ7ENU5zx7ioK+k+AVpCoDj6W1XE2U3f21rN8ENi/co2hMjwCVe95r/4ikguX/q\nnzChBIP3CKzeoqXrIPkKSHMc7AAq8+fG9INFrWV3kMctXsRxXUkAprjgIH2Yc3ng\nDdWMIPqr44WOlcRXGf+44imByMvk4tCro890oy1IEbDqK0yrrifqNGtMiMocdvHh\nr8Lv/KdNW00kP0rJQKQvphd6uPPUTbLoQcBI5ZHn+8Gad8VFcxI7rgoytNMMVY6h\n0wWNDx3WBLbXDfwEeX2x+qtblmQJnWNBrY5F70orhZR/o8itDKI/G1PVYlXf90IY\nRSPIy4Q/bFxBkBUwjQJ+\n=xWqm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1c5314de14be2c0bc5c620e425c4211ee18908e2\nparent fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785870306 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785870306 +0000\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.52 (#5228)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.52](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.51...deepagents-code==0.1.52)\n(2026-08-04)\n\n### Features\n\n- Hooks v2 is now generally available, with support for loading hooks\nfrom installed plugins.\n([#5307](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5307),\n[#5198](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5198))\n- Auto approval classifier configuration now supports selecting the\nclassifier model and setting a review timeout.\n([#5205](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5205),\n[#5302](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5302))\n- HITL rejection reasons are now framed for the model, and the approval\nmenu makes reject-with-feedback easier to discover.\n([#5259](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5259),\n[#5260](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5260))\n- Added a tri-state `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING` environment variable.\n([#5301](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5301))\n- The `/model` footer Ctrl+N hint now follows the current display mode.\n([#5247](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5247))\n- The price catalog now refreshes hourly in the background.\n([#5264](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5264))\n- Updated recommendations to include DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731.\n([#5244](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5244))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Fixed several Hooks v2 lifecycle issues: session-end teardown is now\nbounded, hooks refresh after cwd switches, malformed hook resumes are\nhandled, hook stops surface without agent errors, and unused\n`SessionEndCause` members were removed.\n([#5248](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5248),\n[#5249](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5249),\n[#5233](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5233),\n[#5276](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5276),\n[#5240](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5240))\n- `PreCompact` now fires before auto-compaction.\n([#5277](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5277))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T19:05:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b428644d31dd6b416fe0e2abb5338610a2553d1a/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b"}]},{"sha":"fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlOTVjYzVjM2Q4ZDU0Mzc5NmNkMmYzMTJhOGRhYWUzZmRkNTVhNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T18:22:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T18:22:53Z"},"message":"fix(infra): push pin bump branch without origin refspec (#5308)\n\nFixes the auto-opened SDK pin bump workflow failing at its final push\nwith `error: src refspec origin does not match any`, so the\n`chore(deps):` pin bump PR can be opened again after a `deepagents`\nrelease.\n\n---\n\nThe `Open pin bump PR` step pushed with the remote as a URL literal plus\n`--set-upstream origin \"$BRANCH\"`. With an unnamed URL remote, git\nparses `origin` as the source ref of the refspec; no local ref named\n`origin` exists, so the push failed after the branch had already been\ncommitted. `--set-upstream` is also meaningless against a URL remote.\nThe step now pushes `\"$BRANCH:$BRANCH\"` — local branch to the same-named\nremote branch, no `origin` refspec, no `--set-upstream`.\n\nThe earlier `git push <url> --delete \"$BRANCH\"` in the same step is\nunaffected and intentionally untouched: `--delete` takes only a\ndestination ref, so that form was already correct. The sibling\n`bump_uv_pin.yml` workflow pushes via the named `origin` remote and was\nalready correct.","tree":{"sha":"20af65fba96ded88c17031f6815e7c00afdaec66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/20af65fba96ded88c17031f6815e7c00afdaec66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqci39CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiqwQADvAt/rx9cSn4k3ZXk4uPQCB\nkVxQkrR2KZWHGuRuY7AwO25/ILrCmtza+F8d4q2kmd0pdavc7JEOBrZ2T8jxb+ix\nfw/gho5tws7BLxoqiiVn1QMRWtMVfulEDFbD8jsXopUo8SKnr9a+sEfOaTv3KCwa\noGbZ/4EPhVa2usgzM1Z2QXzx6vEhYObZzzCOUQ74E3sl3JEiOX8jQr4XcW0CjIKD\nsvHBUiYk3nXkBkF9ggmC+OhpZ/B7I/dE/53pFSAc5xdoampZQooG0WspbWlP1wSV\noIUUrVwlezmDUB3w6QahWG5tS3w5RrOnj795xvi4/Ek8HWD7o9dbtiQLu0OAcawE\nnNQpDUeY6BatBykWpvp2prXbi2Grkvb49f+yv9Uqq4tSeRXnThD2yYXlHtBzmSH7\nNbXlGRlpq7LOLQ4g90ogoCur3PS2b6zqrt6o9zBmmSWymHXHJFTTq0vauUAG49AA\nZPCE+ZC9E2z43ohz5iI0VUMexf53BBaYW88SRbsTmuWx+/aTcmlo3l7c4rvRby91\nDjHtEy2PnTdb2b9SPJWi6RlOZ2RwTUzva6ODkUqH16VmywG5bEV/cwyGUiDsCStK\nTtrYvKY/1BEOPY/CPW8QuQimcBV+6NE4prDDO2Nvv1FLN5qXStVTF6tl4vef/X0M\nKOgZ+7gAJIwrgPkq+7DU\n=JnHW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20af65fba96ded88c17031f6815e7c00afdaec66\nparent 28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785867773 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785867773 -0400\n\nfix(infra): push pin bump branch without origin refspec (#5308)\n\nFixes the auto-opened SDK pin bump workflow failing at its final push\nwith `error: src refspec origin does not match any`, so the\n`chore(deps):` pin bump PR can be opened again after a `deepagents`\nrelease.\n\n---\n\nThe `Open pin bump PR` step pushed with the remote as a URL literal plus\n`--set-upstream origin \"$BRANCH\"`. With an unnamed URL remote, git\nparses `origin` as the source ref of the refspec; no local ref named\n`origin` exists, so the push failed after the branch had already been\ncommitted. `--set-upstream` is also meaningless against a URL remote.\nThe step now pushes `\"$BRANCH:$BRANCH\"` — local branch to the same-named\nremote branch, no `origin` refspec, no `--set-upstream`.\n\nThe earlier `git push <url> --delete \"$BRANCH\"` in the same step is\nunaffected and intentionally untouched: `--delete` takes only a\ndestination ref, so that form was already correct. The sibling\n`bump_uv_pin.yml` workflow pushes via the named `origin` remote and was\nalready correct.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T18:22:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fe95cc5c3d8d543796cd2f312a8daae3fdd55a4b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4"}]},{"sha":"28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI4YTdkNWJkZDNmNzgwNDRiNGYzNjEyZjcxZTEzY2UzOGVmNDdiZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-04T17:46:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T17:46:38Z"},"message":"fix(code): bound Hooks v2 session-end teardown (#5248)\n\nHooks v2 `SessionEnd` handlers now have a two-second teardown budget in\nheadless and interactive sessions, preventing slow handlers from\ndelaying process exit.\n\n---\n\nThe generic hook timeout remains unchanged. Session boundaries use a\ndedicated bounded wait, log overruns, and preserve at-most-once\ndelivery.\n\n<details><summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Focused headless and TUI timeout tests, plus the complete\ngraceful-exit test class\n- Ruff formatting/lint and `ty` checks for all modified files\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8af65704-7778-df84-0c27-ad718a80ea7f)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8af65704-7778-df84-0c27-ad718a80ea7f/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"9fdf493ae612f3b4497d806541e7a224f220745a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9fdf493ae612f3b4497d806541e7a224f220745a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqciV+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9LkQAKfW2Zm70klERTx+ADVnUDsV\najc3pxDHbTD7NwDkq7tnEdWuxbZAuoXXWbipnAFTlbK2mIlPCd1FWrj0gYvW4H0O\nwVq/FwlXigDdfKYpJlCY9B9/Z3sc/6K2v4DrBQqcJnh+qA1SiboyigmuKRqKK3Nx\nL5BtcHOcP5fURNvWu4IhXlyFohnr6NU7jGnq2f/cdjbNNB/FRN6NPyJlejzYarXP\noSYQQoDxJi1H61aQp49Wc043wYt/aGZ5uHxqB2Ypc4EYngAh+n2rfNBZSEp2Cz8k\nn7GhP6fX7VmiNaCe/tlCS69g6I8Ui/soFbO3ZosmOqwEw+oItMOf92TIEfBbqiXq\n7Y+6K2We7ta1raQ93YvAvZ2OUdUimV/OmTWohlJJu6+RQ0MmhzLkwvkHCQGE4y6a\nb+XfqTdjRa9KhN/YDNurTRXybvFC1gwCsPSBjD18qR30HwvkoXh2FHyHgYH3PDju\nLlakMCzgZO+kGV0IbD2mZD0irCeESeVcR/vNMO4O1DdM+qyjAPwgn+Zmn+jE7tFL\nQ/FuyIItQ0xB7rUQYaHZcgFLXXqWZrChojocBs47S9oqAk2N2u+B1w2auzWpP266\nQ+8ixtj3xmcJUbMdFoAnHlBao1fmv8DSw5K7RfjnfR3KVD0YEz90+LcsmEsXCNs9\n3h+YJoSj1U7u1ECa917Y\n=cOSr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9fdf493ae612f3b4497d806541e7a224f220745a\nparent 4edebdedd61d6793f0f7b666f5ee26b414576805\nauthor Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com> 1785865598 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785865598 -0700\n\nfix(code): bound Hooks v2 session-end teardown (#5248)\n\nHooks v2 `SessionEnd` handlers now have a two-second teardown budget in\nheadless and interactive sessions, preventing slow handlers from\ndelaying process exit.\n\n---\n\nThe generic hook timeout remains unchanged. Session boundaries use a\ndedicated bounded wait, log overruns, and preserve at-most-once\ndelivery.\n\n<details><summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Focused headless and TUI timeout tests, plus the complete\ngraceful-exit test class\n- Ruff formatting/lint and `ty` checks for all modified files\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8af65704-7778-df84-0c27-ad718a80ea7f)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/8af65704-7778-df84-0c27-ad718a80ea7f/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T17:46:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/28a7d5bdd3f78044b4f3612f71e13ce38ef47bf4/comments","author":{"login":"aolsenjazz","id":13665641,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjY1NjQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13665641?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz","html_url":"https://github.com/aolsenjazz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenja