==0.7.4)\n(2026-08-04)\n\n### Features\n\n- Exposed the `execute` exit code in SDK artifacts.\n([#5300](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5300))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T16:04:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/553a030a5b959ac8bb17d52447f915397f910f03","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/553a030a5b959ac8bb17d52447f915397f910f03","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/553a030a5b959ac8bb17d52447f915397f910f03/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee"}]},{"sha":"124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDEyNDcwNGFjOWI1MTI4MTk0NTJjZDkwNjM3Yzc2MTk2NWI0Y2ZkZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T15:57:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T15:57:55Z"},"message":"feat(infra): branch-name pre-push hook and advisory CI check (#5297)\n\nInternal branches are expected to follow\n`<github-username>/<scope>/<short-description>` per AGENTS.md, but\nnothing enforces it today. This adds two layers of enforcement: a\npre-commit-managed pre-push hook that blocks pushing non-conformant\nbranch names locally, and an advisory CI check that posts a sticky PR\ncomment when a PR head branch does not follow the convention.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nBranch names in this repo are a mix of conformant (`mdrxy/code/...`) and\nad-hoc (`abalone-ricotta`, `fix/vscode-root-interpreter-path`) names.\nThe convention is documented but unenforced, so drift is the default.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`.githooks/pre-push`** (new, committed) — the branch-name check\ninvoked by pre-commit at the `pre-push` stage. It blocks branches that\ndo not match `<github-username>/<scope>/<short-description>`. The\nusername resolves from `git config github.user`, falling back to `gh api\nuser` and then the local part of `user.email`. The scope segment is\nvalidated against the `pr_lint.yml` scope list (plus `docs`).\n`pre-commit install --install-hooks` installs it alongside the existing\npre-commit and commit-message hooks; bypassable with `--no-verify` or\n`SKIP=branch-name`.\n- **`.github/workflows/branch_name_check.yml`** (new) — runs on\nsame-repo PRs (forks are exempt). Posts or updates a sticky warning\ncomment on non-conformant head branches and deletes it once renamed.\nAlways exits green — it is a reminder, not a gate.\n- **`libs/DEVELOPMENT.md`** — setup docs for the hook.\n\nProtected branches (`main`, `vX.Y`) and automation branches\n(`release-please--*`, `dependabot/*`, `copilot/*`) are exempt in both\nlayers.\n\n## Points for review\n\n- The scope list is duplicated across `pr_lint.yml`, the hook, and the\nworkflow (each notes it must stay in sync). A shared source would be\nnicer but adds indirection for three small consumers.\n- The hook enforces the *resolved local user* login as the prefix, so\npushing a branch prefixed with someone else's username from your machine\nis blocked locally. CI does not compare the username segment to the PR\nauthor, since automation and maintainers legitimately push branches on\nothers' behalf.","tree":{"sha":"399b61868ee7c3dc4912695ac66b9d06d64b0bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/399b61868ee7c3dc4912695ac66b9d06d64b0bc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcgwDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbtkQAFfVbGkz1Z57umDVFf3wdLLY\nWD2odm3INfkfTwR4cUaEqZ1aE+XvbhXI/z1s0JNyAwwSXqkEYnwsHHdJb7vsto0r\n2LXNFggwggMkXloTf0i4xbBYVhMTA7AePDeNHQppENY18BSRSK08ISVi1lRwKAeS\nKx1O6qRCM4+EbKt+uZtrjsS29+I1ru+29ZtYG5gNMvLX3akvSjDTGiAVMl9DhE0M\nLzPqJc84b6VKa5fQP3Yz4Ny6AirdCv9ZuQG+fkb+vCpUb+HPBYRqL4ejsLX+q2E4\nsBbTZ51xXLATL5DVUANieQQ1kxUCJ83A3hPINNkvrtIWLjIIJIEW0MV21W3ylFp3\nhdYdwPuVfnUCG7F7QKYlmCAnMXEPVBM2gM3u5I4wM4Yyu0BQ3s+2OmkBQedP23hn\njkFlQZXYAB2yv7OVD4N/E0K94a/hiTm9gco4xk4cY5JPBkvwvT49KZXADouUoTWv\nHJ9xWovQGHOtmBIawhdMbSSBp44Xn/e0ZzOKStZLMZZ6VQJugJW4ervyRRk2epMM\n5/D7Wy2ZJsxN7dReqesEEgOurYoNNiM1hxr9uM0A1woKOjsPsHxvXjt5ZUQKo/RY\n1opSVIpAo30zagjSDyZNEUKfZqd8JzFgRxCmEru7R4WV0Fb6r6dOabiCYlGM83T7\n7w1kuO5PXENNl1kzTdVQ\n=Oq5q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 399b61868ee7c3dc4912695ac66b9d06d64b0bc9\nparent de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785859075 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785859075 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): branch-name pre-push hook and advisory CI check (#5297)\n\nInternal branches are expected to follow\n`<github-username>/<scope>/<short-description>` per AGENTS.md, but\nnothing enforces it today. This adds two layers of enforcement: a\npre-commit-managed pre-push hook that blocks pushing non-conformant\nbranch names locally, and an advisory CI check that posts a sticky PR\ncomment when a PR head branch does not follow the convention.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nBranch names in this repo are a mix of conformant (`mdrxy/code/...`) and\nad-hoc (`abalone-ricotta`, `fix/vscode-root-interpreter-path`) names.\nThe convention is documented but unenforced, so drift is the default.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`.githooks/pre-push`** (new, committed) — the branch-name check\ninvoked by pre-commit at the `pre-push` stage. It blocks branches that\ndo not match `<github-username>/<scope>/<short-description>`. The\nusername resolves from `git config github.user`, falling back to `gh api\nuser` and then the local part of `user.email`. The scope segment is\nvalidated against the `pr_lint.yml` scope list (plus `docs`).\n`pre-commit install --install-hooks` installs it alongside the existing\npre-commit and commit-message hooks; bypassable with `--no-verify` or\n`SKIP=branch-name`.\n- **`.github/workflows/branch_name_check.yml`** (new) — runs on\nsame-repo PRs (forks are exempt). Posts or updates a sticky warning\ncomment on non-conformant head branches and deletes it once renamed.\nAlways exits green — it is a reminder, not a gate.\n- **`libs/DEVELOPMENT.md`** — setup docs for the hook.\n\nProtected branches (`main`, `vX.Y`) and automation branches\n(`release-please--*`, `dependabot/*`, `copilot/*`) are exempt in both\nlayers.\n\n## Points for review\n\n- The scope list is duplicated across `pr_lint.yml`, the hook, and the\nworkflow (each notes it must stay in sync). A shared source would be\nnicer but adds indirection for three small consumers.\n- The hook enforces the *resolved local user* login as the prefix, so\npushing a branch prefixed with someone else's username from your machine\nis blocked locally. CI does not compare the username segment to the PR\nauthor, since automation and maintainers legitimately push branches on\nothers' behalf.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T15:57:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/124704ac9b512819452cd90637c761965b4cfdee/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e"}]},{"sha":"de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRlOGJmY2E4MjU1ZDY3M2MxZTc4NjBlOGMxNThlZDExOTIzODE5N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-04T15:57:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T15:57:09Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): expose `execute` exit code in artifact (#5300)\n\n`execute` tool results now expose the process exit code in\n`ToolMessage.artifact`.\n\n---\n\nThis lets consumers distinguish shell failures without parsing\nmodel-facing content while preserving the existing `ToolMessage.status`\nbehavior. Both synchronous and asynchronous execution, including\ncapture/offload, attach the same JSON-serializable metadata.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cd4daa3c-c4cd-1a1b-fe6b-a6fbe929a285)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e9d236525ee333b7e4b15c43c35a2a3d04caa6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1e9d236525ee333b7e4b15c43c35a2a3d04caa6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcgvVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgbQQAAlS2Gpix6T5o0Do7wUlz0JM\neW7tiv+x1VtcCGRbZ7cZEEI/6rSZ/ZF+oyRTNCi+m6vCtbsqesPzEP4QdJ+Iamg1\n+vAulIYt7ZGnGxyHVAoZCaUD8cjJUyqCzOI68goCPLHERUav/vQHpQ13vZ/VWm9g\n5cqyFdE5MgRlkdOVux5u5D2OcLtDaWe6oFWcw7Qql1+JnZoMw5CtWOgcKmpPqRo3\ngLrS6O7WyBgcMbBb7uNwMLapKNofIPI0XFxYatIRoWRzclB776mGRjvq23YEH4TN\neiGuOBYsmumSBuKVVXMS2cGEtetWqxWLPG3ZLzZXWfc3NTi7J1JtWZ2XruKdJkHn\nluJd9rCRXwDmy1VeLwAMu0pbRogDHOtyqCwGapNYXN/r8cyWjj06wfDcH2Z6q0HU\nDHbQ9nyn6kOFPmrWKEATOZtQEe2iM/PyUtLKrfkokRVOWL20VPfQyph2eUv3ipKY\nCf9R8levq27Oxh1vv6MLHiC5AyLGEgUgqUj/eV/PaWMpHi6NXVmpXSyk/waiB/mO\nOUikxXI16uLTIbgKUHMUZwAK8tOwmAmGTkfbLfwSdJsU0wCPL9yyeKVyi/J1JVK8\nVNRQn0s7aCoJErKpB+sPfnIzQJz6gwUlvEcnYFd8hlQeQDFCQSJ8jJEsWZUSPcfX\nV/WcSmUIO4BizyrgCy2O\n=8CBd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1e9d236525ee333b7e4b15c43c35a2a3d04caa6b\nparent 43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8\nauthor Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com> 1785859029 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785859029 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): expose `execute` exit code in artifact (#5300)\n\n`execute` tool results now expose the process exit code in\n`ToolMessage.artifact`.\n\n---\n\nThis lets consumers distinguish shell failures without parsing\nmodel-facing content while preserving the existing `ToolMessage.status`\nbehavior. Both synchronous and asynchronous execution, including\ncapture/offload, attach the same JSON-serializable metadata.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/cd4daa3c-c4cd-1a1b-fe6b-a6fbe929a285)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T15:57:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de8bfca8255d673c1e7860e8c158ed119238197e/comments","author":{"login":"aolsenjazz","id":13665641,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjY1NjQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13665641?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz","html_url":"https://github.com/aolsenjazz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8"}]},{"sha":"43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzMjkzZTk1Y2IwNzJjOGI5MmE3MzRlY2E4YzAyOTJlNDVkMjc5ZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T15:14:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T15:14:17Z"},"message":"feat(code): tri-state `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING` env var (#5301)\n\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_ONBOARDING` is now `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING`,\nand it works in both directions: set it to a falsy value to skip the\nfirst-run onboarding flow entirely (useful for fresh containers, CI, and\nprovisioned machines), a truthy value to force it open on every\ninteractive startup, or leave it unset for the existing first-run\nbehavior.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the only knob was a debug-only override that could force\nonboarding *on*. There was no supported way to turn it off, so anyone\nprovisioning a fresh instance had to pre-seed the internal completion\nmarker file — an implementation detail that is not part of the\ndocumented surface.\n\n`should_run_onboarding` now reads the variable through the existing\n`classify_env_bool` helper so it resolves three ways: truthy forces the\nflow, falsy suppresses it, and unset (or an unrecognized token, which is\nlogged) defers to the completion marker as before. Suppressing the flow\ndoes not write the marker, so removing the variable restores first-run\nbehavior rather than silently consuming it.\n\nThe config manifest entry moves from `debug.onboarding` to\n`startup.onboarding` and drops its static default, so `config` reports\nit as unset rather than implying a hardcoded `false`. It stays env-only,\nmatching what the runtime actually reads.\n\nThe old variable name is removed rather than aliased: it was documented\nas a debug-only knob, and keeping a second spelling would leave two\nnames with different semantics.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/44ba60bf-19f1-3a82-77ba-6def983ff352)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ff0c410613a588414fc6fd12cc92c378c493f28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4ff0c410613a588414fc6fd12cc92c378c493f28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcgHJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi3cQAKRXLJdBp4XRjlWVL+XuH1GE\nIaGA6yAQsKQqIthbiIIV3fRDRZ3zvBr+6fcGO7xkn7nVzTsxQg1gk7+I2hlfY4ju\n6SysYwkwh2jI3eUShu9WrYmyPRXLy4hF4O9uO/edXOZbQilNUpLyk6oqqhkLR8ZE\nT7wXSjcWz7HEQuoz+tAJckxZDbBBKUrLz0wiPgtd8z/WJhdpWtBp1dtuLYCr8rUl\nI3pIRBzv8TXoRNFXP6DgE0iADXxB+jEY2HQNLyXoHk6XHIk9baCiqKI9rB35pUr1\nvWCOx6Bw89VO2Ayhk7m/3w+LYq6j3RnYYEfy8gBdsndA6xz1TiI8hgU0auN5SLwL\nABpJe175Ghde45EHS2xoerPln6mIY1o/eLz2v+Tq4XiBOLACl0fCQJHrDG0qcDWs\nJihk4K55v8F595Yf1+zSizHk7+5Trxh3HYWqR2KaFP3kZagDvxRZ90r49xeOqh4w\nfiTiqTsXNYk8cp1pDJD6OmBTcbESeZjy38SEqX9zd9he7XWxW0Sw3IP26xki1P4/\nL1R2+EqZdHKe0EmvoMPJ/rXRE2GMYfivMBGdUCbsom08cLptxPY7t/gxL+Lv5NOU\nb7jWlok28jxECwla8eDDsls46367jtjj0qC9xTShy5Mfr2hXachGhRNEFjxFTmyK\nlS6unyCejozP84eSYmFW\n=OJSP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ff0c410613a588414fc6fd12cc92c378c493f28\nparent 3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785856457 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785856457 -0400\n\nfeat(code): tri-state `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING` env var (#5301)\n\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG_ONBOARDING` is now `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ONBOARDING`,\nand it works in both directions: set it to a falsy value to skip the\nfirst-run onboarding flow entirely (useful for fresh containers, CI, and\nprovisioned machines), a truthy value to force it open on every\ninteractive startup, or leave it unset for the existing first-run\nbehavior.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the only knob was a debug-only override that could force\nonboarding *on*. There was no supported way to turn it off, so anyone\nprovisioning a fresh instance had to pre-seed the internal completion\nmarker file — an implementation detail that is not part of the\ndocumented surface.\n\n`should_run_onboarding` now reads the variable through the existing\n`classify_env_bool` helper so it resolves three ways: truthy forces the\nflow, falsy suppresses it, and unset (or an unrecognized token, which is\nlogged) defers to the completion marker as before. Suppressing the flow\ndoes not write the marker, so removing the variable restores first-run\nbehavior rather than silently consuming it.\n\nThe config manifest entry moves from `debug.onboarding` to\n`startup.onboarding` and drops its static default, so `config` reports\nit as unset rather than implying a hardcoded `false`. It stays env-only,\nmatching what the runtime actually reads.\n\nThe old variable name is removed rather than aliased: it was documented\nas a debug-only knob, and keeping a second spelling would leave two\nnames with different semantics.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/44ba60bf-19f1-3a82-77ba-6def983ff352)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T15:14:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/43293e95cb072c8b92a734eca8c0292e45d279e8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae"}]},{"sha":"3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMwMTJiYWM2NjA4YjhhYmQwYWNhNGMwMGMxZjE2Y2QyNjk4Njc2YWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T14:53:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T14:53:35Z"},"message":"style(code): explain why to use `/offload` in the startup tip (#5303)\n\nThe startup tip for `/offload` now explains what the command does and\nwhy it helps — it summarizes older messages to free up the context\nwindow — instead of only saying to run it once the conversation gets\nlong.\n\n---\n\nStartup tips exist for feature discovery, so a tip that names a command\nwithout saying what it gains the user does not do its job. The new\nwording keeps the short, action-oriented format of the other tips while\nstating the benefit.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/985d7cc1-7fab-ad75-7dff-86588a73b73a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"27edddbc9e5e3842a040bf2111840a1c1a35996b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/27edddbc9e5e3842a040bf2111840a1c1a35996b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcfzvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzjEQAJDn8sfjocLalJT7m2fUhbzq\nyKRfz/098N0D8LUeQPQ5ZxY9AEiDHeQSb+hKdjWEc2Sfh0cgRH4wQFLRVDzuCHbM\nbUgf2MmDW0qZf4zVB2VT448rueDxq88wq28swujCmmf167kCde5w7ILuuzYzYMja\nwF/fo6s2UKorACPWrzdPWufa/ZPjcJMmCvSryjZivIXBuIElSc+IASiqvQn1ORfO\nfjmC635HnaShurvZF3yaexiToWNo2YD74Rrid03gK9aBCCilx+xJuxhqbzvuEs63\nIoS29Mb31SpnlAGtTMavjIxdQxmrh4YHlDJKQrdD72s+b3/mqDmzfdCvGqGgtIPG\nWV4hEkvXZ3LcUhTeCapQhMWFrO7qF1SPfHkRwbJOzAXYodOyIs3xsme+HvqxuP6s\nTVZLEJ7DnHkTxZqZGEqQ6BSx+N6hYkgeKJAjl1op4iY/4vgbbRLNhKgW2NcdA7YS\nv+zZ+vNT/KpE9/KtyehyMxWw/agQLlmAxEtgJY1YXVVxME4HSIcNvGvkDrt5i6iZ\nNGU3yM4YQFoKuHvnaEhueoCrljlGrHzgjuaPUhoHYEfVCTTz9yOSDotdg4R+6zvm\nomXx0O1xUxFXsAgD+mEEoMkUOvvD9S3jql5Dv55gefErP6fhBdDgFsYKA2wVjIFn\nNyBkBWZ0r1BYQ1TV8IvK\n=TgQR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 27edddbc9e5e3842a040bf2111840a1c1a35996b\nparent 46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785855215 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785855215 -0400\n\nstyle(code): explain why to use `/offload` in the startup tip (#5303)\n\nThe startup tip for `/offload` now explains what the command does and\nwhy it helps — it summarizes older messages to free up the context\nwindow — instead of only saying to run it once the conversation gets\nlong.\n\n---\n\nStartup tips exist for feature discovery, so a tip that names a command\nwithout saying what it gains the user does not do its job. The new\nwording keeps the short, action-oriented format of the other tips while\nstating the benefit.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/985d7cc1-7fab-ad75-7dff-86588a73b73a)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-04T14:53:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3012bac6608b8abd0aca4c00c1f16cd2698676ae/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca"}]},{"sha":"46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2ZTAwNjc1N2JiNDY1NmJmOTJmNjk1NGY2ZjNmNDdiNTBkNGY2Y2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T14:30:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T14:30:34Z"},"message":"feat(infra): accept maintainer instructions on `@release-bot draft` (#5299)\n\nMaintainers can now steer a release-notes draft in one shot:\n`@release-bot draft <instructions>` feeds the text after the command\ninto the drafting model as guidance, so a draft can be re-generated with\ndirection (e.g. `@release-bot draft emphasize the breaking SDK change\nand lead with it`) instead of drafting blind and hand-editing after.\n\n---\n\nThe release-notes bot's drafting step previously took only the generated\nchangelog — the only way to shape the result was to edit the posted\ndraft by hand. This adds a lightweight way to steer the model at draft\ntime.\n\n- `draft` accepts optional instructions on the same line; `apply` is\nunchanged and ignores trailing text, since it republishes the stored\ndraft verbatim.\n- Instructions are capped at 500 characters and truncated at any `@`, so\ntrailing text can't smuggle a second `@release-bot` mention into the\nprompt.\n- The instruction is passed to the model in the user message as guidance\nexplicitly subordinate to the fixed editing rules, never into the system\nprompt — the \"do not invent behavior / no version heading\" constraints\nstay authoritative.\n- The posted draft comment echoes `Drafted with maintainer instructions:\n…` (outside the metadata block and the editable content markers, so both\nparsers are unaffected), keeping the prompt that produced a draft\nauditable on the PR.\n- `prepareDraft` re-sanitizes instructions independently of the comment\nparser, so the guarantee holds at the process boundary into the model\nrequest regardless of caller.\n\nThe drafting model still runs with no filesystem, shell, or network\ntools, and its output is re-validated by `validateDraftOutput` before\npublishing — this change only widens what a maintainer can ask for, not\nwhat the model can do.","tree":{"sha":"444c9d9bdb9bb3274bf2ccf27f31dda9749197f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/444c9d9bdb9bb3274bf2ccf27f31dda9749197f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcfeKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAivIQAKN6Z5hoicNsPJT3H1CtXHwS\n5bPv8XTt1Pz1lM52gGQeUMJmRnstAf4pqCLAt3MkScpo7RMZbPC1kxbF9XDAFwjl\nr/CkJBu5VysfeWdAvq9IA3irkpRIgbMPwpi2/gGLfEwwf/1RSiFW+djcKolRRmaq\nWKfJDnMSWkwzT2xy5fAEEQp64+XHW347hJVP8lpzD8oWU6qkyO3TrTAi1+MB96m+\noekx1Jf5Yfd3oZJVyt9w/FTbzAq7K0eWO0dVGodjpK6qO6r15VNbdNE537wY8qZ/\nrpUMweDqpawJ6GO9Rj8V6ljTuYaSx0IOpWt1+flrFzbl+twPwiaYpUqJjz9nC/HY\nJqeB1LHdrcnnP5iv9S8KdYvjBhrDT8kpW8tlOTFhI/uBfTRe3O1uKAtOWYq258om\nvXYLrrj8PH7UOTYR2564LH0lh1+gZ7jTyAPosrkyKTe+lTgQDMUIR/ExKnhmbZ3r\nP0XJl1D3a+duhwfOw9qezVkjbbvtyjZPmn/yffZ8W0T4yDxU7dL0uJecN5wAmLPU\nFYMUSsIlDGuVhAb530zV+kNblPrMmDXAt2qNAA75Ptpa6xzijJptwrjjZ6PUAY8l\nuZg0FmKCHjDnrlUBTJ0cStKAIemwSlPdbAzTaTrjTk7nVlWhkSJg+rFakTU72tVd\nO8SrfkTVu2kqeCzOoWFT\n=1TZ3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 444c9d9bdb9bb3274bf2ccf27f31dda9749197f7\nparent 68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785853834 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785853834 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): accept maintainer instructions on `@release-bot draft` (#5299)\n\nMaintainers can now steer a release-notes draft in one shot:\n`@release-bot draft <instructions>` feeds the text after the command\ninto the drafting model as guidance, so a draft can be re-generated with\ndirection (e.g. `@release-bot draft emphasize the breaking SDK change\nand lead with it`) instead of drafting blind and hand-editing after.\n\n---\n\nThe release-notes bot's drafting step previously took only the generated\nchangelog — the only way to shape the result was to edit the posted\ndraft by hand. This adds a lightweight way to steer the model at draft\ntime.\n\n- `draft` accepts optional instructions on the same line; `apply` is\nunchanged and ignores trailing text, since it republishes the stored\ndraft verbatim.\n- Instructions are capped at 500 characters and truncated at any `@`, so\ntrailing text can't smuggle a second `@release-bot` mention into the\nprompt.\n- The instruction is passed to the model in the user message as guidance\nexplicitly subordinate to the fixed editing rules, never into the system\nprompt — the \"do not invent behavior / no version heading\" constraints\nstay authoritative.\n- The posted draft comment echoes `Drafted with maintainer instructions:\n…` (outside the metadata block and the editable content markers, so both\nparsers are unaffected), keeping the prompt that produced a draft\nauditable on the PR.\n- `prepareDraft` re-sanitizes instructions independently of the comment\nparser, so the guarantee holds at the process boundary into the model\nrequest regardless of caller.\n\nThe drafting model still runs with no filesystem, shell, or network\ntools, and its output is re-validated by `validateDraftOutput` before\npublishing — this change only widens what a maintainer can ask for, not\nwhat the model can do.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T14:30:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46e006757bb4656bf92f6954f6f3f47b50d4f6ca/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a"}]},{"sha":"68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY4YmE0NWE0ZWIxNTQ5N2Y3NDNiMzNiZWY2ODkyNmU0ZmQ4NmNlNmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-04T14:22:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T14:22:33Z"},"message":"ci(infra): auto-open Code SDK pin bump PR after deepagents release (#5298)\n\nAfter every `deepagents` release, someone has to hand-bump the exact\n`deepagents==X.Y.Z` pin in `libs/code/pyproject.toml` before the next\n`deepagents-code` release (the release workflow hard-gates on it). This\nautomates that: once the SDK publish to PyPI succeeds, `release.yml`\ndispatches a new `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` workflow that opens a\n`chore(deps):` PR bumping the pin and regenerating `libs/code/uv.lock`.\n\n---\n\nHow it works:\n\n- **`bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`** (new, `workflow_dispatch` only): compares\nthe workspace SDK version to the Code pin via PEP 440 and exits cleanly\nwhen the pin is current or ahead (intentional prerelease pins are never\nclobbered). Rewrites the one quoted `deepagents==X.Y.Z` dependency line\nand regenerates `libs/code/uv.lock` in the same commit. Dedupes against\nan already-open PR on the same branch and cleans up orphan branches.\nStays manually dispatchable for recovery.\n- **`release.yml`** (new `bump-code-sdk-pin` job): runs only when\n`publish` succeeded for `deepagents`, mints an App token scoped to\n`actions: write`, and runs `gh workflow run bump_code_sdk_pin.yml --ref\nmain`.\n\nTwo deliberate choices:\n\n- The PR opens as `chore(deps):` via the Org Membership App installation\ntoken. The `chore` type keeps release-please from fanning out a spurious\n`release(deepagents-code)` PR for a change inside the managed\n`libs/code` package, and the App token (vs. `GITHUB_TOKEN`) ensures the\nPR's required checks actually run.\n- Dispatching post-publish (rather than on the version-commit push to\n`main`) means the new SDK is already on PyPI when the auto-PR's CI\nresolves `deepagents==X.Y.Z` from the real index — no race between the\nPR's checks and the publish.","tree":{"sha":"b7ea95f7fb92dfb4f7d6fcb41993215335486a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b7ea95f7fb92dfb4f7d6fcb41993215335486a5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcfWpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwzEQAD/5EnMJEVifI84offu1twLc\nNo80Vclqbuu4szJe/nscT4vR4bJGaKK0xJlIc1SCihSyToeoXHUojkyjFPkNl78B\nAuyLyEdbZmSiF0p4FZbP/kB0nXTHdYx2ezzJYu7U2a2jPn9+TvAFBbDvebOKkktR\nn9Gk9cHc0GZnEtAJb9HIZ3e9K0jFZmGS9tmhhlMDkn17Yh61rT/lwhpbd5JIO8MD\n1qgubJvNFlUMN9rt7ohqM3YmY+4Z/pdVPVXuCtrfUYo1eEF8mYakxN/3qGgnOLJs\nHZ6dFCZDlJC6Gx9Ooh1gvLbfp8u+j8a3QnUMGMPIM113FnmCP/7FsyONUWHJjXl7\n/WtWmp6A6DZ8HjL0kWB2BbWQdwAlirQoN+TV3cvdgUQLivkmFeJbvyNecU66TdaF\naRyj3F2jnJmpWGMJ0klort5qp6Ko/5IDqlAbwTpvSFONX3IpU04qXhV2fZf3BoTM\noUexmVRfRXXjdPyu77D/d35S2d9wjqjjRi3gSvVxYh3QomUEGB7BrJz7+2p3rBcy\nYpTFdocozAsusVTVLeWCwoFSLwAvnlinuOw2w+/4noCZXXzsS7xUbOtzsjLBL4eH\n8xl98bTFs5X291t2oTH2F3vF/u08Sbs+Mb1yOn/S5ABruV3xHOslnEw6TtzF/JRx\ntN6Ce441d1Lq0oGVkF8D\n=x7KL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b7ea95f7fb92dfb4f7d6fcb41993215335486a5d\nparent 5f776b5882709b62332183b8cae6a1c71866b43a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785853353 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785853353 -0400\n\nci(infra): auto-open Code SDK pin bump PR after deepagents release (#5298)\n\nAfter every `deepagents` release, someone has to hand-bump the exact\n`deepagents==X.Y.Z` pin in `libs/code/pyproject.toml` before the next\n`deepagents-code` release (the release workflow hard-gates on it). This\nautomates that: once the SDK publish to PyPI succeeds, `release.yml`\ndispatches a new `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` workflow that opens a\n`chore(deps):` PR bumping the pin and regenerating `libs/code/uv.lock`.\n\n---\n\nHow it works:\n\n- **`bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`** (new, `workflow_dispatch` only): compares\nthe workspace SDK version to the Code pin via PEP 440 and exits cleanly\nwhen the pin is current or ahead (intentional prerelease pins are never\nclobbered). Rewrites the one quoted `deepagents==X.Y.Z` dependency line\nand regenerates `libs/code/uv.lock` in the same commit. Dedupes against\nan already-open PR on the same branch and cleans up orphan branches.\nStays manually dispatchable for recovery.\n- **`release.yml`** (new `bump-code-sdk-pin` job): runs only when\n`publish` succeeded for `deepagents`, mints an App token scoped to\n`actions: write`, and runs `gh workflow run bump_code_sdk_pin.yml --ref\nmain`.\n\nTwo deliberate choices:\n\n- The PR opens as `chore(deps):` via the Org Membership App installation\ntoken. The `chore` type keeps release-please from fanning out a spurious\n`release(deepagents-code)` PR for a change inside the managed\n`libs/code` package, and the App token (vs. `GITHUB_TOKEN`) ensures the\nPR's required checks actually run.\n- Dispatching post-publish (rather than on the version-commit push to\n`main`) means the new SDK is already on PyPI when the auto-PR's CI\nresolves `deepagents==X.Y.Z` from the real index — no race between the\nPR's checks and the publish.","verified_at":"2026-08-04T14:22:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68ba45a4eb15497f743b33bef68926e4fd86ce6a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5f776b5882709b62332183b8cae6a1c71866b43a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5f776b5882709b62332183b8cae6a1c71866b43a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5f776b5882709b62332183b8cae6a1c71866b43a"}]},{"sha":"5f776b5882709b62332183b8cae6a1c71866b43a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVmNzc2YjU4ODI3MDliNjIzMzIxODNiOGNhZTZhMWM3MTg2NmI0M2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-04T08:59:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-04T08:59:29Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump aiohttp from 3.14.2 to 3.14.3 in /libs/partners/daytona (#5274)\n\nBumps [aiohttp](https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp) from 3.14.2 to\n3.14.3.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">aiohttp's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.14.3 (2026-07-22)</h1>\n<h2>Bug fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fixed the client dropping only the first <code>Authorization</code>,\n<code>Cookie</code> and\n<code>Proxy-Authorization</code> header when a redirect crossed an\norigin -- by :user:<code>arshsmith1</code>.</p>\n<p><em>Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:</em>\n:issue:<code>13180</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixed error message construction in the C HTTP parser -- by\n:user:<code>bdraco</code>.</p>\n<p><em>Related issues and pull requests on GitHub:</em>\n:issue:<code>13222</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/5e392ce0456f5235a4ee6ad46f0e806df2f15873\"><code>5e392ce</code></a>\nRelease v3.14.3 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/13225\">#13225</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/49f65d54150397892f7bcc4aae887767d51c322d\"><code>49f65d5</code></a>\n[PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/13222\">#13222</a>/f4866933\nbackport][3.14] Build C parser error message from bounded...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/240099e5216a01b32919dcd8dd5c6c0b1bf83671\"><code>240099e</code></a>\n[PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/13180\">#13180</a>/ee53d655\nbackport][3.14] drop every copy of credential headers on ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/d93f30a302f8b930074fe14a2be7b2088ba28111\"><code>d93f30a</code></a>\nBump version (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/13202\">#13202</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/compare/v3.14.2...v3.14.3\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authore